{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open","sort":"updated","order":"desc","topn":50},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\", \"issue_number\": 2269, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\\n\\nPart of #1782.\\nPrimary reference: #25.\\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\\n\\nExpected deliverables:\\n- baseline docs\\n- run/validation entrypoints\\n- minimal smoke example\\n- troubleshooting guidance\\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\\n\\n## Notes\\nImplementation should prefer:\\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"display_title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\", \"issue_number\": 2402, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR\\u00d72 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model \\u00a77 \\u2014 **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model \\u00a73).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per \\u00a73 \\u2014 enforced and tested\\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s \\u2014 measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) \\u2014 live in their own issues.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"display_title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2529\", \"title\": \"[Daily] Inbox manageability tracker \\u2014 auto-comment thread from daily-inbox-manageability agent\", \"issue_number\": 2529, \"body\": \"## Purpose\\n\\nSingle-issue thread for the `daily-inbox-manageability` remote routine to post its daily report. Each comment is a single day's inbox state across `aceengineer.com` and `achantav@gmail.com` (personal). Mute this issue when graduated; close it when the routine is disabled.\\n\\n## Graduation criteria (the \\\"under control\\\" definition)\\n\\n- Inbox unread count **< 25** across both monitored accounts\\n- **\\u2265 5 of the 7 filter rules** in `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md` showing nonzero label counts\\n- **No new high-volume sender** (>10 messages in last 7 days) outside AutoNoise / CRE / O&G Industry / gh-dependabot labels\\n\\nWhen all 3 conditions hold for **3 consecutive days**, the agent will recommend disabling the routine in its daily comment.\\n\\n## Routine config (for reference)\\n\\n- Schedule: `0 12 * * *` UTC = **7:00 AM America/Chicago** daily\\n- Repo context: `vamseeachanta/workspace-hub`\\n- Accounts monitored: `vamsee.achanta@aceengineer.com`, `achantav@gmail.com`\\n- MCP: claude.ai Gmail connector (read+compose; mutation gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527))\\n- Tools: Bash, Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep\\n- Routine ID: `trig_01JtTcPPmVfZv6g9K846o7oN`\\n\\n## Companion artifacts\\n\\n- Filter runbook: `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`\\n- Workflow: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` (queue model per [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017))\\n- Scope-bump gate: [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527)\\n- Skill consolidation residue: [#2528](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2529\", \"display_title\": \"[Daily] Inbox manageability tracker \\u2014 auto-comment thread from daily-inbox-manageability agent\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2634\", \"title\": \"Compliance alert: W19 \\u2014 35% (high)\", \"issue_number\": 2634, \"body\": \"## Compliance Alert \\u2014 2026-05-04\\n\\n**Compliance rate:** 35% | **Severity:** high\\n**Total commits:** 31 | **Reviewed:** 6 | **Unreviewed:** 11\\n**Dashboard verdict:** FAIL\\npass\\n\\n### Unreviewed Commits\\n```\\n  - aaaefd9e wiki(engineering-standards): create DNV-RP-F103 page (closes #2627)\\n  - 75b2ea65 hermes: backfill 1 skills to .claude/skills/\\n  - 6d3483bc feat(llm-wiki): close Tier C Batch C \\u2014 engineering riser + pipeline + index sync\\n  - 38b6e0ee feat(llm-wiki): close Tier C Batch B \\u2014 maritime-law + lng-projects\\n  - d4992ec7 feat(llm-wiki): close Tier C Batch A \\u2014 asset-management + naval-architecture\\n  - 5e84e913 fix(hooks): pin python 3.11 + pyyaml for drift checks (#2618) (#2620)\\n  - 1862e004 feat(llm-wiki): close Tier B Batch 3 \\u2014 14 standards pages for #2595/#2611\\n  - 343a5937 feat(llm-wiki): close Tier B Batch 2 \\u2014 27 standards pages for #2594/#2599/#2600/#2610\\n  - 9a036003 feat(llm-wiki): close Tier B Batch 1 \\u2014 30 standards pages for #2586/#2590/#2591\\n  - e1fd3678 feat(audits): close Tier A \\u2014 marine-engineering audit + online-resource-registry refresh\\n  - 28677cc7 feat(audits): engineering wiki gap audit deliverable for #2588 (W1-C)\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Thresholds\\n| Range | Action |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| >= 80% | Pass \\u2014 no action |\\n| 50-79% | Medium priority issue |\\n| 30-49% | High priority issue |\\n| < 30% | Critical \\u2014 immediate action |\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n- [ ] Run cross-review on unreviewed commits\\n- [ ] Investigate bypass patterns\\n- [ ] Address root cause if systemic\\n\\n---\\n*Auto-generated by `scripts/enforcement/compliance-cron.sh` (#2031)*\\n*Dedup key: compliance-alert-2026-W19*\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2634\", \"display_title\": \"Compliance alert: W19 \\u2014 35% (high)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2652\", \"title\": \"Daily repo readiness tracker\", \"issue_number\": 2652, \"body\": \"# Readiness \\u2014 2026-05-06 (UTC)\\n\\n**Status:** \\u26a0 3 flags\\n\\n---\\n\\n## GSD drift\\n\\n\\u26a0 **Behind by 2 minor versions** \\u2014 installed `1.38.1`, latest `1.40.0`.\\nRunning `/gsd:update` would pull `1.40.0` from npm (`get-shit-done-cc`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Repo hygiene\\n\\n\\u2705 **Active and clean.**\\n- **24h commits:** 20+ (auto-sync \\u00d74, wiki ingest, nightly artifacts, research, handoffs, session signals \\u2014 healthy automation cadence)\\n- **Remote branches:** only `origin/main` tracked (4 days since last push)\\n- **Stale branches (>30d):** 0 \\u2014 no idle branches to prune\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PRs\\n\\n\\u2705 **1 open PR, not yet flagged.**\\n\\n| # | Title | Age | Draft? |\\n|---|-------|-----|--------|\\n| [#2649](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/pull/2649) | chore(spinout): move llm-wiki content to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki | ~1 day | No |\\n\\nPR #2649 removes 20,160 wiki files following the llm-wiki spinout. Non-draft, created 2026-05-05 \\u2014 under the 7-day flag threshold.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\n\\u26a0 **4 labels exceed 20 open issues.**\\n\\n| Label | Open | Flag |\\n|-------|------|------|\\n| `priority:medium` | 65 | \\u26a0 >20 |\\n| `enhancement` | 60 | \\u26a0 >20 |\\n| `cat:harness` | 31 | \\u26a0 >20 |\\n| `priority:high` | 24 | \\u26a0 >20 |\\n| `cat:ai-orchestration` | 18 | \\u2014 |\\n| `cat:engineering` | 17 | \\u2014 |\\n| `cat:documentation` | 16 | \\u2014 |\\n| `cat:skills` | 10 | \\u2014 |\\n| `domain:frontend-design` | 10 | \\u2014 |\\n| `claude:design` | 10 | \\u2014 |\\n\\n100 open issues fetched (page 1 limit). The `priority:high` + `cat:harness` combo suggests engineering harness improvements are accumulating \\u2014 worth a triage pass.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Planning\\n\\n\\u26a0 **Phase 07 STATE.md stale (15 days).**\\n\\n**Milestone:** v1.0 Foundation Sprint \\u2014 \\u2705 Shipped 2026-03-30 (6 phases, 21 plans, 47 tasks)\\n\\n**Active phases:**\\n\\n| Phase | Name | Plans | Status | Last STATE update |\\n|-------|------|-------|--------|-------------------|\\n| 07 | solver-verification-gate | 2/3 complete (67%) | executing | 2026-04-21 \\u26a0 15d ago |\\n| 1000 | cross-ai-parallel-planning | 3 plans present | unclear | \\u2014 |\\n\\nPhase 07 `STATE.md` records context exhaustion on 2026-04-21. One merge commit (`7cfa5c1a`) touched phase-07 files within the last 7 days, but the state file itself has not been updated \\u2014 the phase may need a resume handoff (`/gsd:resume-work`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n\\u2705 **No JS package.json at repo root** (no npm outdated to check).\\n`pyproject.toml` present with ~20 dependency lines. No automated outdated check run (no `uv` or `pip-audit` wired to this check yet).\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Generated by daily readiness checker \\u2014 2026-05-06 UTC*\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2652\", \"display_title\": \"Daily repo readiness tracker\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2003\", \"title\": \"Fix 5 failing tests in worldenergydata \\u2014 test suite cleanup (#1962 Phase 3)\", \"issue_number\": 2003, \"body\": \"## Context\\\\n\\\\nAs part of the Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring (#1962), the audit found worldenergydata has 5 failing tests that must be resolved before any refactoring can proceed safely.\\\\n\\\\n## Current State\\\\n\\\\n- Total tests: 431 (5 errors detected during collection)\\\\n- Command: `cd assetutilities && uv run python -m pytest ../worldenergydata/tests/ --noconftest` (or run from worldenergydata root)\\\\n\\\\n## Failing Tests\\\\n\\\\nRun `cd /mnt/local-analysis/workspace-hub/worldenergydata && uv run python -m pytest tests/ -v 2>&1 | grep FAILED` to identify exact failures.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\\\n- [ ] All 431 tests pass with 0 errors\\\\n- [ ] No test regressions\\\\n- [ ] Commits follow TDD convention\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2003\", \"display_title\": \"Fix 5 failing tests in worldenergydata \\u2014 test suite cleanup (#1962 Phase 3)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2006\", \"title\": \"audit(worldenergydata): 14000+ orphan modules \\u2014 triage for archival vs active use (#1962 Phase 3)\", \"issue_number\": 2006, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nTier-1 Repo Audit (#1962) identified **10+ orphan modules** in worldenergydata (files with 0 imports).\\n\\n## Orphan Detection Method\\n\\nThe audit used grep-based import counting \\u2014 a weak heuristic that misses dynamic imports, __import__(), and importlib usage. So the true orphan count may be lower.\\n\\n## Work\\n\\n1. Run AST-based orphan detection (proper import analysis)\\n2. For each confirmed orphan: check if it's a CLI entry point (not imported but executed)\\n3. Archive truly unused modules or mark with `# CLI entry point` header\\n4. Update documentation accordingly\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] AST-based orphan scan complete\\n- [ ] All orphans categorized (archive / CLI / dynamic import / keep)\\n- [ ] Unused code archived with clear git history\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2006\", \"display_title\": \"audit(worldenergydata): 14000+ orphan modules \\u2014 triage for archival vs active use (#1962 Phase 3)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2005\", \"title\": \"audit(digitalmodel): worldenergydata test collection timeout + 14K bytecode files \\u2014 investigate and resolve\", \"issue_number\": 2005, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nTier-1 Repo Audit (#1962) found critical infrastructure issues in worldenergydata:\\n\\n### Test Collection Timeout\\n- The test suite times out during collection (>30s)\\n- Cannot even enumerate tests, let alone run them\\n- Likely caused by heavy imports or expensive fixture setup\\n\\n### 14,145 Bytecode Files\\n- Extremely deep dependency tree\\n- 11.71s compile time \\u2014 major code smell\\n- May indicate excessive dependencies in pyproject.toml\\n- Consider lazy imports or splitting dev dependencies\\n\\n## Investigation Steps\\n\\n1. `uv run python -c \\\"import time; start=time.time(); import worldenergydata; print(f'import took {time.time()-start:.2f}s')\\\"`\\n2. Audit pyproject.toml \\u2014 check for unnecessary dev dependencies being installed\\n3. Profile imports: `python -X importtime -m worldenergydata 2>&1 | tail -50`\\n4. Identify which 14K .pyc files belong to which packages\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Test collection completes within 30s\\n- [ ] All 431 tests pass with 0 errors\\n- [ ] Bytecode file count explained or reduced\\n- [ ] pyproject.toml cleaned if needed\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2005\", \"display_title\": \"audit(digitalmodel): worldenergydata test collection timeout + 14K bytecode files \\u2014 investigate and resolve\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962\", \"title\": \"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring \\u2014 audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode\", \"issue_number\": 1962, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nSystematic refactoring of the workspace-hub repo ecosystem, starting with tier-1 repositories. The goal is to reduce architectural debt, consolidate duplicate patterns, enforce consistent structure, and improve agent navigability across all tier-1 repos.\\n\\n## Tier-1 Repos (Priority Order)\\n\\n| # | Repo | Purpose | Maturity | Depends On |\\n|---|------|---------|----------|------------|\\n| 1 | `digitalmodel/` | Engineering digital twin (asset integrity, CP, GIS, hydro) | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 2 | `assetutilities/` | Shared engineering utilities (config, units, calculations) | stable | \\u2014 |\\n| 3 | `assethold/` | Asset portfolio financial analysis | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 4 | `worldenergydata/` | Global energy market data (BSEE, EIA, drilling) | beta | assetutilities |\\n| 5 | `CAD-DEVELOPMENTS/` | CAD solvers, models, database, utilities | beta | \\u2014 |\\n| 6 | `aceengineer-website/` | Consulting website | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n| 7 | `aceengineer-strategy/` | GTM, business strategy | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n| 8 | `sabithaandkrishnaestates/` | SKEstates Inc. business ops | \\u2014 | \\u2014 |\\n\\n## Refactoring Scope\\n\\n### Phase 1: Audit (analysis-only, no code changes)\\n- [ ] Run `repo-architecture-analysis` on each tier-1 repo\\n- [ ] Identify cross-repo duplicate code (especially assetutilities consumers)\\n- [ ] Map dependency graph (imports, shared configs, data flows)\\n- [ ] Catalog test coverage per repo (current state)\\n- [ ] Identify orphaned/dead code, unused modules, oversized files (>400 lines)\\n- [ ] Score each repo against the Control-Plane Contract (AGENTS.md, provider adapters)\\n- [ ] Identify skill duplicates across repos (134 known from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 audit)\\n\\n### Phase 2: Plan (per-repo refactor plans)\\n- [ ] Generate refactor plan per tier-1 repo with estimated effort\\n- [ ] Prioritize by: business value \\u00d7 technical debt severity \\u00d7 dependency impact\\n- [ ] Identify breaking changes and migration paths\\n- [ ] Define test coverage targets (tier-1 = 85% per pytest.tier1.ini)\\n\\n### Phase 3: Execute (TDD, incremental, per-repo)\\n- [ ] Execute refactors repo-by-repo following dependency order (assetutilities first)\\n- [ ] TDD mandatory \\u2014 tests before implementation\\n- [ ] Each repo refactor as a separate sub-issue for tracking\\n\\n## Execution Strategy: Claude Code Plan Mode (Cloud)\\n\\n### Claude Code `--permission-mode plan` (\\\"Ultraplan\\\")\\n\\nClaude Code v2.1.92 supports `--permission-mode plan` which restricts the agent to **read-only analysis and planning** \\u2014 no file writes, no shell mutations. This is ideal for Phase 1 (Audit) and Phase 2 (Plan).\\n\\n**Proposed execution:**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Phase 1: Audit each tier-1 repo in plan mode (safe, read-only)\\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\\\\n  --print \\\\\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\\\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\\\\n  -p \\\"Audit the repository architecture of digitalmodel/. Analyze: module structure, dependency graph, test coverage, dead code, file sizes >400 lines, AGENTS.md compliance. Output a structured JSON report.\\\"\\n\\n# Phase 2: Generate refactor plan\\nclaude --permission-mode plan \\\\\\n  --print \\\\\\n  --model claude-opus-4-6 \\\\\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\\\\n  -p \\\"Given the audit report, generate a prioritized refactor plan for digitalmodel/. Include: breaking changes, migration steps, test targets, estimated effort per module.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### Cloud Execution Considerations\\n\\n| Aspect | Status | Notes |\\n|--------|--------|-------|\\n| **Claude Code CLI** | Installed (v2.1.92) | Available on ace-linux-1 |\\n| **Plan mode** | Supported | `--permission-mode plan` \\u2014 read-only, safe for audit |\\n| **API-key mode** | Supported | `--bare` + `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for headless/cloud runs |\\n| **Print mode** | Supported | `-p` / `--print` for non-interactive batch execution |\\n| **Budget cap** | Supported | `--max-budget-usd` to control spend per run |\\n| **Cloud sandbox** | Possible | Can run via Hermes `delegate_task` with `acp_command='claude'` |\\n| **Max subscription** | Claude Max $200/mo | Rate-limited but sufficient for plan-mode audit |\\n\\n### Recommended Approach\\n1. **Phase 1 + 2 (Audit + Plan)**: Run Claude Code in plan mode via `delegate_task(acp_command='claude')` \\u2014 subagents get isolated context, read-only, budget-capped\\n2. **Phase 3 (Execute)**: Requires interactive Claude Code sessions with full permissions \\u2014 NOT suited for autonomous cloud execution without user oversight\\n\\n## Adversarial Review Requirements\\n\\nPer [AI Review Routing Policy](docs/standards/AI_REVIEW_ROUTING_POLICY.md):\\n\\n- **3-agent adversarial review at BOTH stages** (plan + code/artifact)\\n- Claude: orchestrator + reviewer\\n- Codex: implementation worker + adversarial reviewer\\n- Gemini: architecture reviewer + adversarial reviewer\\n- Max 3 review iterations per deliverable\\n- All MAJOR findings must be resolved before completion\\n\\n### Review Checkpoints\\n1. **After Phase 1 (Audit)**: All 3 agents review the audit findings\\n2. **After Phase 2 (Plan)**: All 3 agents review each repo's refactor plan\\n3. **After Phase 3 (Execute)**: All 3 agents review code changes per repo\\n\\n## Related Issues\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1567 \\u2014 Feature: Continuous Repo Architecture Intelligence\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1545 \\u2014 Agentic feature progression for repo ecosystem productivity under GSD\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1603 \\u2014 Multi-repo architecture scan \\u2014 expand scanner to all tier-1 repos\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1720 \\u2014 Cross-agent session corpus audit (134 duplicate skills identified)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1734 \\u2014 chore: add domain skills to assethold (tier-1 with 0 skills)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1661 \\u2014 Architecture scanner: dependency cycle detection and layering violations\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#113 \\u2014 ROADMAP: Repo ecosystem 3-6 month horizon\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Audit report generated for each tier-1 repo\\n- [ ] Refactor plan per repo reviewed and approved by all 3 agents\\n- [ ] Phase 3 sub-issues created with clear scope per repo\\n- [ ] Test coverage meets tier-1 target (85%) after refactoring\\n- [ ] Zero cross-repo duplicate skills remaining\\n- [ ] All repos score 100% on Control-Plane Contract compliance\\n- [ ] Dependency graph documented and validated\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1962\", \"display_title\": \"FEATURE: Tier-1 Repo Ecosystem Refactoring \\u2014 audit, plan, execute with Claude Code plan mode\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2658\", \"title\": \"O&G-Standards consolidator: 8 catalog-classification defects surfaced by parallel-agent ingest\", \"issue_number\": 2658, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nIterations 8-9 of the LLM-wiki completeness loop ran 9 parallel research agents against `/mnt/ace/O&G-Standards/`. They independently surfaced the same structural classification gap in the upstream **O&G Standards Consolidation System** (per `_catalog.json` `metadata.source`, version 1.0.0, generated 2025-12-25). The consolidator's outputs \\u2014 `_catalog.json` (19.5 MB), `_inventory.db` (6.8 GB SQLite), `_catalog.html` \\u2014 encode the eight defects below, which all downstream wiki ingest, retrieval, and citation consumers inherit.\\n\\nCross-agent confirmation across 9 independent passes makes this a high-confidence, reproducible defect \\u2014 not a sampling artifact.\\n\\nSession log with full iteration history: [docs/sessions/2026-05-08-llm-wiki-completeness-loop.md](../blob/main/docs/sessions/2026-05-08-llm-wiki-completeness-loop.md)\\n\\n## Defects\\n\\n### 1. Missing organization buckets in classifier enum\\n`_catalog.json` `statistics.by_organization` enumerates only ASTM / Unknown / API / ISO / DNV / OnePetro / BSI / Norsok / MIL / NEMA / SNAME. **ABS, ASCE, ASME, AWS, NACE, IEC, HSE are absent from the enum** despite having on-disk folders (ABS / 29 PDFs, ASME / 88, AWS / 15, etc.). Their docs spill into the Unknown bucket or adjacent publishers.\\n\\n### 2. Unknown-bucket pollution (n=629)\\nSampling the 629-doc Unknown bucket shows it is dominated by ASME B16/B31 codes and ASCE-7 standards that should reclassify cleanly to their proper publisher once #1 is fixed.\\n\\n### 3. Personal-document misfiling into ISO (~196 of 308)\\n~196 of 308 ISO-tagged docs are personal/legal correspondence (BVI legal letters, bank correspondence, etc.) accidentally tagged as ISO. **Real ISO standards population is ~112 docs** \\u2014 i.e. the ISO bucket is ~64% noise.\\n\\n### 4. BSI bucket impurity ~25% (20 of 80)\\n20 of 80 BSI-tagged docs are misclassified: 4 ABS Guide PDFs, 11 FAOS joint-industry publications, 7 generic `Corrigenda.pdf` / `RCN1.pdf` files.\\n\\n### 5. API structural-fragment artefacts (n=125)\\n125 docs in API are page-fragments (`Sect_*`, `append_*`, `Page-NN-Metric-Table`) inflating the Unclassified sub-bucket. These appear to be PDF-extraction debris that was indexed as standalone docs.\\n\\n### 6. ASTM cross-series misfiling (~1,000+)\\nAcross A/D/E/G-Series boundaries: 190 misfiled in A, 121 in D, several in E, 9 in G. C/B/F-committee codes are scattered across a top-level loose bucket rather than routed to their committee folders.\\n\\n### 7. Filename quality degraded (54.7% of ASTM top-level loose)\\n54.7% of ASTM top-level loose docs carry corrupted base64-ish trailing tokens (e.g. `_QJMYNW_`), likely PDF-metadata-extraction artifacts that bled into filenames.\\n\\n### 8. OCR coverage <1% on ASTM\\nOnly **71 OCR text files for 18,000+ ASTM PDFs** \\u2014 full-text retrieval is effectively unavailable for the largest publisher in the corpus.\\n\\n## Proposed remediation\\n\\nRe-run the consolidator with:\\n\\n1. **Expanded organization enum** \\u2014 add ABS, ASCE, ASME, AWS, NACE, IEC, HSE (defect #1), unblocking #2.\\n2. **Filename heuristics** \\u2014 pre-filter personal correspondence (defect #3), structural fragments (#5), and base64 trailing tokens (#7) before classification.\\n3. **Unknown-bucket reclassification pass** \\u2014 run after #1 lands; expected to drain the bulk of the 629-doc bucket.\\n4. **Cross-series ASTM router** \\u2014 committee-prefix routing for A/B/C/D/E/F/G (defect #6); fix BSI bucket as a side-effect of stricter publisher matching (#4).\\n5. **OCR backfill** \\u2014 run OCR over the ASTM corpus (defect #8); current <1% coverage blocks any retrieval-grounded wiki page that would cite ASTM body text.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- `_catalog.json` `statistics.by_organization` includes the 7 missing publishers.\\n- Unknown bucket drops from 629 to <100.\\n- ISO bucket size reflects real ISO standards (~112), not ~308.\\n- BSI bucket purity >95%.\\n- ASTM OCR coverage >50%.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Defect surfaced by parallel-agent confirmation, not single-source reading. Memory ref: cross-agent ingest patterns make consolidator-level structural defects visible that single-pass review misses.\\n- This issue is filed against `workspace-hub` (the orchestrator/pipeline repo), not the spinout `llm-wiki` content repo, because the defect is in the upstream consolidator tooling that feeds the wiki \\u2014 not in wiki content.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2658\", \"display_title\": \"O&G-Standards consolidator: 8 catalog-classification defects surfaced by parallel-agent ingest\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423\", \"title\": \"feat: automated Gmail-side delete/archive for email-as-queue (follow-on to #2017)\", \"issue_number\": 2423, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nFollow-on to #2017 (email-as-queue workflow). Per v6 scope decision (Path 3 hybrid), #2017 v1 delivers **local-queue contract only** \\u2014 state tracking, extraction, classification. Gmail-side inbox hygiene is handled by the user manually via the Gmail UI.\\n\\nThis issue tracks the **automated Gmail-side delete/archive** capability that was de-scoped from #2017 v1.\\n\\n## Why deferred from #2017\\n\\n- Current Gmail MCP scope is read+compose only (per `reference_gmail_mcp_scope.md` memory, established 2026-04-20 session). Mutation requires either re-authorization with \\\\`gmail.modify\\\\` or browser automation.\\n- Honest scope separation: #2017 should not block on scope-negotiation work or browser-reliability engineering.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Design choice: \\\\`gmail.modify\\\\` re-auth vs browser automation vs both\\n- [ ] Implementation: when a thread reaches local state \\\\`purged\\\\`, corresponding Gmail-side action (archive-only default; optional delete behind config flag)\\n- [ ] Re-activation path tested: reply arrives on a Gmail-archived thread, local queue re-activates, Gmail label restored\\n- [ ] No regression on #2017's local queue contract\\n- [ ] User-override: any operation can be suppressed per sender domain\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **#2017 must be status:plan-approved first** \\u2014 this issue extends that contract, doesn't replace it.\\n- May be preceded by #2019 (skill consolidation) if the consolidated skill becomes the place Gmail-mutation verbs live.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent epic: #2413\\n- Contract source: #2017 v6 plan at \\\\`docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md\\\\`\\n- Memory: \\\\`reference_gmail_mcp_scope.md\\\\`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423\", \"display_title\": \"feat: automated Gmail-side delete/archive for email-as-queue (follow-on to #2017)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2572\", \"title\": \"Routine: /repo-sync + /mnt/local-analysis cleanup audit (every 2 days)\", \"issue_number\": 2572, \"body\": \"## Tracking issue for the recurring `/repo-sync` routine\\n\\n**Schedule:** every 2 days at 5am Chicago (10am UTC) \\u2014 cron `0 10 */2 * *`\\n**Routine ID:** `trig_01L3z5Q99KrmTgfEa9jhQBNo`\\n**Manage:** https://claude.ai/code/routines/trig_01L3z5Q99KrmTgfEa9jhQBNo\\n\\nThe routine posts a status comment to this issue on every run. Each comment is a single markdown table:\\n\\n| scope | action | count | notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n\\nFollowed by a `## DECISION-PENDING` section listing anything that needs human judgment (dirty worktrees, push-blocked branches, mass-deletion fingerprints matching the wave-dump pattern, etc.).\\n\\n## Operating context\\n\\nThe manual `/repo-sync` resume on 2026-05-01 cleaned 53 worktrees and freed ~36GB. Baseline going forward:\\n- `/mnt/local-analysis/` should be ~1 top-level dir (`workspace-hub`) plus optional siblings\\n- `workspace-hub` registered worktrees: ~5 (active only, no detached or orphaned)\\n- `acma-projects`: fully materialized (368K files, sparse disabled, 0 skip-worktree bits)\\n\\n## Iron Law for routine runs\\n\\n- NO `git push --force`, NO `git reset --hard`\\n- NO auto-resolve of merge conflicts\\n- NO `git commit --no-verify`\\n- `git push --no-verify` IS allowed for preservation-only branch pushes\\n- Anything ambiguous \\u2192 `DECISION-PENDING`, never decide on the user's behalf\\n\\n## Reacting to a routine comment\\n\\n- Zero `DECISION-PENDING`: drift under control, nothing to do.\\n- Non-empty `DECISION-PENDING`: triage. Common patterns:\\n  - New `codex/*` branches with unique commits \\u2192 `--no-verify` push or patch-export\\n  - Mass-deletion fingerprint (~31K dirty `D` rows) \\u2192 sparse-disable artifact, restore via `git checkout HEAD -- .`\\n  - Detached worktrees with no upstream \\u2192 ancestry probe vs `origin/main`, then keep or remove\\n\\n## Closing the issue\\n\\nDon't close \\u2014 this is a persistent watcher. To pause, toggle `enabled: false` at https://claude.ai/code/routines/trig_01L3z5Q99KrmTgfEa9jhQBNo\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2572\", \"display_title\": \"Routine: /repo-sync + /mnt/local-analysis cleanup audit (every 2 days)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\", \"issue_number\": 2657, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\\n\\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\\n\\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\\n\\nReads:\\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\\n- `github.github-issues`\\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\\n\\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\\n\\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\\n\\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\\n\\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"display_title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312\", \"title\": \"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority\", \"issue_number\": 2312, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nClaude continues to read removed local work-queue lifecycle scripts even though GitHub issues and `.planning/` are now the authoritative work-tracking surfaces:\\n\\n- `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh` \\u2014 94 reads\\n- `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh` \\u2014 62 reads\\n- `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh` \\u2014 60 reads\\n- 216 total remediation-mapped stale reads in the latest provider-session ecosystem audit\\n\\nThis indicates parts of the repo ecosystem still imply that local queue lifecycle scripts are canonical, which wastes session budget and weakens the GitHub-first workflow.\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nRemove remaining live references that teach agents to use the deleted local lifecycle scripts, and replace them with current queue-authority surfaces.\\n\\n## Canonical redirect targets\\n\\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.py`\\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.sh`\\n- `notes/agent-work-queue.md`\\n- `.planning/`\\n- GitHub issues\\n- `docs/work-queue-workflow.md`\\n- `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Find live docs, prompts, templates, and routing instructions that still reference:\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh`\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh`\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh`\\n2. Update those surfaces so they describe GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh scripts as the authoritative workflow.\\n3. Expand stale-reference regression coverage where needed so deleted lifecycle-script references stay confined to explicit legacy/reference docs.\\n4. Refresh the provider-session ecosystem audit after cleanup.\\n\\n## Existing related issues\\n\\n- #1717 \\u2014 policy/docs contradiction between GitHub issues and legacy work-queue guidance\\n- #2213 \\u2014 expand strict stale-reference enforcement across more live docs\\n- #2214 \\u2014 split current architecture guidance from legacy wrapper redirects\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Live instructional surfaces no longer reference the deleted lifecycle scripts\\n- [ ] Current queue authority is documented as GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh helpers\\n- [ ] Regression tests cover the deleted lifecycle-script references in protected live docs/templates\\n- [ ] Provider-session ecosystem audit is refreshed after cleanup and linked from the issue\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n- `analysis/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.json`\\n- `docs/reports/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.md`\\n- Audit timestamp: `2026-04-16T23:34:23Z`\\n- Reference doc: `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312\", \"display_title\": \"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2310\", \"title\": \"analysis(harness): rank Claude stale-read migration-debt backlog and link remediation issues\", \"issue_number\": 2310, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe refreshed provider session ecosystem audit (generated 2026-04-16T23:34:23Z) shows Claude still carries the highest absolute migration-debt volume in the repo ecosystem:\\n\\n- 7,563 missing repo reads\\n- 972 remediation-mapped stale reads across the top 4 known rule clusters\\n- 12.56 known migration-debt reads per 1k Claude records\\n\\nThis issue is the ranked backlog anchor for the strongest Claude stale-read clusters so follow-up cleanup stays deliberate instead of being repeatedly rediscovered in session logs.\\n\\n## Ranked stale-read clusters\\n\\n1. `legacy_work_queue_transition` \\u2014 318 reads\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/start_stage.py` \\u2014 138\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/exit_stage.py` \\u2014 137\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/verify_checklist.py` \\u2014 43\\n   - Canonical redirects: `docs/governance/SESSION-GOVERNANCE.md`, `docs/governance/TRUST-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `scripts/workflow/governance-checkpoints.yaml`, `.claude/hooks/plan-approval-gate.sh`, `.claude/hooks/session-governor-check.sh`, `scripts/review/cross-review.sh`\\n\\n2. `legacy_work_queue_html_review` \\u2014 249 reads\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/generate-html-review.py` \\u2014 249\\n   - Canonical redirects: `scripts/review/cross-review.sh`, `templates/review-standard.html`, `docs/work-queue-workflow.md`\\n   - Existing related issues: #104, #105, #1351\\n\\n3. `legacy_work_queue_lifecycle` \\u2014 216 reads\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh` \\u2014 94\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh` \\u2014 62\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh` \\u2014 60\\n   - Canonical redirects: `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.py`, `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.sh`, `notes/agent-work-queue.md`, `.planning/`, GitHub issues\\n\\n4. `legacy_work_queue_skills` \\u2014 189 reads\\n   - `.claude/skills/workspace-hub/work-queue-workflow/SKILL.md` \\u2014 123\\n   - `.claude/skills/coordination/workspace/work-queue/SKILL.md` \\u2014 66\\n   - Canonical redirects: `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/commands/gsd/*`, `.gemini/get-shit-done/workflows/*`, `docs/work-queue-workflow.md`\\n   - Existing related issues: #1717, #2213, #2214\\n\\n## Why this matters\\n\\nClaude session logs are still wasting reads on removed work-queue surfaces, which means:\\n- prompt/context drift is still teaching obsolete paths\\n- audits keep rediscovering the same migration debt\\n- agent sessions lose efficiency by probing dead files instead of current governance/issue-tracking surfaces\\n\\n## Desired outcome\\n\\n- Ranked follow-up issues exist for the strongest uncovered clusters\\n- Existing related issues are explicitly linked so we do not duplicate cleanup work\\n- Future audit refreshes can report progress against concrete issue numbers instead of generic remediation hints\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] The strongest Claude stale-read clusters are linked to concrete GitHub issues\\n- [ ] Existing overlapping issues are referenced instead of duplicated\\n- [ ] New follow-up issues are created for any top-ranked clusters not already covered\\n- [ ] This issue records the current audit timestamp and ranking basis\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n- `analysis/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.json`\\n- `docs/reports/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.md`\\n- Audit timestamp: `2026-04-16T23:34:23Z`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2310\", \"display_title\": \"analysis(harness): rank Claude stale-read migration-debt backlog and link remediation issues\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\", \"issue_number\": 2656, \"body\": \"## Objective\\n\\nPlan a conservative, repo-by-repo folder/file structure normalization for `workspace-hub` under the workspace-hub tier-1 ecosystem workflow.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nPlanning only until explicit user approval. The plan must inventory current structure, identify root clutter/generated-output risk, propose a bounded Phase 1 refactor contract, define TDD/verification gates, and preserve evidence needed for rollback.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n- Canonical plan artifact under `docs/plans/`.\\n- Review artifact under `scripts/review/results/`.\\n- Final issue comment linking the plan and review artifact.\\n\\n## Approval Gate\\n\\nNo file moves, package reorganization, deletion, or cleanup execution is authorized until this issue is explicitly approved after plan review.\\n\\nParent ecosystem anchors: `workspace-hub#1962`, `workspace-hub#2397`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"display_title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\", \"issue_number\": 2653, \"body\": \"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\\npipeline cleanly.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] New session \\u2192 new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) \\u2192 same log file continues\\n- [ ] Session idle >2h \\u2192 next tool call starts a new log file\\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **19. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **20. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\", \"issue_number\": 2551, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\\n\\n## Why\\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\\n\\n## Scope\\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Root hardening: #2546\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"display_title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\", \"issue_number\": 2528, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\\\"12 skills \\u2192 4-5\\\") is partially complete \\u2014 `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\\n\\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\\n\\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\\n\\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\\n\\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n\\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed \\u2014 no broken references to deleted skills\\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable \\u2014 referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\\\"*.md\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.py\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.yaml\\\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\\n