{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/llm-wiki","query":"is:issue is:open","sort":"updated","order":"desc","topn":30},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/13\", \"title\": \"epic(knowledge): llm-wiki strengthening roadmap and execution waves\", \"issue_number\": 13, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nCreate an umbrella roadmap for the current llm-wiki strengthening program, grouping the recently created issues into execution waves with explicit dependencies, parallelization notes, and staging guidance.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe repo now has a substantial llm-wiki improvement portfolio spanning provenance, governance, promotion waves, and navigation/discoverability. The next bottleneck is no longer idea discovery; it is execution sequencing.\\n\\nA dependency-aware roadmap is needed so the work does not start in the wrong order, duplicate effort, or force rework across related surfaces such as provenance fields, promotion audit trails, batch-pack execution, and wiki navigation.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Group the current llm-wiki issue set into execution waves.\\n- Record hard prerequisites vs soft sequencing preferences.\\n- Mark which issues can run safely in parallel in separate worktrees.\\n- Highlight readiness mismatches and scope caveats discovered during recommendation review.\\n- Keep this issue as a planning/steering umbrella only; do not absorb implementation work from child issues.\\n\\n## Current issue set in scope\\n### Provenance / governance / data foundation\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363 wiki_refs reverse lookup\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 provenance backfill on pre-existing wiki pages\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2382 promotion audit-trail checker\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 GUARD-1 invented-layer detector\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 transient-promotion candidate queue\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 WRK completions normalization\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2381 handoff expiration metadata\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2384 recurring-run output pruner\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 source_doc_key threading through promotion pipeline\\n\\n### Promotion waves / content expansion\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 Batch Pack 1 API/standards-portal metadata promotion\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 Batch Pack 2 indexed conference-summary promotion\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2373 Batch Pack 4 non-ACMA standards-summary promotion\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 Batch Pack 3 Tier A external engineering software profiles\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 design-code registry promotion\\n\\n### Navigation / discoverability\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 strengthening scorecard\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 large-domain portal pages\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29 source-title aliasing\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2378 canonical marine-engineering index chunking/pagination\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379 registry/task explorer\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#27 wiki index uplink/back-navigation standard\\n\\n## Recommended execution waves\\n### Wave 0 \\u2014 external prerequisites / schema authority\\nThese are prerequisite context or adjacent issues that shape later work:\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 update wiki CLAUDE.md files to require doc_key\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2233 promoted_from frontmatter guidance\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362 back-populate doc_key on pre-existing standards-transfer-ledger entries\\n\\n### Wave 1 \\u2014 low-risk provenance and guardrail foundations\\nCan largely run in parallel in separate worktrees:\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 GUARD-1 invented-layer detector\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 source_doc_key threading through promotion pipeline\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363 wiki_refs reverse lookup (best after vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23; stronger after vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362)\\n\\n### Wave 2 \\u2014 legacy provenance repair and transient metadata substrate\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 provenance backfill on pre-existing wiki pages\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2381 computable expiration metadata on session handoffs\\n\\n### Wave 3 \\u2014 transient intake and candidate extraction\\nCan run in parallel after Wave 2 metadata is stable:\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 transient-promotion candidate queue\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 WRK completions normalization\\n\\n### Wave 4 \\u2014 governance enforcement / cleanup on top of the new substrate\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2382 promotion audit-trail checker\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2384 promotion-aware recurring-run output pruner\\n\\n### Wave 5 \\u2014 first promotion-family execution\\nCan run in parallel in separate worktrees:\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 Batch Pack 1 API/standards-portal metadata promotion\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 design-code registry promotion\\n\\n### Wave 6 \\u2014 next promotion-family execution\\nCan run in parallel, but note readiness caveat on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369:\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 Batch Pack 3 Tier A external engineering software profiles\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 Batch Pack 2 indexed conference-summary promotion\\n\\nReadiness note:\\n- review found a live scope mismatch for vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369: the issue body names DOT/OMAE/ISOPE as phase-A-complete starter collections, but repo data indicated DOT/OMAE/OTC are phase-A complete while ISOPE is not yet indexed. This should be reconciled before execution.\\n\\n### Wave 7 \\u2014 broader standards-summary promotion\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2373 Batch Pack 4 non-ACMA standards-summary promotion\\n\\n### Wave 8 \\u2014 navigation/discoverability improvements after content/provenance progress\\nRecommended sequence:\\n1. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29 source-title aliasing\\n2. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 strengthening scorecard (can overlap with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29)\\n3. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 large-domain portal pages and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379 registry/task explorer in parallel\\n4. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2378 canonical marine-engineering index chunking/pagination\\n5. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#27 wiki index uplink/back-navigation standard\\n\\n## Parallelization rules\\n- Separate worktrees are required for concurrent implementation waves touching shared docs/wiki/report surfaces.\\n- Good parallel bundles:\\n  - Wave 1: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\\n  - Wave 3: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 + vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38\\n  - Wave 5: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 + vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n  - Wave 6: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 (after vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 readiness fix)\\n  - Wave 8 mid-phase: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Canonical roadmap/dependency graph for the llm-wiki strengthening program.\\n- Child-issue grouping by wave.\\n- Explicit notes on hard vs soft dependencies.\\n- Parallelization guidance for future execution planning.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] current llm-wiki strengthening issues are grouped into waves with rationale\\n- [ ] hard and soft dependencies are called out explicitly\\n- [ ] known readiness mismatches are recorded in the roadmap\\n- [ ] roadmap remains a planning/steering umbrella rather than absorbing child implementation scope\\n\\n## Related\\n- Parent operating model: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Durable/transient boundary: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209\\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\\n- Priority queue + batch-pack design: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n\\n## Work Stream G: Tier-1 repo ecosystem routing + retrieval surfaces (Priority 1.5)\\n*Make the durable knowledge layer actually usable across the repo portfolio, not just inside workspace-hub wiki artifacts*\\n\\nThis roadmap originally focused on wiki/provenance/promotion internals. A portfolio review on 2026-04-22 found an adjacent bottleneck: even when knowledge exists, workers still lack consistent per-repo routing surfaces for where code/docs/tests should live and how future issue work should retrieve canonical targets. That gap weakens llm-wiki compounding value because promoted knowledge cannot land cleanly in downstream repos.\\n\\n| Issue | Title | Function |\\n|-------|-------|----------|\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 | Tier-1 indexing and code-placement contract | portfolio-wide routing contract |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461 | assetutilities routing surfaces and source-hygiene cleanup | highest-risk repo remediation |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462 | digitalmodel repo-wide operator map and canonical routing surfaces | engineering-core remediation |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463 | aceengineer-website canonical routing surfaces cleanup | GTM/externalization remediation |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464 | workspace-hub curated routing index + routing-noise cleanup | control-plane remediation |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465 | daily tier-1 indexing freshness audit | ongoing governance loop |\\n\\nRecommended sequence:\\n1. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 defines the shared contract.\\n2. Execute repo remediations in this order: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464.\\n3. Keep vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465 as the sustaining daily audit/scorecard loop.\\n\\nWhy this belongs in the llm-wiki roadmap:\\n- llm-wiki is the durable cross-repo knowledge layer in the repo ecosystem model.\\n- repo-specific routing/index surfaces are the landing pads that convert knowledge into correct repo-level execution.\\n- without these repo surfaces, agents still rediscover placement and retrieval paths, reducing the return on wiki promotion work.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/13\", \"display_title\": \"epic(knowledge): llm-wiki strengthening roadmap and execution waves\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40\", \"title\": \"Research: reservoir engineering literature \\u2014 local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki\", \"issue_number\": 40, \"body\": \"## Goal\\n\\nBuild out the reservoir-engineering substrate of llm-wiki by mining (a) the user's existing local PDF corpus on ace-linux-1 (`/mnt/ace`, 30,499 PDFs) and (b) public online sources, then ingesting the relevant material under llm-wiki's MIT + CC-BY-4.0 license. Drives both the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026) competition (deeper domain literacy \\u2192 better modeling decisions) and longer-term wikis around oil & gas / subsurface engineering.\\n\\nCompanion issue: [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) covers competition-specific *prior art* (datasets + ML papers); this issue covers the broader *educational foundation* (textbooks, coursework, classic papers).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n**In-scope source types**\\n\\n- Textbooks on reservoir engineering, petroleum engineering, formation evaluation, well logging, drilling, geosteering.\\n- University coursework \\u2014 open syllabi, lecture notes, problem sets from Stanford SDSS, Texas A&M, U Texas Austin, Heriot-Watt, IFP, Imperial.\\n- Conference papers \\u2014 SPE, AAPG, SEG, EAGE \\u2014 with care about open-access vs paywalled.\\n- Industry standards / methodology PDFs (DNV, API, ISO).\\n- Theses and dissertations from public university repositories.\\n- ArXiv preprints in petroleum engineering, geophysics, ML-for-geosteering categories.\\n\\n**Out of scope (license / IP risk)**\\n\\n- Pirated or unauthorized copies of paywalled textbooks, even if found locally.\\n- Vendor-derivative material under proprietary license.\\n- The deny-list per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482) governance: nothing under `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/sources/` should be cited; cite the canonical standard or concept page instead.\\n\\n## Sources to mine\\n\\n### Local \\u2014 `/mnt/ace` (ace-linux-1)\\n\\n- `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` \\u2014 top candidate directory by name. First pass: recursively list, classify by filename / metadata, flag candidates.\\n- `/mnt/ace/aceengineer-admin/Reference/` \\u2014 mixed (mostly tax / admin docs in spot-check, but may contain technical references).\\n- Other dirs revealed during initial sweep.\\n- Total PDFs in `/mnt/ace`: ~30,499. Realistic target: 50\\u2013200 ingest-worthy after deduplication and license filtering.\\n\\n### Online (representative starting points)\\n\\n- **Stanford Stanford Doerr School OCW**: open courses on petroleum / energy resources.\\n- **Texas A&M PETE OCW** and **U Texas Austin Petroleum Engineering** open content.\\n- **Heriot-Watt PE** open materials.\\n- **arXiv physics.geo-ph** and **stat.ML** intersection \\u2014 search \\\"well log\\\", \\\"geosteering\\\", \\\"lithology classification\\\".\\n- **OnePetro** free-access entries (SPE / AAPG / SEG; many old papers are now open).\\n- **AAPG Datapages** open-access portion.\\n- **USGS Open-File Reports** in petroleum geology.\\n- **OAPEN** and **Springer Open** for free textbooks.\\n- **MIT OpenCourseWare** earth-and-planetary courses with subsurface relevance.\\n\\n## Output: llm-wiki structure\\n\\nExisting top-level dirs (verified 2026-05-06): `docs/`, `scripts/`, `seeds/`, `tests/`, `wikis/`.\\n\\nProposed additions / extensions (subject to existing wiki conventions; defer final layout to whoever owns llm-wiki structure decisions):\\n\\n- `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` (new, if not present) with:\\n  - `concepts/` \\u2014 fundamentals: porosity, permeability, saturation, capillary pressure, relative permeability, etc.\\n  - `methodology/` \\u2014 geosteering workflow, reservoir characterization, log interpretation, formation evaluation.\\n  - `standards/` \\u2014 DNV / API / ISO references with [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)-shape frontmatter (`code_id`, `publisher`, `revision`).\\n  - `sources/` \\u2014 citation index, NOT ingestion targets per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482).\\n- `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` \\u2014 log of every source examined, decision (ingest / skip / defer), license note.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. **Local sweep.** Inventory `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` and other candidate dirs. Output: a manifest of `(filepath, size, page-count, title-from-metadata, classification)` rows. ~1 hr scripted.\\n2. **Online sweep.** 6\\u201310 best-of-class courses, textbooks (open-access only), and survey papers. Bookmark + brief description. ~1\\u20132 hr.\\n3. **License triage.** Drop everything that's not clearly redistributable. Prefer creative-commons or public-domain (older works > 70 yrs).\\n4. **Wiki page drafts.** Write 5\\u201315 concept pages (`wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/*.md`) in llm-wiki's existing style. Cite sources, never copy. Apply the calc-citation contract (`workspace-hub/.claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md`) where formulas appear.\\n5. **PR with the corpus + wiki pages + citation log.** Reviewer checks license, citation, and that copy is original (not paraphrased > 30-word chunks).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `/mnt/ace` reservoir-engineering inventory at `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` lists at least 50 candidate sources with classification (ingest / skip / defer) and license note.\\n- [ ] At least 5 concept pages drafted under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/` covering core fundamentals (porosity, permeability, gamma-ray log interpretation, dip / azimuth, formation tops).\\n- [ ] At least 2 methodology pages under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/methodology/` covering geosteering workflow + log correlation.\\n- [ ] All cited sources licensed for redistribution OR cited only as reference (no in-page copying).\\n- [ ] PR opened, reviewed, merged with the standard llm-wiki review process.\\n- [ ] Cross-link added to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) when the wiki pages are ready, so Kaggle modeling work can reference them.\\n\\n## Risks and open questions\\n\\n- **Risk:** `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` may contain user-purchased textbooks not licensed for redistribution. Triage carefully \\u2014 local-use-only OK, ingestion-to-public-repo NOT OK.\\n- **Open:** Should reservoir-engineering wiki pages live under a top-level `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` or inside the existing marine/offshore family? Defer to llm-wiki maintainer decision.\\n- **Open:** What citation style \\u2014 IEEE-numeric, APA, or the inline `code_id` style from [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)? Likely match the existing llm-wiki convention.\\n\\n## Time budget\\n\\nA few sessions across 1\\u20132 weeks. Don't disappear into a literature rabbit hole; the 50-source target keeps it bounded.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40\", \"display_title\": \"Research: reservoir engineering literature \\u2014 local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\", \"issue_number\": 26, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\\n\\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\\n- Explicitly exclude:\\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs\", \"issue_number\": 48, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #26 Batch Pack 4 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #26\\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #26: plan branch `plan/issue-2373-batch-pack-4` at approved SHA `c516ec853`.\\n- Upstream gate `vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471` is now closed, but the public spinout repo still lacks the approval-bound plan artifact and required data inputs.\\n\\n## Scope\\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 4 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 4\\n- transfer ledger input required for the cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural standards slice\\n- topic-cluster and alias inputs required by the approved plan\\n- any approved summary-backed evidence surface required to avoid raw PDF rereads\\n- provenance notes binding restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\\n- validation checklist for duplicate/extend-vs-create mapping, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw/vendor boundaries\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No Batch Pack 4 promotion execution in this prep issue.\\n- No ledger/cluster reconstruction from memory.\\n- No raw PDF rereads, source extraction, OCR, or standards text summarization.\\n- No standards wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\\n- No credentials, private source text, vendor standards text, formulas, tables, or copied clauses in the public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 4 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\\n- [ ] Required transfer ledger, topic-cluster, and alias inputs are available in a public-safe form.\\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\\n- [ ] Future #26 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\\n- [ ] #26 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #26\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\", \"issue_number\": 25, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\\n\\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \\\"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\\\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\\n\\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\\n\\n## Related\\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs\", \"issue_number\": 47, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #25 Batch Pack 1 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #25\\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #25: plan branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` at approved SHA `7cc1c0b1a`.\\n- Current blocker: the public spinout repo does not contain the approval-bound plan artifact or the required online-resource registry inputs.\\n\\n## Scope\\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 1 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 1\\n- `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` or an approved public-safe extracted subset sufficient for Batch Pack 1\\n- any overlay/processed input required by the approved plan\\n- provenance notes binding the restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\\n- validation checklist for duplicate checks, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw boundaries\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No Batch Pack 1 promotion execution in this prep issue.\\n- No registry reconstruction from memory.\\n- No source re-download or raw source parsing.\\n- No API/portal wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\\n- No credentials, API keys, private endpoints, private source text, or vendor text in the public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 1 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\\n- [ ] The required registry input or approved subset is available in a public-safe form.\\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\\n- [ ] Future #25 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\\n- [ ] #25 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #25\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\", \"issue_number\": 19, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\\n\\n## Context\\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\\n\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` \\u2014 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` \\u2014 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` \\u2014 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\\n\\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\\n\\n## Problem\\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\\n\\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\\n\\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 46, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations material:\\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\\n- handling rules for magazine/offshore-operation articles, heavy-lift/pipelay source material, images, PDFs, and archives\\n- allowed public bibliographic metadata and authored high-level synthesis\\n- disallowed copied article text, figures, vendor/private material, and raw archive contents\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` content into git.\\n- No OCR, article summarization from raw files, figure extraction, archive extraction, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No copyrighted article text, images, credentials, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored synthesis, copyrighted article text, images/figures, archives, and vendor/private material.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 45, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any HSE/safety dataset metadata or wiki promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until dataset clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for HSE/safety dataset material:\\n- dataset-level clearance fields required before promotion\\n- allowed public metadata fields, dataset citations, and aggregate descriptions\\n- disallowed personally identifiable information, incident-sensitive records, raw CSV/TXT rows, and proprietary/private derived data\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules for HSE concepts and source metadata\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/PII/secret scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw dataset extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` content into git.\\n- No CSV/TXT row promotion, ZIP extraction, incident-record summarization, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No PII, private source text, credentials, or raw safety data in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate dataset/artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, aggregate public synthesis, raw rows, PII/sensitive incident records, archives, and derived summaries.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/PII boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 44, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any BSEE/offshore source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #19\\n- Source family: BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates\\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for BSEE/offshore candidate material:\\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\\n- handling rules for client/project-sensitive files, permit/activity samples, spreadsheets, document archives, and data descriptions\\n- allowed public metadata fields versus disallowed extracted content\\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/client-sensitive boundary scans\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` content into git.\\n- No OCR, table extraction, workbook extraction, PDF/DOCX summarization, ZIP inspection for promotion, or direct wiki stub generation.\\n- No client/project-sensitive files, credentials, permit details, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, client/project-sensitive data, proprietary/project material, archives, and authored synthesis.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/client-sensitive boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #19\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\", \"issue_number\": 14, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\\n\\n## Source of record\\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\\n\\n## Why\\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\\n\\n## Scope\\nIn scope:\\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\\n- No source/staging cleanup.\\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43\", \"title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist\", \"issue_number\": 43, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any SESA LNG corpus extraction can proceed from #14.\\n\\n## Parent blocker\\n- Parent issue: #14\\n- Raw/source family: SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa`\\n- Current status: extraction remains blocked until clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist that defines what must exist before extraction starts:\\n- row-level or artifact-level clearance fields required for any proposed first tranche\\n- allowed source evidence types and disallowed source evidence types\\n- public-repo output boundaries for summaries, metadata, and target wiki pages\\n- required approvals for vendor, client/project-sensitive, archive, workbook, and standards-derived materials\\n- validation expectations before any future extraction commit\\n- required separate implementation issue structure after clearance is complete\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw file extraction.\\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa` content into git.\\n- No OCR, text extraction, table extraction, workbook extraction, or PDF summarization.\\n- No vendor standards text, private archive material, credentials, client-sensitive content, or project specifications in this public repo.\\n- No closing #14 until this checklist and a later bounded implementation lane are complete.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored public synthesis, vendor-derived text, client/project-sensitive files, archives, and standards material.\\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor boundary explicitly.\\n- [ ] #14 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #14\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43\", \"display_title\": \"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions\", \"issue_number\": 41, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the maritime-law wiki.\\n\\n## Decision source\\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for IMO/ILO convention and code pages.\\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Plan and then implement a bounded metadata-only migration or mirror strategy for eligible maritime-law convention/code pages currently under `wikis/maritime-law/wiki/concepts/`.\\n- Candidate pages include SOLAS, MARPOL, MLC, and ISM Code, subject to duplicate/path review.\\n- Preserve `consolidated_edition` where that is the correct public metadata field.\\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No convention/code text copying.\\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, or source excerpts.\\n- No broad maritime-law schema rewrite beyond the routing implementation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Eligible pages have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\\n- Existing concept links are preserved or redirected/mirrored safely.\\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #15\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing\", \"issue_number\": 42, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the LNG-projects wiki.\\n\\n## Decision source\\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for LNG codes and standards pages.\\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Plan and then implement bounded metadata-only standards pages for LNG codes when public metadata is sufficient.\\n- Candidate families include CSA-Z276, NFPA 59A, and IGC Code, subject to public metadata verification and duplicate/path review.\\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No standard text copying.\\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, project specifications, or source excerpts.\\n- No broad LNG content expansion beyond standards-routing implementation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Eligible LNG standards have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\\n- Any insufficient public metadata is split into follow-up work instead of guessed.\\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\\n\\n## Related\\n- #15\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/39\", \"title\": \"feat: engineering wiki \\u2014 ingest skill metadata as wiki pages\", \"issue_number\": 39, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nIngest the 691+ skill definitions from `.claude/skills/` into the engineering wiki as entity/concept pages.\\n\\n## Context\\nThe engineering wiki SOURCE_INVENTORY.md lists skill metadata as a future source class. Each engineering skill (OrcaFlex, FEA, cathodic protection, API standards, etc.) contains structured knowledge that should compound into the wiki.\\n\\n## Approach\\n- Scan `.claude/skills/` for engineering-relevant skills\\n- Classify each as entity (tool/system) or concept (methodology/pattern)\\n- Create wiki pages with frontmatter, cross-references to existing pages\\n- Estimated yield: 50-100 additional wiki pages\\n\\n## Related\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (parent \\u2014 engineering wiki seed)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2022 (skills \\u2192 service pages for aceengineer.com)\\n- SOURCE_INVENTORY.md \\\"Future Source Classes\\\" section\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/39\", \"display_title\": \"feat: engineering wiki \\u2014 ingest skill metadata as wiki pages\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/38\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): normalize WRK completions into structured seeds and wiki-candidate corpus\", \"issue_number\": 38, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nNormalize `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` into structured seeds and a wiki-candidate corpus, so archived work completions become queryable durable knowledge instead of raw memory-migration blobs.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that the WRK completion corpus still exists primarily as raw JSONL:\\n- `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` contains the migrated corpus, but records are still raw-string oriented.\\n- the knowledge-persistence architecture explicitly proposed a structured `knowledge/seeds/wrk-completions.yaml` target and follow-on hook work.\\n- current repo state still does not expose a normalized WRK seed surface for durable wiki promotion.\\n\\nThis is a strong tacit-knowledge opportunity because the repo already has the corpus; what is missing is structure and promotion-readiness.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Parse existing `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` into a normalized structured seed surface.\\n- Add fields such as category, subcategory, title, completed_at, artifacts, tests, reusable patterns, follow-ons, related docs, and GitHub issue references where recoverable.\\n- Produce a second-stage wiki-candidate projection for reusable domain/process learnings.\\n- Frame this as a follow-on to existing archive/backfill work rather than a duplicate of it.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Structured WRK completion seed artifact(s).\\n- Mapping/report from raw WRK completions -> normalized entries.\\n- Wiki-candidate projection/report for durable promotion opportunities.\\n- Guidance for future append/update flow so new completions do not remain raw-only.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] raw WRK completion records are normalized into structured fields where evidence exists\\n- [ ] a durable seed/corpus replaces raw-only querying for this knowledge surface\\n- [ ] output includes wiki-candidate routing rather than only archival normalization\\n- [ ] scope is positioned as a follow-on to archive/backfill work, not a duplicate of it\\n\\n## Related\\n- Archive synthesis + knowledge backfill: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#103\\n- Knowledge-persistence architecture / closed predecessor: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#894\\n- Transient-promotion queue: companion issue\\n- Closed-issue promotion ledger: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2370\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/38\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): normalize WRK completions into structured seeds and wiki-candidate corpus\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/36\", \"title\": \"feat: cross-wiki link discovery and infrastructure\", \"issue_number\": 36, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nBuild tooling to discover and maintain cross-links between the 3 domain wikis (marine-engineering, maritime-law, naval-architecture).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWikis are currently siloed. Real engineering topics span domains:\\n- Deepwater Horizon \\u2192 engineering (engineering) + law (OPA 90)  \\n- Mooring failures \\u2192 marine-eng + naval-arch stability analysis\\n- Classification society rules \\u2192 naval-arch + maritime-law liability\\n\\n## Proposed: Cross-Wiki Link Index\\n\\n```\\nknowledge/wikis/cross-links.md\\n```\\n\\n| Source Wiki | Entity/Concept | Target Wiki | Target Page | Link Type |\\n|-------------|---------------|-------------|-------------|-----------|\\n| maritime-law | Deepwater Horizon | marine-engineering | lng-carrier-mooring | related-case |\\n| maritime-law | Amoco Cadiz | naval-architecture | ship-structures | hull-failure |\\n\\n## Tooling\\n\\n`llm-wiki cross-links --source wiki --target wiki` command:\\n1. Scan source wiki for mentions of entities in target wiki\\n2. Scan target wiki for mentions of source wiki entities\\n3. Report candidate links\\n4. Optionally create cross-wiki reference pages\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] cross-lines.md generated with at least 10 discovered links\\n- [ ] `llm-wiki cross-links` CLI command\\n- [ ] Existing wiki pages updated with cross-references\\n\\n## Related\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1995 (closed)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2000 (closed \\u2014 seeds migrated)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/36\", \"display_title\": \"feat: cross-wiki link discovery and infrastructure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/35\", \"title\": \"feat: engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis\", \"issue_number\": 35, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nRun cross-wiki link discovery between the engineering wiki and the 3 domain wikis (marine-engineering, maritime-law, naval-architecture) to surface implicit connections.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe engineering wiki (#2034) has 52 pages with 111 cross-references, but links to domain wikis are minimal. Many concepts (VIV, mooring failures, cathodic protection, pipeline integrity) appear in both the engineering methodology wiki and the marine-engineering domain wiki. These implicit connections should be surfaced.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Run `llm-wiki cross-links` (from vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36) between engineering <-> marine-engineering\\n2. Update engineering wiki pages with `[[wiki:marine-engineering/page]]` links where relevant\\n3. Update domain wiki pages with `[[wiki:engineering/page]]` links back\\n4. Generate `knowledge/wikis/cross-links.md` index of discovered connections\\n\\n## Expected High-Value Connections\\n\\n| Engineering Wiki Page | Domain Wiki Page | Link Type |\\n|----------------------|-----------------|-----------|\\n| VIV Riser Fatigue | marine-eng/mooring-line-failure | related-concept |\\n| Cathodic Protection Design | marine-eng/cathodic-protection-system | methodology |\\n| Pipeline Integrity Assessment | marine-eng/corrosion-control | assessment |\\n| Solver Queue | marine-eng/lng-carrier-mooring | tool-usage |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Cross-link scan completed between engineering and all 3 domain wikis\\n- [ ] At least 15 bidirectional cross-references discovered and added\\n- [ ] `knowledge/wikis/cross-links.md` index created\\n- [ ] Both engineering and domain wiki indexes updated\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 (cross-wiki link discovery \\u2014 parent issue)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (engineering wiki seed \\u2014 completed)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/35\", \"display_title\": \"feat: engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/34\", \"title\": \"feat: engineering wiki \\u2014 ingest remaining high-value sources (skills metadata, closed issues)\", \"issue_number\": 34, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nExpand the engineering wiki with pages from the remaining high-value source classes identified but not yet ingested during the initial seed (#2034).\\n\\n## Source Classes to Ingest\\n\\n### Skills Metadata (`.claude/skills/`)\\n- 691+ skills, each could become a wiki entity or concept page\\n- Focus on engineering-specific skills first (orcaflex, fea, cathodic, mooring, etc.)\\n- Extract: skill name, domain, key capabilities, dependencies\\n- Target: 20-30 pages covering the most valuable skills\\n\\n### Closed Engineering GitHub Issues\\n- Issues with labels `cat:engineering`, `cat:engineering-calculations`, `cat:engineering-methodology`\\n- Extract: problem solved, approach taken, key decisions\\n- Target: 10-15 pages from the most instructive closed issues\\n\\n### Mooring Failures Seed (`knowledge/seeds/mooring-failures-lng-terminals.yaml`)\\n- 40 entries of real mooring failure incidents\\n- Each entry could become an entity page or feed existing marine-engineering wiki\\n- Cross-link to engineering wiki's VIV, mooring, and pipeline concepts\\n\\n### Overnight Batch Run Reports\\n- Outputs from nightly researcher agents (`.planning/research/`)\\n- Extract: key findings, domain insights, methodology patterns\\n- Target: 5-10 pages from highest-value research outputs\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] At least 30 new pages from the above sources\\n- [ ] SOURCE_INVENTORY.md updated with new class entries\\n- [ ] Index and log updated\\n- [ ] Lint passes clean\\n- [ ] Cross-references to existing pages added\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (engineering wiki seed \\u2014 completed, 52 pages)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2036 (cron ingest)\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 (cross-wiki link discovery)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/34\", \"display_title\": \"feat: engineering wiki \\u2014 ingest remaining high-value sources (skills metadata, closed issues)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/33\", \"title\": \"WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities\", \"issue_number\": 33, \"body\": \"## WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** pending | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** knowledge-domain | **Subcategory:** maritime-law\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### Mission\\n\\nEstablish maritime law as a first-class knowledge domain in workspace-hub by creating a dedicated skill, curating public-domain case law and liability data, and wiring it into the resource-intelligence and session-start pipelines.\\n\\n### What\\n\\n- Create `.claude/skills/domains/maritime-law/SKILL.md` covering: jurisdiction (UNCLOS, flag-state, port-state), liability regimes (CLC 1992, Bunker Convention 2001, HNS Convention, Athens Convention), standard forms (B/L, charter-party, P&I club), and dispute resolution (Lloyd's, LMAA, SCMA).\\n- Curate a `knowledge/seeds/maritime-law-cases.yaml` file with \\u226510 landmark public cases (e.g. The MSC Flaminia, Prestige, Erika, MV Wakashio, Ever Given) including: case name, year, jurisdiction, key finding, liability outcome, and source URL (public record).\\n- Add `knowledge/seeds/maritime-liabilities.yaml` covering standard liability caps, conventions, and indemnity chains (ship-owner \\u2192 P&I club \\u2192 cargo interests \\u2192 reinsurer).\\n- Index both YAML seeds into the knowledge base via `scripts/knowledge/build-knowledge-index.sh`.\\n- Add a `maritime-law` entry to `config/ai_agents/ai-tools-status.yaml` domain registry (if one exists) or equivalent config.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nThe workspace handles offshore engineering assets (OrcaFlex, ANSYS, CFD). Maritime law governs liability, insurance, and regulatory compliance for offshore structures and vessels. Having machine-readable case law and liability conventions allows agents to answer regulatory questions and flag compliance risks in WRK items.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/33\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/32\", \"title\": \"feat: career-learnings seed migration \\u2014 pipeline integrity, OrcaFlex VIV, FEA, CFD, energy economics\", \"issue_number\": 32, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMigrate career-learnings YAML seed into appropriate wiki domains.\\n\\n## Entries (11 total)\\n\\n| # | Title | Category | Target |\\n|---|-------|----------|--------|\\n| 1 | Pipeline integrity (DNV RP-F101, API 579) | Engineering | marine-engineering |\\n| 2 | OrcaFlex VIV analysis | Engineering | marine-engineering |\\n| 3 | FEA structural analysis | Engineering | marine-engineering |\\n| 4 | CFD for offshore | Engineering | marine-engineering |\\n| 5 | Cathodic protection design | Engineering | marine-engineering (already exists!) |\\n| 6 | Energy economics (NPV, field dev) | Engineering | marine-engineering |\\n| 7 | AI in DWOP | Drilling | marine-engineering |\\n| 8 | Real estate analysis | Finance | personal wiki |\\n| 9 | Shell scripting patterns | Software | personal wiki |\\n| 10 | Python type safety | Software | personal wiki |\\n| 11 | JSONL knowledge stores | Software | wiki-patterns |\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\n1. Create entity pages for pipeline integrity, VIV, FEA, CFD in marine-engineering\\n2. Update cross-references to existing concepts (cathodic-protection already exists)\\n3. Create personal wiki for finance/software entries\\n4. Update index.md for any existing target Wiki\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] 6 engineering entries as new entities/concepts in marine-engineering wiki.\\n- [ ] Cross-references to existing pages verified.\\n- [ ] 4 software/finance entries migrated to personal wiki.\\n- [ ] index.md updated for all wikis.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/32\", \"display_title\": \"feat: career-learnings seed migration \\u2014 pipeline integrity, OrcaFlex VIV, FEA, CFD, energy economics\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/31\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): promote design-code registry into standards overviews and repo-target backlinks\", \"issue_number\": 31, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nPromote the design code registry into first-class LLM-wiki strengthening outputs: standards-family overview pages, edition-awareness cross-links, and repo-target backlinks that connect standards knowledge to downstream engineering repos.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe repo already has a high-signal design-code registry, but it is not being used as a wiki-strengthening surface:\\n- `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml` tracks ~30 engineering codes with edition status, disciplines, and `repos` mappings.\\n- `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md` explicitly says the design code registry is only partially discoverable and is not referenced from engineering wiki or standards wiki pages.\\n- Existing wiki work is mostly source-document and standards-ledger oriented; the code registry is the repo ecosystem's curated view of which standards matter to which downstream repos.\\n\\nThis means the wiki layer is missing a compact, navigable bridge from standards knowledge -> edition status -> repo applicability.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Review `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml` as a promotion source for L3 wiki strengthening.\\n- Define standards-family overview pages or updates that summarize code families already tracked in the registry (DNV, API, ISO, ASME/BSI/ASME as applicable).\\n- Add repo-target backlinks so wiki pages can point to the downstream repos named in the registry (for example `digitalmodel`, `doris`).\\n- Surface edition-status signals (`current`, `check`, `superseded`) in a wiki-friendly way without duplicating the registry as a second source of truth.\\n- Recommend how this promotion should interact with existing standard-specific pages like DNV/API/OCIMF pages.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- A promotion design/report mapping code-registry entries to target wiki pages.\\n- Proposed family-overview pages and/or updates to existing standards pages.\\n- Repo-target backlink convention grounded in the registry `repos` field.\\n- Guidance for keeping registry truth in L2 while exposing useful summaries in L3.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] code-registry entries are mapped to concrete wiki targets or explicit deferrals\\n- [ ] repo-target backlinks are proposed using existing `repos` metadata\\n- [ ] edition-awareness is surfaced without making the wiki the source of truth for edition tracking\\n- [ ] overlap with current standard pages is handled by extend-vs-create guidance\\n- [ ] resulting artifact improves discoverability of the design code registry from the wiki layer\\n\\n## Related\\n- Design code registry: `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml`\\n- Capabilities summary: `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_CAPABILITIES_SUMMARY.md`\\n- Accessibility map: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2096 / `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md`\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Existing wiki standard promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/31\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): promote design-code registry into standards overviews and repo-target backlinks\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/30\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): backfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages\", \"issue_number\": 30, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nBackfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages so older LLM-wiki content can answer what source artifact, issue, seed, or registry record it was promoted from.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that the policy stack now expects stronger provenance, but much of the existing wiki corpus predates that discipline:\\n- the provenance contract defines richer `doc_key`/promotion semantics\\n- new work is adding `doc_key` and `wiki_refs` capabilities (#2363, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362)\\n- older wiki pages and logs still often lack page-level promotion lineage, which weakens maintenance and reuse\\n\\nWithout provenance backfill, older pages remain hard to audit when source docs, issues, or registries change.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Inventory pre-existing wiki pages across current domains that lack strong promotion provenance.\\n- Define bounded backfill rules by source class (issues, seeds, skills, registry-backed sources, research outputs).\\n- Add page-level promotion references where deterministic evidence exists.\\n- Emit an explicit ambiguity report for pages that cannot be backfilled safely.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Provenance-backfill inventory and strategy.\\n- Backfilled promotion lineage for deterministic cases.\\n- Ambiguity/no-safe-backfill report for the rest.\\n- Guidance for how this interacts with doc_key and reverse-lookup work.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] legacy wiki pages are classified into deterministic backfill vs ambiguous buckets\\n- [ ] deterministic cases gain promotion provenance without hallucinated lineage\\n- [ ] ambiguous cases are reported explicitly rather than silently guessed\\n- [ ] resulting output improves future doc_key/wiki_refs maintenance work\\n\\n## Related\\n- Parent operating model: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n- Wiki reverse lookup: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\\n- L3 frontmatter/doc_key follow-ons: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2233, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\\n- Closed-issue citation guardrail: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2238\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/30\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): backfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/29\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): add canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages\", \"issue_number\": 29, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages so filename-only and numeric source pages become discoverable by human-readable titles, citation aliases, and stable search labels.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found a large live navigation problem in the source layer of the wiki corpus:\\n- `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/sources/` currently contains 19,159 source pages.\\n- 19,137 of those pages use filename-style titles like `spe143317.pdf`.\\n- 1,458 use purely numeric titles like `22035.pdf`.\\n- Sample source pages confirm this title pattern in frontmatter.\\n\\nThis makes the source corpus technically present but practically hard to navigate. Source pages should be discoverable by canonical title and common citation alias, not only by opaque filenames.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Start with the marine-engineering wiki source corpus.\\n- Derive `canonical_title` / `title_aliases` / equivalent display metadata from existing L2 evidence where available (conference metadata, summaries, registry titles, extracted titles).\\n- Keep raw filename as one preserved alias, not the primary display label when better metadata exists.\\n- Update index/search generation to prefer human-readable titles while preserving stable links.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Source-title aliasing strategy for wiki source pages.\\n- Backfill pass for marine-engineering source pages with deterministic alias/title evidence.\\n- Updated source/index generation rules so filename-only rows are no longer the default display surface.\\n- Explicit ambiguity report for pages that cannot be safely renamed/labeled from existing evidence.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] source pages can be discovered by canonical title or known alias rather than only raw filename\\n- [ ] numeric/filename-only source titles are reduced wherever deterministic metadata exists\\n- [ ] raw filenames are preserved as aliases for stability\\n- [ ] wiki index/search surfaces prefer readable titles without breaking links\\n\\n## Related\\n- Wiki reverse lookup: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\\n- Faceted portals for large domains: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\\n- Conference-summary promotion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369\\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/29\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): add canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/28\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): chunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index\", \"issue_number\": 28, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nChunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index so it remains authoritative but no longer forces users and agents through a single 21K-line navigation surface.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that the canonical index itself remains a major usability bottleneck even after portal and aliasing follow-ons:\\n- `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md` is 21,605 lines.\\n- Its frontmatter reports `page_count: 19181` and `source_count: 19159`.\\n- The domain currently has only a small number of entity/concept pages relative to source pages, so the canonical index is dominated by exhaustive source rows.\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 improves discovery through faceted portal pages, but explicitly does not replace the canonical index.\\n\\nThe repo still needs the authoritative index surface itself to be navigable and bounded.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Keep one canonical top-level `index.md` entry point for marine-engineering.\\n- Generate bounded chunk pages for oversized sections, especially Sources.\\n- Add stable section/range navigation (`next` / `prev` / jump links) without breaking current links.\\n- Make chunking reproducible/scripted rather than hand-maintained.\\n- Define a reusable chunking policy that can later apply to other oversized wiki indexes.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Canonical-index chunking/pagination design.\\n- Generated source/section sub-indexes for marine-engineering.\\n- Stable navigation model between top-level index and chunk pages.\\n- Chunking policy documentation for future large domains.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] marine-engineering no longer requires reading one 21K-line index file for exhaustive navigation\\n- [ ] top-level index remains canonical and authoritative\\n- [ ] chunk pages are generated, not manually curated\\n- [ ] stable links/navigation exist across chunk pages and back to the top-level index\\n\\n## Related\\n- Faceted portal pages: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\\n- Source-title aliasing: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29\\n- Strengthening scorecard: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37\\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/28\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): chunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/27\", \"title\": \"docs(knowledge): add standard uplink/back-navigation block to wiki index pages\", \"issue_number\": 27, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd a small, consistent navigation block to every `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/index.md` so wiki index pages expose both an upward link into the intelligence ecosystem and local back-navigation to sibling wiki surfaces.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel-agent review confirmed this residual gap is still real in repo state:\\n- `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md` explicitly says the unified intelligence landing page exists, but wiki `index.md` files still have no upward link to the intelligence ecosystem.\\n- Live inspection of current wiki indexes shows they do not consistently link to:\\n  - `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\\n  - local `CLAUDE.md`\\n  - local `wiki/log.md`\\n  - local `wiki/overview.md` / portal page when present\\n- Current indexes act as downward-only content tables rather than full navigation entry points.\\n\\nThis is a lightweight cross-wiki navigation standard, distinct from portal generation or index pagination.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Define one reusable nav/uplink block convention for `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/index.md`.\\n- Include at minimum:\\n  - intelligence landing page: `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\\n  - local `CLAUDE.md`\\n  - local `log.md` when present\\n  - local `overview.md` and/or portal page when present\\n- Apply the convention across existing wiki domains, with graceful handling where a sibling surface does not yet exist.\\n- Keep scope focused on index-page navigation standardization only.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Standard wiki-index navigation block pattern.\\n- Updates to current wiki index pages to use that pattern.\\n- Minimal guidance for optional targets (`overview.md`, portal page, `log.md`) when absent.\\n- Optional lightweight lint/check so the block does not drift.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] every wiki `index.md` links upward to `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\\n- [ ] every wiki `index.md` links to its local `CLAUDE.md`\\n- [ ] wiki indexes link to `log.md` / `overview.md` / portal when those files exist\\n- [ ] the pattern is consistent across domains and does not depend on one-off formatting\\n- [ ] scope stays distinct from portal generation (#2368) and marine index pagination (#2378)\\n\\n## Related\\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\\n- Large-domain portal generation: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\\n- Marine index chunking/pagination: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#28\\n- Registry-backed explorer views: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379\\n- Durable/transient boundary context: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/27\", \"display_title\": \"docs(knowledge): add standard uplink/back-navigation block to wiki index pages\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/24\", \"title\": \"Phase 2: Promote CSA Z276.1-20 + Z276.18 into marine-engineering wiki/standards/\", \"issue_number\": 24, \"body\": \"Phase split off from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 to decouple CSA work from OCIMF Tandem.\\n\\nTargets:\\n- knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/standards/csa-z276-1-20.md\\n- knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/standards/csa-z276-18.md\\n\\nFrontmatter contract from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 and .claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md:\\n- code_id, publisher, revision are required unless vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 lands a documented alias.\\n\\nPrereqs:\\n1. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 codification merged to main: schema CLAUDE.md amendment, .gitignore re-include for marine wiki/standards/, and lint path coverage.\\n2. CSA OCR remediation: text_preview for both CSA artifacts is currently unusable/corrupted according to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 v5 plan evidence.\\n3. Per-code wiki routing decision remains marine-engineering vs naval-architecture per vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 sanction.\\n\\nThis issue does not block vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 closure. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 closes only when OCIMF Phase 1 Branch A lands on origin/main.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/24\", \"display_title\": \"Phase 2: Promote CSA Z276.1-20 + Z276.18 into marine-engineering wiki/standards/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/23\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): update wiki CLAUDE.md files to declare doc_key in L3 frontmatter required-set\", \"issue_number\": 23, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nParent vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 operating model Section 8.1 (amendment 2026-04-19, [comment](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2205#issuecomment-4277238819)) mandates a baseline floor of `{title, last_updated, doc_key}` as required fields in every wiki `CLAUDE.md` schema declaration. No wiki `CLAUDE.md` currently declares `doc_key` as required.\\n\\nThis blocks the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 conformance check from being enforced without day-one failures.\\n\\n## Current state (verified 2026-04-19)\\n\\n| Wiki | `CLAUDE.md` path | Current required-set | Missing from baseline floor |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| engineering | `knowledge/wikis/engineering/CLAUDE.md` | `{title, tags, added, last_updated}` | `doc_key` |\\n| maritime-law | `knowledge/wikis/maritime-law/CLAUDE.md` (if present) | uses `{domain, created, last_updated, page_count}` in index | `title`, `doc_key` |\\n| naval-architecture | `knowledge/wikis/naval-architecture/CLAUDE.md` (if present) | uses `{domain, created, last_updated, page_count}` in index | `title`, `doc_key` |\\n| _other wikis_ | per-wiki `CLAUDE.md` | varies | all must add `doc_key` |\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Audit every `knowledge/wikis/*/CLAUDE.md` file.\\n2. For each, update the required-set declaration to include all three baseline-floor fields: `title`, `last_updated`, `doc_key`.\\n3. Preserve domain-specific required fields already in place.\\n4. For wikis lacking a `CLAUDE.md`, decide whether to create one (likely yes for any wiki with governed L3 content).\\n5. Update existing L3 pages that lack `doc_key` \\u2014 either backfill from the registry or add a grace-period transition policy.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Changing the baseline floor itself (locked by parent Section 8.1).\\n- Implementing the FRONT-1 conformance check in code (separate issue under vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206).\\n- Per-child contract fields (#2207, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 own those).\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- Parent operating model: `docs/document-intelligence/llm-wiki-resource-doc-intelligence-operating-model.md` \\u00a78.1\\n- Parent amendment summary: [#2205 comment 4277238819](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2205#issuecomment-4277238819)\\n- Surfaced by: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207 residual vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 residual vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 residual R1 (all three 2026-04-19 revision runs)\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 (amendment is authoritative)\\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 check enforcement\\n- Related: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207 \\u00a76.3 (adds provenance fields on top of baseline), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 \\u00a710.1 (adds durability fields on top of baseline)\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Every `knowledge/wikis/*/CLAUDE.md` declares `title`, `last_updated`, `doc_key` as required.\\n- L3 pages across all wikis have `doc_key` set (via backfill or documented transition policy).\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 passes when run against the live wikis.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/23\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): update wiki CLAUDE.md files to declare doc_key in L3 frontmatter required-set\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/21\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): regenerate cross-links.md across 8 wikis after Tier C page additions\", \"issue_number\": 21, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nTier C added ~75 new wiki pages across 6 wikis (asset-management, naval-architecture, maritime-law, lng-projects, engineering riser, engineering pipeline). The auto-generated `wiki/cross-links.md` files and any faceted-portal pages (#2368 territory) are now stale and need a regeneration pass.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` (#2011) auto-generates per-wiki `cross-links.md` files showing inbound/outbound links across wikis. These files are not git-committed by Tier C agents \\u2014 they're meant to be refreshed by the script.\\n\\nSurfaced specifically by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2587 close-out: the planned `test_asset_management_appears_in_cross_links_md` was rewritten by the implementing agent because:\\n- `cross-links.md` is auto-generated, not hand-edited\\n- The agent's scope contract forbade editing files outside its wiki tree\\n- The test was replaced with a positive inbound-reference assertion on the new pages themselves\\n\\nThe result is that asset-management's `cross-links.md` doesn't yet exist, and the other 5 newly-populated wikis' `cross-links.md` files (where they exist) don't reflect the new pages.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Run `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` (or its current entry point \\u2014 verify before running) across all 8 wikis: marine-engineering, engineering, naval-architecture, engineering-standards, asset-management, maritime-law, lng-projects, acma-projects\\n2. Commit the regenerated `cross-links.md` files\\n3. Spot-check that the asset-management `cross-links.md` now exists and shows the inbound references from `risk-based-inspection.md`, `fitness-for-service.md`, `integrity-management-cycle.md` to the engineering wiki\\n4. (Optional, scope decision) If vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted-portal generation is wired up, run that too \\u2014 engineering wiki is now at 103 pages and is the largest target\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- 8 `cross-links.md` files refreshed and committed (or note if any wikis don't yet have one as a deliberate gap)\\n- Diff reviewable (~bounded by net new pages \\u00d7 link density)\\n- No test regressions \\u2014 `tests/knowledge/test_*` stay green\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Hand-editing `cross-links.md` files (they're auto-gen)\\n- Schema changes to the script\\n- Cross-link discovery improvements (#2044, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068 territory)\\n- Faceted-portal authoring (separate scope under vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2587 (closed) \\u2014 asset-management close-out flagged the gap\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 \\u2014 cross-link discovery infrastructure\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#35 \\u2014 engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 \\u2014 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 \\u2014 llm-wiki strengthening epic\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/21\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): regenerate cross-links.md across 8 wikis after Tier C page additions\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/20\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): backfill engineering-wiki reverse cross-links to Tier C riser/pipeline pages\", \"issue_number\": 20, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe 20 new engineering-wiki concept pages added in Tier C Batch C (#2597 risers + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 pipelines, commit `6d3483bc5`) have one-way cross-links to existing related pages but the inbound (reverse) links from those existing pages were intentionally deferred to avoid cross-agent races on shared files during the parallel-dispatch phase.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nBoth implementation agents (#2597, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602) flagged this in their close-out reports as a known deferral:\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2597 deferred the \\\"Related design pages\\\" pointer block on `concepts/viv-riser-fatigue.md`\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 deferred reverse pointer blocks on `concepts/pipeline-integrity-assessment.md` and `concepts/free-span-viv-fatigue.md`\\n\\nWithout the reverse links, navigation from existing established pages to the new specialized sub-domain pages requires the user to know the new pages exist. The cross-link discoverability layer (#2011, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#35) and the auto-generated `cross-links.md` (script `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py`) help, but human-curated reverse anchors on the established hub pages are higher-signal.\\n\\n## Scope (single-session implementation, ~30 min)\\n\\nAdd a `## Related design pages` block to each of:\\n\\n1. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/viv-riser-fatigue.md`\\n   - Link to all 10 `riser-*.md` pages (or the navigationally relevant subset: configurations, steel-catenary, top-tensioned, flexible, hybrid-tower, drilling-system, global-analysis-load-cases, soil-interaction)\\n\\n2. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/pipeline-integrity-assessment.md`\\n   - Link to relevant `pipeline-*.md` pages (lateral-buckling, upheaval-buckling, walking, soil-interaction, on-bottom-stability, route-selection, installation-methods, end-expansion-spool-design, trawl-impact-protection, coatings)\\n\\n3. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/free-span-viv-fatigue.md`\\n   - Link to `pipeline-on-bottom-stability.md`, `pipeline-soil-interaction.md`, `pipeline-route-selection.md`, `riser-soil-interaction.md` (the soil/seabed cluster)\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- 3 existing pages amended with `## Related design pages` block\\n- Each new link verified to resolve (the riser-*/pipeline-* targets exist on `main` per Batch C)\\n- `tests/knowledge/test_engineering_riser_expansion.py` and `test_engineering_pipeline_expansion.py` still pass (no new tests required \\u2014 the existing one-way `test_at_least_one_cross_link_to_existing_pipeline_page` already covers the inbound side)\\n- Optional: re-run `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` to refresh `engineering/wiki/cross-links.md`\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Editing other established pages (limit to the 3 named above)\\n- Adding reverse links into other wikis (Tier C agents stayed in single-wiki scope; cross-wiki backfill is vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 territory)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2597 (closed) \\u2014 riser dispatch close-out report flags deferral\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 (closed) \\u2014 pipeline dispatch close-out report flags deferral\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 \\u2014 llm-wiki strengthening epic\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#35 \\u2014 cross-link infrastructure\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/20\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): backfill engineering-wiki reverse cross-links to Tier C riser/pipeline pages\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/13","title":"epic(knowledge): llm-wiki strengthening roadmap and execution waves","issue_number":13,"body":"## Summary\nCreate an umbrella roadmap for the current llm-wiki strengthening program, grouping the recently created issues into execution waves with explicit dependencies, parallelization notes, and staging guidance.\n\n## Why\nThe repo now has a substantial llm-wiki improvement portfolio spanning provenance, governance, promotion waves, and navigation/discoverability. The next bottleneck is no longer idea discovery; it is execution sequencing.\n\nA dependency-aware roadmap is needed so the work does not start in the wrong order, duplicate effort, or force rework across related surfaces such as provenance fields, promotion audit trails, batch-pack execution, and wiki navigation.\n\n## Scope\n- Group the current llm-wiki issue set into execution waves.\n- Record hard prerequisites vs soft sequencing preferences.\n- Mark which issues can run safely in parallel in separate worktrees.\n- Highlight readiness mismatches and scope caveats discovered during recommendation review.\n- Keep this issue as a planning/steering umbrella only; do not absorb implementation work from child issues.\n\n## Current issue set in scope\n### Provenance / governance / data foundation\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363 wiki_refs reverse lookup\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 provenance backfill on pre-existing wiki pages\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2382 promotion audit-trail checker\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 GUARD-1 invented-layer detector\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 transient-promotion candidate queue\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 WRK completions normalization\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2381 handoff expiration metadata\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2384 recurring-run output pruner\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 source_doc_key threading through promotion pipeline\n\n### Promotion waves / content expansion\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 Batch Pack 1 API/standards-portal metadata promotion\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 Batch Pack 2 indexed conference-summary promotion\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2373 Batch Pack 4 non-ACMA standards-summary promotion\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 Batch Pack 3 Tier A external engineering software profiles\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 design-code registry promotion\n\n### Navigation / discoverability\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 strengthening scorecard\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 large-domain portal pages\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29 source-title aliasing\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2378 canonical marine-engineering index chunking/pagination\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379 registry/task explorer\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#27 wiki index uplink/back-navigation standard\n\n## Recommended execution waves\n### Wave 0 — external prerequisites / schema authority\nThese are prerequisite context or adjacent issues that shape later work:\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 update wiki CLAUDE.md files to require doc_key\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2233 promoted_from frontmatter guidance\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362 back-populate doc_key on pre-existing standards-transfer-ledger entries\n\n### Wave 1 — low-risk provenance and guardrail foundations\nCan largely run in parallel in separate worktrees:\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 GUARD-1 invented-layer detector\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 source_doc_key threading through promotion pipeline\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363 wiki_refs reverse lookup (best after vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23; stronger after vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362)\n\n### Wave 2 — legacy provenance repair and transient metadata substrate\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 provenance backfill on pre-existing wiki pages\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2381 computable expiration metadata on session handoffs\n\n### Wave 3 — transient intake and candidate extraction\nCan run in parallel after Wave 2 metadata is stable:\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 transient-promotion candidate queue\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 WRK completions normalization\n\n### Wave 4 — governance enforcement / cleanup on top of the new substrate\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2382 promotion audit-trail checker\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2384 promotion-aware recurring-run output pruner\n\n### Wave 5 — first promotion-family execution\nCan run in parallel in separate worktrees:\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 Batch Pack 1 API/standards-portal metadata promotion\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 design-code registry promotion\n\n### Wave 6 — next promotion-family execution\nCan run in parallel, but note readiness caveat on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369:\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 Batch Pack 3 Tier A external engineering software profiles\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 Batch Pack 2 indexed conference-summary promotion\n\nReadiness note:\n- review found a live scope mismatch for vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369: the issue body names DOT/OMAE/ISOPE as phase-A-complete starter collections, but repo data indicated DOT/OMAE/OTC are phase-A complete while ISOPE is not yet indexed. This should be reconciled before execution.\n\n### Wave 7 — broader standards-summary promotion\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2373 Batch Pack 4 non-ACMA standards-summary promotion\n\n### Wave 8 — navigation/discoverability improvements after content/provenance progress\nRecommended sequence:\n1. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29 source-title aliasing\n2. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 strengthening scorecard (can overlap with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29)\n3. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 large-domain portal pages and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379 registry/task explorer in parallel\n4. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2378 canonical marine-engineering index chunking/pagination\n5. vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#27 wiki index uplink/back-navigation standard\n\n## Parallelization rules\n- Separate worktrees are required for concurrent implementation waves touching shared docs/wiki/report surfaces.\n- Good parallel bundles:\n  - Wave 1: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2383 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\n  - Wave 3: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374 + vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38\n  - Wave 5: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25 + vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n  - Wave 6: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2380 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 (after vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369 readiness fix)\n  - Wave 8 mid-phase: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379\n\n## Deliverables\n- Canonical roadmap/dependency graph for the llm-wiki strengthening program.\n- Child-issue grouping by wave.\n- Explicit notes on hard vs soft dependencies.\n- Parallelization guidance for future execution planning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] current llm-wiki strengthening issues are grouped into waves with rationale\n- [ ] hard and soft dependencies are called out explicitly\n- [ ] known readiness mismatches are recorded in the roadmap\n- [ ] roadmap remains a planning/steering umbrella rather than absorbing child implementation scope\n\n## Related\n- Parent operating model: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Durable/transient boundary: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\n- Priority queue + batch-pack design: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n\n## Work Stream G: Tier-1 repo ecosystem routing + retrieval surfaces (Priority 1.5)\n*Make the durable knowledge layer actually usable across the repo portfolio, not just inside workspace-hub wiki artifacts*\n\nThis roadmap originally focused on wiki/provenance/promotion internals. A portfolio review on 2026-04-22 found an adjacent bottleneck: even when knowledge exists, workers still lack consistent per-repo routing surfaces for where code/docs/tests should live and how future issue work should retrieve canonical targets. That gap weakens llm-wiki compounding value because promoted knowledge cannot land cleanly in downstream repos.\n\n| Issue | Title | Function |\n|-------|-------|----------|\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 | Tier-1 indexing and code-placement contract | portfolio-wide routing contract |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461 | assetutilities routing surfaces and source-hygiene cleanup | highest-risk repo remediation |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462 | digitalmodel repo-wide operator map and canonical routing surfaces | engineering-core remediation |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463 | aceengineer-website canonical routing surfaces cleanup | GTM/externalization remediation |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464 | workspace-hub curated routing index + routing-noise cleanup | control-plane remediation |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465 | daily tier-1 indexing freshness audit | ongoing governance loop |\n\nRecommended sequence:\n1. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 defines the shared contract.\n2. Execute repo remediations in this order: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463 -> vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464.\n3. Keep vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465 as the sustaining daily audit/scorecard loop.\n\nWhy this belongs in the llm-wiki roadmap:\n- llm-wiki is the durable cross-repo knowledge layer in the repo ecosystem model.\n- repo-specific routing/index surfaces are the landing pads that convert knowledge into correct repo-level execution.\n- without these repo surfaces, agents still rediscover placement and retrieval paths, reducing the return on wiki promotion work.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/13","display_title":"epic(knowledge): llm-wiki strengthening roadmap and execution waves"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40","title":"Research: reservoir engineering literature — local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki","issue_number":40,"body":"## Goal\n\nBuild out the reservoir-engineering substrate of llm-wiki by mining (a) the user's existing local PDF corpus on ace-linux-1 (`/mnt/ace`, 30,499 PDFs) and (b) public online sources, then ingesting the relevant material under llm-wiki's MIT + CC-BY-4.0 license. Drives both the [Kaggle ROGII Wellbore Geology Prediction](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026) competition (deeper domain literacy → better modeling decisions) and longer-term wikis around oil & gas / subsurface engineering.\n\nCompanion issue: [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) covers competition-specific *prior art* (datasets + ML papers); this issue covers the broader *educational foundation* (textbooks, coursework, classic papers).\n\n## Scope\n\n**In-scope source types**\n\n- Textbooks on reservoir engineering, petroleum engineering, formation evaluation, well logging, drilling, geosteering.\n- University coursework — open syllabi, lecture notes, problem sets from Stanford SDSS, Texas A&M, U Texas Austin, Heriot-Watt, IFP, Imperial.\n- Conference papers — SPE, AAPG, SEG, EAGE — with care about open-access vs paywalled.\n- Industry standards / methodology PDFs (DNV, API, ISO).\n- Theses and dissertations from public university repositories.\n- ArXiv preprints in petroleum engineering, geophysics, ML-for-geosteering categories.\n\n**Out of scope (license / IP risk)**\n\n- Pirated or unauthorized copies of paywalled textbooks, even if found locally.\n- Vendor-derivative material under proprietary license.\n- The deny-list per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482) governance: nothing under `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/sources/` should be cited; cite the canonical standard or concept page instead.\n\n## Sources to mine\n\n### Local — `/mnt/ace` (ace-linux-1)\n\n- `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` — top candidate directory by name. First pass: recursively list, classify by filename / metadata, flag candidates.\n- `/mnt/ace/aceengineer-admin/Reference/` — mixed (mostly tax / admin docs in spot-check, but may contain technical references).\n- Other dirs revealed during initial sweep.\n- Total PDFs in `/mnt/ace`: ~30,499. Realistic target: 50–200 ingest-worthy after deduplication and license filtering.\n\n### Online (representative starting points)\n\n- **Stanford Stanford Doerr School OCW**: open courses on petroleum / energy resources.\n- **Texas A&M PETE OCW** and **U Texas Austin Petroleum Engineering** open content.\n- **Heriot-Watt PE** open materials.\n- **arXiv physics.geo-ph** and **stat.ML** intersection — search \"well log\", \"geosteering\", \"lithology classification\".\n- **OnePetro** free-access entries (SPE / AAPG / SEG; many old papers are now open).\n- **AAPG Datapages** open-access portion.\n- **USGS Open-File Reports** in petroleum geology.\n- **OAPEN** and **Springer Open** for free textbooks.\n- **MIT OpenCourseWare** earth-and-planetary courses with subsurface relevance.\n\n## Output: llm-wiki structure\n\nExisting top-level dirs (verified 2026-05-06): `docs/`, `scripts/`, `seeds/`, `tests/`, `wikis/`.\n\nProposed additions / extensions (subject to existing wiki conventions; defer final layout to whoever owns llm-wiki structure decisions):\n\n- `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` (new, if not present) with:\n  - `concepts/` — fundamentals: porosity, permeability, saturation, capillary pressure, relative permeability, etc.\n  - `methodology/` — geosteering workflow, reservoir characterization, log interpretation, formation evaluation.\n  - `standards/` — DNV / API / ISO references with [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)-shape frontmatter (`code_id`, `publisher`, `revision`).\n  - `sources/` — citation index, NOT ingestion targets per [vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2482](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2482).\n- `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` — log of every source examined, decision (ingest / skip / defer), license note.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Local sweep.** Inventory `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` and other candidate dirs. Output: a manifest of `(filepath, size, page-count, title-from-metadata, classification)` rows. ~1 hr scripted.\n2. **Online sweep.** 6–10 best-of-class courses, textbooks (open-access only), and survey papers. Bookmark + brief description. ~1–2 hr.\n3. **License triage.** Drop everything that's not clearly redistributable. Prefer creative-commons or public-domain (older works > 70 yrs).\n4. **Wiki page drafts.** Write 5–15 concept pages (`wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/*.md`) in llm-wiki's existing style. Cite sources, never copy. Apply the calc-citation contract (`workspace-hub/.claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md`) where formulas appear.\n5. **PR with the corpus + wiki pages + citation log.** Reviewer checks license, citation, and that copy is original (not paraphrased > 30-word chunks).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `/mnt/ace` reservoir-engineering inventory at `docs/research/reservoir-engineering-corpus.md` lists at least 50 candidate sources with classification (ingest / skip / defer) and license note.\n- [ ] At least 5 concept pages drafted under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/concepts/` covering core fundamentals (porosity, permeability, gamma-ray log interpretation, dip / azimuth, formation tops).\n- [ ] At least 2 methodology pages under `wikis/reservoir-engineering/methodology/` covering geosteering workflow + log correlation.\n- [ ] All cited sources licensed for redistribution OR cited only as reference (no in-page copying).\n- [ ] PR opened, reviewed, merged with the standard llm-wiki review process.\n- [ ] Cross-link added to [vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026#5](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/kaggle-rogii-2026/issues/5) when the wiki pages are ready, so Kaggle modeling work can reference them.\n\n## Risks and open questions\n\n- **Risk:** `/mnt/ace/rock-oil-field/` may contain user-purchased textbooks not licensed for redistribution. Triage carefully — local-use-only OK, ingestion-to-public-repo NOT OK.\n- **Open:** Should reservoir-engineering wiki pages live under a top-level `wikis/reservoir-engineering/` or inside the existing marine/offshore family? Defer to llm-wiki maintainer decision.\n- **Open:** What citation style — IEEE-numeric, APA, or the inline `code_id` style from [#2471](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2471)? Likely match the existing llm-wiki convention.\n\n## Time budget\n\nA few sessions across 1–2 weeks. Don't disappear into a literature rabbit hole; the 50-source target keeps it bounded.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/40","display_title":"Research: reservoir engineering literature — local /mnt/ace + online; ingest to llm-wiki"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion","issue_number":26,"body":"## Summary\nExecute Batch Pack 4 as a narrowly scoped, summary-backed promotion wave for non-ACMA standards knowledge in cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that this is the strongest remaining designed batch-pack opportunity:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` and the YAML queue rank standards-with-existing-summaries as the next major promotion family.\n- `data/document-index/resource-intelligence-maturity.yaml` reports 639,585 existing summaries and 425 standards in active maturity scope.\n- This work can promote existing L2 evidence into L3 wiki knowledge without rereading source PDFs.\n\nThe key is to scope it carefully so it complements, rather than duplicates, ACMA/OCIMF/CSA or design-code-registry work.\n\n## Scope\n- Use only existing summary-backed and ledger-backed evidence.\n- Start with non-ACMA domains/sub-slices: cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural.\n- Generate topic/domain stubs and cross-links from existing summary + ledger data.\n- Explicitly exclude:\n  - ACMA/naval-architecture/OCIMF/CSA-specific promotion already covered by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n  - design-code-registry family overviews/backlinks covered by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n  - raw source-PDF rereads\n\n## Deliverables\n- Batch Pack 4 execution artifact/report for the chosen non-ACMA domains.\n- Summary-backed wiki-ready topic/domain stubs.\n- Duplicate/extend-vs-create map against existing standards/wiki pages.\n- Provenance references back to the transfer ledger and summary sources.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] promotion uses existing summary/ledger evidence only\n- [ ] first slice is limited to cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural domains\n- [ ] ACMA/design-code-registry scope is explicitly excluded to avoid duplication\n- [ ] outputs include extend-vs-create and provenance mapping, not raw dump notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Engineering wiki ingest umbrella: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Design-code registry promotion: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31\n- ACMA/standards promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2284\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/26","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 4 for non-ACMA standards summary promotion"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48","title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs","issue_number":48,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #26 Batch Pack 4 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #26\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #26: plan branch `plan/issue-2373-batch-pack-4` at approved SHA `c516ec853`.\n- Upstream gate `vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471` is now closed, but the public spinout repo still lacks the approval-bound plan artifact and required data inputs.\n\n## Scope\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 4 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 4\n- transfer ledger input required for the cathodic-protection, pipeline, and structural standards slice\n- topic-cluster and alias inputs required by the approved plan\n- any approved summary-backed evidence surface required to avoid raw PDF rereads\n- provenance notes binding restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\n- validation checklist for duplicate/extend-vs-create mapping, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw/vendor boundaries\n\n## Out of scope\n- No Batch Pack 4 promotion execution in this prep issue.\n- No ledger/cluster reconstruction from memory.\n- No raw PDF rereads, source extraction, OCR, or standards text summarization.\n- No standards wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\n- No credentials, private source text, vendor standards text, formulas, tables, or copied clauses in the public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 4 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\n- [ ] Required transfer ledger, topic-cluster, and alias inputs are available in a public-safe form.\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\n- [ ] Future #26 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\n- [ ] #26 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\n\n## Related\n- #26\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/48","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 4 approved execution inputs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains","issue_number":25,"body":"## Summary\nExecute the already-designed external-source Batch Pack 1 so the repo promotes metadata-rich online data APIs and standards portals into wiki-ready stubs for the thin LLM-wiki domains.\n\n## Why\nThe repo ecosystem review showed a strong imbalance:\n- engineering wiki: 83 pages\n- naval-architecture wiki: 45 pages\n- maritime-law wiki: 22 pages\n- marine-engineering wiki: 19,184 pages\n\nAt the same time, the repo already has a prepared execution design:\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-external-source-priority-queue.md` identifies \"Online Data APIs & Standards Portals\" as P1 / high-ROI / promotable now.\n- `docs/reports/llm-wiki-staged-batch-packs.md` defines Batch Pack 1 as a bounded, overnight-safe metadata-first sweep of 40 entries from `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml`.\n- The review explicitly says these entries already have enough structured notes that wiki strengthening can happen without source re-download.\n\nThis is low-friction wiki expansion work that uses existing registry intelligence instead of re-parsing raw sources.\n\n## Scope\n- Execute Batch Pack 1 from the existing priority-queue and staged-pack artifacts.\n- Filter `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` for `type in [data_api, standard_portal]`.\n- Group entries by target wiki domain.\n- Produce wiki-ready metadata stubs and a report showing where each source should promote.\n- Identify entries that are insufficiently documented and split them into follow-on issues rather than silently expanding scope.\n\n## Deliverables\n- A concrete execution artifact/report for the 40 API/portal entries.\n- Wiki-ready stubs grouped by engineering, marine-engineering, and naval-architecture target domains.\n- Duplicate check against existing wiki pages.\n- Follow-on issue map for entries that need extra download/auth work.\n- Cross-links to related wiki pages and registry entries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] all currently eligible API/portal entries are triaged through the batch-pack flow\n- [ ] each output stub has a clear target wiki domain and provenance reference\n- [ ] duplicate targets are identified before promotion\n- [ ] insufficient-note entries are explicitly split into follow-on work\n- [ ] the run produces a reusable report rather than one-off notes\n\n## Related\n- Priority queue: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2242\n- Staged batch packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2243\n- Download automation: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1609\n- Engineering wiki ingest: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#34\n- Research/ingest expansion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067\n- Cross-link follow-on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/25","display_title":"feat(knowledge): execute Batch Pack 1 to promote API/standards-portal metadata into thin wiki domains"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47","title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs","issue_number":47,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the exact approved execution inputs needed before #25 Batch Pack 1 can safely run in the public `llm-wiki` repo.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #25\n- Approved plan lineage recorded on #25: plan branch `plan/issue-2364-batch-pack-1` at approved SHA `7cc1c0b1a`.\n- Current blocker: the public spinout repo does not contain the approval-bound plan artifact or the required online-resource registry inputs.\n\n## Scope\nRestore or expose the approved Batch Pack 1 execution surfaces in a public-safe way:\n- approval-bound plan artifact for Batch Pack 1\n- `data/document-index/online-resource-registry.yaml` or an approved public-safe extracted subset sufficient for Batch Pack 1\n- any overlay/processed input required by the approved plan\n- provenance notes binding the restored inputs to the approved plan SHA or documenting a new user-approved replacement\n- validation checklist for duplicate checks, generated report/stub paths, and public/raw boundaries\n\n## Out of scope\n- No Batch Pack 1 promotion execution in this prep issue.\n- No registry reconstruction from memory.\n- No source re-download or raw source parsing.\n- No API/portal wiki stubs until the approved inputs are restored and verified.\n- No credentials, API keys, private endpoints, private source text, or vendor text in the public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The approval-bound Batch Pack 1 plan artifact is available or a replacement is explicitly user-approved.\n- [ ] The required registry input or approved subset is available in a public-safe form.\n- [ ] Input provenance is documented with approved SHA/source and drift checks.\n- [ ] Future #25 execution commands and validation checks are specified.\n- [ ] #25 is updated with a link to this prep issue and remains blocked until inputs are ready.\n\n## Related\n- #25\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/47","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): restore Batch Pack 1 approved execution inputs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data","issue_number":19,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data\n\n## Context\nMetadata-only discovery of `/mnt/ace-data` raw-like stores identified several high-value offshore/energy source families that are not directly covered by existing llm-wiki completion plans:\n\n- `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` — 10 files (PDF/XLSX/DOCX/ZIP), BSEE/offshore well data descriptions and sample permit/activity material.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` — 97 files / 7 dirs, OSHA/HSE CSV/TXT/ZIP datasets and metadata.\n- `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` — 4 files / 1 dir, offshore magazine/heavy-lift/pipelay source material.\n\nFocused duplicate searches found no direct open issue for `energy_bsee raw_data`, `worldenergydata hse llm-wiki`, or `frontierdeepwater llm-wiki`. Existing adjacent anchors remain vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 (roadmap), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 (coverage-gap detector), and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 (raw-data-to-readiness spine).\n\n## Problem\nThese offshore/energy raw-source families may contain useful llm-wiki completion signals for engineering, marine-engineering, HSE/safety, drilling, production, and offshore operations domains, but they must be handled carefully:\n\n- only metadata and derived summaries may be promoted;\n- client/project-sensitive files require separate approval;\n- raw data and proprietary files must remain mounted-source only;\n- source-family package boundaries must be approved before any extraction/backfill work.\n\n## Scope\nCreate an approval-ready canonical plan that defines bounded source-family packages for:\n1. BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates,\n2. HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates, and\n3. Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates.\n\nThe plan should produce a safe, reviewable execution route after approval, including target wiki domains, expected summary/page types, exclusions, tests/checks, and provenance gates.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data copying into git/wiki.\n- No direct extraction from client-sensitive files without separate approval.\n- No website/GTM artifact generation.\n- No AQWA/OrcaFlex/O&G standards work here; those map to existing issues (#2103, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards waves) or the raw-like routing issue.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan includes a source-family matrix with BSEE, HSE, and Frontier Deepwater candidates, target wiki domains, exclusion rules, provenance requirements, and follow-up package sequencing.\n- [ ] The plan cites metadata-only inventory evidence and focused duplicate-search evidence showing no direct duplicate issue for these three families.\n- [ ] The plan defines approval gates for any raw/project-sensitive material before summary promotion.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/19","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan offshore raw-source family wiki backfill candidates from /mnt/ace-data"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":46,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations source candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for Frontier Deepwater/offshore operations material:\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\n- handling rules for magazine/offshore-operation articles, heavy-lift/pipelay source material, images, PDFs, and archives\n- allowed public bibliographic metadata and authored high-level synthesis\n- disallowed copied article text, figures, vendor/private material, and raw archive contents\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` content into git.\n- No OCR, article summarization from raw files, figure extraction, archive extraction, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No copyrighted article text, images, credentials, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored synthesis, copyrighted article text, images/figures, archives, and vendor/private material.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor/copyright boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/46","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare Frontier Deepwater source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":45,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any HSE/safety dataset metadata or wiki promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: HSE/safety dataset metadata and wiki concept/source candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until dataset clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for HSE/safety dataset material:\n- dataset-level clearance fields required before promotion\n- allowed public metadata fields, dataset citations, and aggregate descriptions\n- disallowed personally identifiable information, incident-sensitive records, raw CSV/TXT rows, and proprietary/private derived data\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules for HSE concepts and source metadata\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/PII/secret scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw dataset extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` content into git.\n- No CSV/TXT row promotion, ZIP extraction, incident-record summarization, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No PII, private source text, credentials, or raw safety data in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate dataset/artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, aggregate public synthesis, raw rows, PII/sensitive incident records, archives, and derived summaries.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/PII boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/45","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare HSE dataset source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist","issue_number":44,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any BSEE/offshore source-family promotion can proceed from #19.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #19\n- Source family: BSEE/offshore source metadata and summary candidates\n- Current status: promotion remains blocked until source-family clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist for BSEE/offshore candidate material:\n- artifact-level clearance fields required before any source is summarized\n- handling rules for client/project-sensitive files, permit/activity samples, spreadsheets, document archives, and data descriptions\n- allowed public metadata fields versus disallowed extracted content\n- target wiki domain/page-type decision rules\n- required approval gates before any future implementation issue\n- validation expectations for raw/private/vendor/client-sensitive boundary scans\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` content into git.\n- No OCR, table extraction, workbook extraction, PDF/DOCX summarization, ZIP inspection for promotion, or direct wiki stub generation.\n- No client/project-sensitive files, credentials, permit details, private source text, or proprietary material in this public repo.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, client/project-sensitive data, proprietary/project material, archives, and authored synthesis.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/client-sensitive boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #19 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #19\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/44","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare BSEE source-family clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements","issue_number":14,"body":"## Summary\nPlan a bounded curated extraction pass for the SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa` corpus now represented metadata-first in the LLM-wikis.\n\n## Source of record\n- Raw corpus: `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa`\n- Wiki domain: `lng-projects`\n- Existing metadata page from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535: bucket-level Elements source/catalog page in `knowledge/wikis/lng-projects/`\n- Candidate queue: `.planning/intel/elements-to-llm-wiki/deep-extraction-candidates.tsv`\n\n## Why\nThe SESA corpus is medium-sized compared with Woodfibre but rich in reusable LNG/subsea engineering artifacts: reference studies, DNV/API standards, free-span analysis, material specs/datasheets, valve TBE files, logistics descriptions, and deliverables. It should be triaged into high-value extraction targets before any text extraction is run.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope:\n- Build a candidate dossier for SESA files grouped by engineering theme and document family.\n- Identify a first extraction tranche of no more than 20 documents/workbooks.\n- Deduplicate obvious repeated revision/path variants where metadata is enough to decide.\n- Draft an approval-ready plan for a later bounded extraction implementation.\n\nOut of scope:\n- No broad extraction over all 418 files.\n- No raw files copied into git/wiki raw folders.\n- No source/staging cleanup.\n- No changes to `/mnt/ace` contents.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-issue-NNN-elements-sesa-curated-extraction-plan.md`\n- `.planning/intel/elements-overnight-wave/sesa-candidate-dossier.md`\n- Proposed first-tranche file list with paths, byte sizes, rationale, extraction method, and target wiki page(s).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Dossier covers at least these themes if present: reference studies, free-span/metocean, material specs/datasheets, subsea valves/TBE, logistics/project deliverables.\n- [ ] Proposed tranche is bounded to <=20 source artifacts.\n- [ ] Every proposed artifact has source path, rationale, extraction method, expected wiki target, and risk note.\n- [ ] Plan explicitly preserves raw-data policy and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2534 retention boundary.\n- [ ] Issue is left at plan-review, not self-approved.\n\n## Related\n- Umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540\n- Completed metadata indexing: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2535\n- Completed first-pass extraction: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2536\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/14","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan curated SESA LNG corpus extraction from Elements"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43","title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist","issue_number":43,"body":"## Summary\nPrepare the governance/clearance checklist required before any SESA LNG corpus extraction can proceed from #14.\n\n## Parent blocker\n- Parent issue: #14\n- Raw/source family: SESA FLNG Terminal / DORIS `62092_sesa`\n- Current status: extraction remains blocked until clearance artifacts and a separate bounded implementation lane exist.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a public-safe clearance checklist that defines what must exist before extraction starts:\n- row-level or artifact-level clearance fields required for any proposed first tranche\n- allowed source evidence types and disallowed source evidence types\n- public-repo output boundaries for summaries, metadata, and target wiki pages\n- required approvals for vendor, client/project-sensitive, archive, workbook, and standards-derived materials\n- validation expectations before any future extraction commit\n- required separate implementation issue structure after clearance is complete\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw file extraction.\n- No reading or copying `/mnt/ace/doris/62092_sesa` content into git.\n- No OCR, text extraction, table extraction, workbook extraction, or PDF summarization.\n- No vendor standards text, private archive material, credentials, client-sensitive content, or project specifications in this public repo.\n- No closing #14 until this checklist and a later bounded implementation lane are complete.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Checklist names required clearance fields for each candidate artifact.\n- [ ] Checklist distinguishes public metadata, authored public synthesis, vendor-derived text, client/project-sensitive files, archives, and standards material.\n- [ ] Checklist defines the future implementation issue template and approval gate.\n- [ ] Checklist states the raw/private/vendor boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] #14 is updated with a link to this checklist issue and remains blocked.\n\n## Related\n- #14","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/43","display_title":"governance(llm-wiki): prepare SESA extraction clearance checklist"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41","title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions","issue_number":41,"body":"## Summary\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the maritime-law wiki.\n\n## Decision source\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for IMO/ILO convention and code pages.\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\n\n## Scope\n- Plan and then implement a bounded metadata-only migration or mirror strategy for eligible maritime-law convention/code pages currently under `wikis/maritime-law/wiki/concepts/`.\n- Candidate pages include SOLAS, MARPOL, MLC, and ISM Code, subject to duplicate/path review.\n- Preserve `consolidated_edition` where that is the correct public metadata field.\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No convention/code text copying.\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, or source excerpts.\n- No broad maritime-law schema rewrite beyond the routing implementation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Eligible pages have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\n- Existing concept links are preserved or redirected/mirrored safely.\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\n\n## Related\n- #15\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/41","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement maritime-law standards routing for conventions"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42","title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing","issue_number":42,"body":"## Summary\nImplement the standards-routing decision from #15 for the LNG-projects wiki.\n\n## Decision source\n- #15 sanctions `wiki/standards/<code-id>.md` routing for LNG codes and standards pages.\n- Governance record: `docs/governance/deferred-wiki-standards-routing-decisions.md`.\n\n## Scope\n- Plan and then implement bounded metadata-only standards pages for LNG codes when public metadata is sufficient.\n- Candidate families include CSA-Z276, NFPA 59A, and IGC Code, subject to public metadata verification and duplicate/path review.\n- Update index/log/navigation surfaces.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No standard text copying.\n- No raw PDFs, private archives, vendor text, paywalled text, project specifications, or source excerpts.\n- No broad LNG content expansion beyond standards-routing implementation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Eligible LNG standards have a clear `wiki/standards/` routing plan before implementation.\n- Standards pages are metadata-only/public synthesis and carry required frontmatter.\n- Any insufficient public metadata is split into follow-up work instead of guessed.\n- Local markdown links and targeted raw/private/secret scans pass.\n\n## Related\n- #15\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/42","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): implement LNG-projects standards routing"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/39","title":"feat: engineering wiki — ingest skill metadata as wiki pages","issue_number":39,"body":"## Summary\nIngest the 691+ skill definitions from `.claude/skills/` into the engineering wiki as entity/concept pages.\n\n## Context\nThe engineering wiki SOURCE_INVENTORY.md lists skill metadata as a future source class. Each engineering skill (OrcaFlex, FEA, cathodic protection, API standards, etc.) contains structured knowledge that should compound into the wiki.\n\n## Approach\n- Scan `.claude/skills/` for engineering-relevant skills\n- Classify each as entity (tool/system) or concept (methodology/pattern)\n- Create wiki pages with frontmatter, cross-references to existing pages\n- Estimated yield: 50-100 additional wiki pages\n\n## Related\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (parent — engineering wiki seed)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2022 (skills → service pages for aceengineer.com)\n- SOURCE_INVENTORY.md \"Future Source Classes\" section","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/39","display_title":"feat: engineering wiki — ingest skill metadata as wiki pages"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/38","title":"feat(knowledge): normalize WRK completions into structured seeds and wiki-candidate corpus","issue_number":38,"body":"## Summary\nNormalize `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` into structured seeds and a wiki-candidate corpus, so archived work completions become queryable durable knowledge instead of raw memory-migration blobs.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that the WRK completion corpus still exists primarily as raw JSONL:\n- `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` contains the migrated corpus, but records are still raw-string oriented.\n- the knowledge-persistence architecture explicitly proposed a structured `knowledge/seeds/wrk-completions.yaml` target and follow-on hook work.\n- current repo state still does not expose a normalized WRK seed surface for durable wiki promotion.\n\nThis is a strong tacit-knowledge opportunity because the repo already has the corpus; what is missing is structure and promotion-readiness.\n\n## Scope\n- Parse existing `knowledge-base/wrk-completions.jsonl` into a normalized structured seed surface.\n- Add fields such as category, subcategory, title, completed_at, artifacts, tests, reusable patterns, follow-ons, related docs, and GitHub issue references where recoverable.\n- Produce a second-stage wiki-candidate projection for reusable domain/process learnings.\n- Frame this as a follow-on to existing archive/backfill work rather than a duplicate of it.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Structured WRK completion seed artifact(s).\n- Mapping/report from raw WRK completions -> normalized entries.\n- Wiki-candidate projection/report for durable promotion opportunities.\n- Guidance for future append/update flow so new completions do not remain raw-only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] raw WRK completion records are normalized into structured fields where evidence exists\n- [ ] a durable seed/corpus replaces raw-only querying for this knowledge surface\n- [ ] output includes wiki-candidate routing rather than only archival normalization\n- [ ] scope is positioned as a follow-on to archive/backfill work, not a duplicate of it\n\n## Related\n- Archive synthesis + knowledge backfill: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#103\n- Knowledge-persistence architecture / closed predecessor: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#894\n- Transient-promotion queue: companion issue\n- Closed-issue promotion ledger: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2370\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/38","display_title":"feat(knowledge): normalize WRK completions into structured seeds and wiki-candidate corpus"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/36","title":"feat: cross-wiki link discovery and infrastructure","issue_number":36,"body":"## Summary\n\nBuild tooling to discover and maintain cross-links between the 3 domain wikis (marine-engineering, maritime-law, naval-architecture).\n\n## Problem\n\nWikis are currently siloed. Real engineering topics span domains:\n- Deepwater Horizon → engineering (engineering) + law (OPA 90)  \n- Mooring failures → marine-eng + naval-arch stability analysis\n- Classification society rules → naval-arch + maritime-law liability\n\n## Proposed: Cross-Wiki Link Index\n\n```\nknowledge/wikis/cross-links.md\n```\n\n| Source Wiki | Entity/Concept | Target Wiki | Target Page | Link Type |\n|-------------|---------------|-------------|-------------|-----------|\n| maritime-law | Deepwater Horizon | marine-engineering | lng-carrier-mooring | related-case |\n| maritime-law | Amoco Cadiz | naval-architecture | ship-structures | hull-failure |\n\n## Tooling\n\n`llm-wiki cross-links --source wiki --target wiki` command:\n1. Scan source wiki for mentions of entities in target wiki\n2. Scan target wiki for mentions of source wiki entities\n3. Report candidate links\n4. Optionally create cross-wiki reference pages\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] cross-lines.md generated with at least 10 discovered links\n- [ ] `llm-wiki cross-links` CLI command\n- [ ] Existing wiki pages updated with cross-references\n\n## Related\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1995 (closed)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2000 (closed — seeds migrated)\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/36","display_title":"feat: cross-wiki link discovery and infrastructure"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/35","title":"feat: engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis","issue_number":35,"body":"## Summary\n\nRun cross-wiki link discovery between the engineering wiki and the 3 domain wikis (marine-engineering, maritime-law, naval-architecture) to surface implicit connections.\n\n## Context\n\nThe engineering wiki (#2034) has 52 pages with 111 cross-references, but links to domain wikis are minimal. Many concepts (VIV, mooring failures, cathodic protection, pipeline integrity) appear in both the engineering methodology wiki and the marine-engineering domain wiki. These implicit connections should be surfaced.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Run `llm-wiki cross-links` (from vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36) between engineering <-> marine-engineering\n2. Update engineering wiki pages with `[[wiki:marine-engineering/page]]` links where relevant\n3. Update domain wiki pages with `[[wiki:engineering/page]]` links back\n4. Generate `knowledge/wikis/cross-links.md` index of discovered connections\n\n## Expected High-Value Connections\n\n| Engineering Wiki Page | Domain Wiki Page | Link Type |\n|----------------------|-----------------|-----------|\n| VIV Riser Fatigue | marine-eng/mooring-line-failure | related-concept |\n| Cathodic Protection Design | marine-eng/cathodic-protection-system | methodology |\n| Pipeline Integrity Assessment | marine-eng/corrosion-control | assessment |\n| Solver Queue | marine-eng/lng-carrier-mooring | tool-usage |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Cross-link scan completed between engineering and all 3 domain wikis\n- [ ] At least 15 bidirectional cross-references discovered and added\n- [ ] `knowledge/wikis/cross-links.md` index created\n- [ ] Both engineering and domain wiki indexes updated\n\n## Related\n\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 (cross-wiki link discovery — parent issue)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (engineering wiki seed — completed)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/35","display_title":"feat: engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/34","title":"feat: engineering wiki — ingest remaining high-value sources (skills metadata, closed issues)","issue_number":34,"body":"## Summary\n\nExpand the engineering wiki with pages from the remaining high-value source classes identified but not yet ingested during the initial seed (#2034).\n\n## Source Classes to Ingest\n\n### Skills Metadata (`.claude/skills/`)\n- 691+ skills, each could become a wiki entity or concept page\n- Focus on engineering-specific skills first (orcaflex, fea, cathodic, mooring, etc.)\n- Extract: skill name, domain, key capabilities, dependencies\n- Target: 20-30 pages covering the most valuable skills\n\n### Closed Engineering GitHub Issues\n- Issues with labels `cat:engineering`, `cat:engineering-calculations`, `cat:engineering-methodology`\n- Extract: problem solved, approach taken, key decisions\n- Target: 10-15 pages from the most instructive closed issues\n\n### Mooring Failures Seed (`knowledge/seeds/mooring-failures-lng-terminals.yaml`)\n- 40 entries of real mooring failure incidents\n- Each entry could become an entity page or feed existing marine-engineering wiki\n- Cross-link to engineering wiki's VIV, mooring, and pipeline concepts\n\n### Overnight Batch Run Reports\n- Outputs from nightly researcher agents (`.planning/research/`)\n- Extract: key findings, domain insights, methodology patterns\n- Target: 5-10 pages from highest-value research outputs\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] At least 30 new pages from the above sources\n- [ ] SOURCE_INVENTORY.md updated with new class entries\n- [ ] Index and log updated\n- [ ] Lint passes clean\n- [ ] Cross-references to existing pages added\n\n## Related\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 (engineering wiki seed — completed, 52 pages)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2036 (cron ingest)\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 (cross-wiki link discovery)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/34","display_title":"feat: engineering wiki — ingest remaining high-value sources (skills metadata, closed issues)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/33","title":"WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities","issue_number":33,"body":"## WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities\n\n\n\n**Status:** pending | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** knowledge-domain | **Subcategory:** maritime-law\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### Mission\n\nEstablish maritime law as a first-class knowledge domain in workspace-hub by creating a dedicated skill, curating public-domain case law and liability data, and wiring it into the resource-intelligence and session-start pipelines.\n\n### What\n\n- Create `.claude/skills/domains/maritime-law/SKILL.md` covering: jurisdiction (UNCLOS, flag-state, port-state), liability regimes (CLC 1992, Bunker Convention 2001, HNS Convention, Athens Convention), standard forms (B/L, charter-party, P&I club), and dispute resolution (Lloyd's, LMAA, SCMA).\n- Curate a `knowledge/seeds/maritime-law-cases.yaml` file with ≥10 landmark public cases (e.g. The MSC Flaminia, Prestige, Erika, MV Wakashio, Ever Given) including: case name, year, jurisdiction, key finding, liability outcome, and source URL (public record).\n- Add `knowledge/seeds/maritime-liabilities.yaml` covering standard liability caps, conventions, and indemnity chains (ship-owner → P&I club → cargo interests → reinsurer).\n- Index both YAML seeds into the knowledge base via `scripts/knowledge/build-knowledge-index.sh`.\n- Add a `maritime-law` entry to `config/ai_agents/ai-tools-status.yaml` domain registry (if one exists) or equivalent config.\n\n### Why\n\nThe workspace handles offshore engineering assets (OrcaFlex, ANSYS, CFD). Maritime law governs liability, insurance, and regulatory compliance for offshore structures and vessels. Having machine-readable case law and liability conventions allows agents to answer regulatory questions and flag compliance risks in WRK items.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/33","display_title":"WRK-1126: Add maritime law domain: skill, data, public cases, liabilities"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/32","title":"feat: career-learnings seed migration — pipeline integrity, OrcaFlex VIV, FEA, CFD, energy economics","issue_number":32,"body":"## Summary\n\nMigrate career-learnings YAML seed into appropriate wiki domains.\n\n## Entries (11 total)\n\n| # | Title | Category | Target |\n|---|-------|----------|--------|\n| 1 | Pipeline integrity (DNV RP-F101, API 579) | Engineering | marine-engineering |\n| 2 | OrcaFlex VIV analysis | Engineering | marine-engineering |\n| 3 | FEA structural analysis | Engineering | marine-engineering |\n| 4 | CFD for offshore | Engineering | marine-engineering |\n| 5 | Cathodic protection design | Engineering | marine-engineering (already exists!) |\n| 6 | Energy economics (NPV, field dev) | Engineering | marine-engineering |\n| 7 | AI in DWOP | Drilling | marine-engineering |\n| 8 | Real estate analysis | Finance | personal wiki |\n| 9 | Shell scripting patterns | Software | personal wiki |\n| 10 | Python type safety | Software | personal wiki |\n| 11 | JSONL knowledge stores | Software | wiki-patterns |\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Create entity pages for pipeline integrity, VIV, FEA, CFD in marine-engineering\n2. Update cross-references to existing concepts (cathodic-protection already exists)\n3. Create personal wiki for finance/software entries\n4. Update index.md for any existing target Wiki\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] 6 engineering entries as new entities/concepts in marine-engineering wiki.\n- [ ] Cross-references to existing pages verified.\n- [ ] 4 software/finance entries migrated to personal wiki.\n- [ ] index.md updated for all wikis.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/32","display_title":"feat: career-learnings seed migration — pipeline integrity, OrcaFlex VIV, FEA, CFD, energy economics"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/31","title":"feat(knowledge): promote design-code registry into standards overviews and repo-target backlinks","issue_number":31,"body":"## Summary\nPromote the design code registry into first-class LLM-wiki strengthening outputs: standards-family overview pages, edition-awareness cross-links, and repo-target backlinks that connect standards knowledge to downstream engineering repos.\n\n## Why\nThe repo already has a high-signal design-code registry, but it is not being used as a wiki-strengthening surface:\n- `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml` tracks ~30 engineering codes with edition status, disciplines, and `repos` mappings.\n- `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md` explicitly says the design code registry is only partially discoverable and is not referenced from engineering wiki or standards wiki pages.\n- Existing wiki work is mostly source-document and standards-ledger oriented; the code registry is the repo ecosystem's curated view of which standards matter to which downstream repos.\n\nThis means the wiki layer is missing a compact, navigable bridge from standards knowledge -> edition status -> repo applicability.\n\n## Scope\n- Review `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml` as a promotion source for L3 wiki strengthening.\n- Define standards-family overview pages or updates that summarize code families already tracked in the registry (DNV, API, ISO, ASME/BSI/ASME as applicable).\n- Add repo-target backlinks so wiki pages can point to the downstream repos named in the registry (for example `digitalmodel`, `doris`).\n- Surface edition-status signals (`current`, `check`, `superseded`) in a wiki-friendly way without duplicating the registry as a second source of truth.\n- Recommend how this promotion should interact with existing standard-specific pages like DNV/API/OCIMF pages.\n\n## Deliverables\n- A promotion design/report mapping code-registry entries to target wiki pages.\n- Proposed family-overview pages and/or updates to existing standards pages.\n- Repo-target backlink convention grounded in the registry `repos` field.\n- Guidance for keeping registry truth in L2 while exposing useful summaries in L3.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] code-registry entries are mapped to concrete wiki targets or explicit deferrals\n- [ ] repo-target backlinks are proposed using existing `repos` metadata\n- [ ] edition-awareness is surfaced without making the wiki the source of truth for edition tracking\n- [ ] overlap with current standard pages is handled by extend-vs-create guidance\n- [ ] resulting artifact improves discoverability of the design code registry from the wiki layer\n\n## Related\n- Design code registry: `data/design-codes/code-registry.yaml`\n- Capabilities summary: `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_CAPABILITIES_SUMMARY.md`\n- Accessibility map: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2096 / `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md`\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Existing wiki standard promotions: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2216, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/31","display_title":"feat(knowledge): promote design-code registry into standards overviews and repo-target backlinks"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/30","title":"feat(knowledge): backfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages","issue_number":30,"body":"## Summary\nBackfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages so older LLM-wiki content can answer what source artifact, issue, seed, or registry record it was promoted from.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that the policy stack now expects stronger provenance, but much of the existing wiki corpus predates that discipline:\n- the provenance contract defines richer `doc_key`/promotion semantics\n- new work is adding `doc_key` and `wiki_refs` capabilities (#2363, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362)\n- older wiki pages and logs still often lack page-level promotion lineage, which weakens maintenance and reuse\n\nWithout provenance backfill, older pages remain hard to audit when source docs, issues, or registries change.\n\n## Scope\n- Inventory pre-existing wiki pages across current domains that lack strong promotion provenance.\n- Define bounded backfill rules by source class (issues, seeds, skills, registry-backed sources, research outputs).\n- Add page-level promotion references where deterministic evidence exists.\n- Emit an explicit ambiguity report for pages that cannot be backfilled safely.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Provenance-backfill inventory and strategy.\n- Backfilled promotion lineage for deterministic cases.\n- Ambiguity/no-safe-backfill report for the rest.\n- Guidance for how this interacts with doc_key and reverse-lookup work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] legacy wiki pages are classified into deterministic backfill vs ambiguous buckets\n- [ ] deterministic cases gain promotion provenance without hallucinated lineage\n- [ ] ambiguous cases are reported explicitly rather than silently guessed\n- [ ] resulting output improves future doc_key/wiki_refs maintenance work\n\n## Related\n- Parent operating model: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n- Wiki reverse lookup: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\n- L3 frontmatter/doc_key follow-ons: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2233, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\n- Closed-issue citation guardrail: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2238\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/30","display_title":"feat(knowledge): backfill promotion provenance on pre-existing wiki pages"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/29","title":"feat(knowledge): add canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages","issue_number":29,"body":"## Summary\nAdd canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages so filename-only and numeric source pages become discoverable by human-readable titles, citation aliases, and stable search labels.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found a large live navigation problem in the source layer of the wiki corpus:\n- `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/sources/` currently contains 19,159 source pages.\n- 19,137 of those pages use filename-style titles like `spe143317.pdf`.\n- 1,458 use purely numeric titles like `22035.pdf`.\n- Sample source pages confirm this title pattern in frontmatter.\n\nThis makes the source corpus technically present but practically hard to navigate. Source pages should be discoverable by canonical title and common citation alias, not only by opaque filenames.\n\n## Scope\n- Start with the marine-engineering wiki source corpus.\n- Derive `canonical_title` / `title_aliases` / equivalent display metadata from existing L2 evidence where available (conference metadata, summaries, registry titles, extracted titles).\n- Keep raw filename as one preserved alias, not the primary display label when better metadata exists.\n- Update index/search generation to prefer human-readable titles while preserving stable links.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Source-title aliasing strategy for wiki source pages.\n- Backfill pass for marine-engineering source pages with deterministic alias/title evidence.\n- Updated source/index generation rules so filename-only rows are no longer the default display surface.\n- Explicit ambiguity report for pages that cannot be safely renamed/labeled from existing evidence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] source pages can be discovered by canonical title or known alias rather than only raw filename\n- [ ] numeric/filename-only source titles are reduced wherever deterministic metadata exists\n- [ ] raw filenames are preserved as aliases for stability\n- [ ] wiki index/search surfaces prefer readable titles without breaking links\n\n## Related\n- Wiki reverse lookup: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2363\n- Faceted portals for large domains: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\n- Conference-summary promotion: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2369\n- Provenance/reuse contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/29","display_title":"feat(knowledge): add canonical source-title aliasing for wiki source pages"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/28","title":"feat(knowledge): chunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index","issue_number":28,"body":"## Summary\nChunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index so it remains authoritative but no longer forces users and agents through a single 21K-line navigation surface.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that the canonical index itself remains a major usability bottleneck even after portal and aliasing follow-ons:\n- `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md` is 21,605 lines.\n- Its frontmatter reports `page_count: 19181` and `source_count: 19159`.\n- The domain currently has only a small number of entity/concept pages relative to source pages, so the canonical index is dominated by exhaustive source rows.\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 improves discovery through faceted portal pages, but explicitly does not replace the canonical index.\n\nThe repo still needs the authoritative index surface itself to be navigable and bounded.\n\n## Scope\n- Keep one canonical top-level `index.md` entry point for marine-engineering.\n- Generate bounded chunk pages for oversized sections, especially Sources.\n- Add stable section/range navigation (`next` / `prev` / jump links) without breaking current links.\n- Make chunking reproducible/scripted rather than hand-maintained.\n- Define a reusable chunking policy that can later apply to other oversized wiki indexes.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Canonical-index chunking/pagination design.\n- Generated source/section sub-indexes for marine-engineering.\n- Stable navigation model between top-level index and chunk pages.\n- Chunking policy documentation for future large domains.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] marine-engineering no longer requires reading one 21K-line index file for exhaustive navigation\n- [ ] top-level index remains canonical and authoritative\n- [ ] chunk pages are generated, not manually curated\n- [ ] stable links/navigation exist across chunk pages and back to the top-level index\n\n## Related\n- Faceted portal pages: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\n- Source-title aliasing: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#29\n- Strengthening scorecard: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/28","display_title":"feat(knowledge): chunk and paginate the canonical marine-engineering wiki index"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/27","title":"docs(knowledge): add standard uplink/back-navigation block to wiki index pages","issue_number":27,"body":"## Summary\nAdd a small, consistent navigation block to every `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/index.md` so wiki index pages expose both an upward link into the intelligence ecosystem and local back-navigation to sibling wiki surfaces.\n\n## Why\nParallel-agent review confirmed this residual gap is still real in repo state:\n- `docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md` explicitly says the unified intelligence landing page exists, but wiki `index.md` files still have no upward link to the intelligence ecosystem.\n- Live inspection of current wiki indexes shows they do not consistently link to:\n  - `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\n  - local `CLAUDE.md`\n  - local `wiki/log.md`\n  - local `wiki/overview.md` / portal page when present\n- Current indexes act as downward-only content tables rather than full navigation entry points.\n\nThis is a lightweight cross-wiki navigation standard, distinct from portal generation or index pagination.\n\n## Scope\n- Define one reusable nav/uplink block convention for `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/index.md`.\n- Include at minimum:\n  - intelligence landing page: `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\n  - local `CLAUDE.md`\n  - local `log.md` when present\n  - local `overview.md` and/or portal page when present\n- Apply the convention across existing wiki domains, with graceful handling where a sibling surface does not yet exist.\n- Keep scope focused on index-page navigation standardization only.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Standard wiki-index navigation block pattern.\n- Updates to current wiki index pages to use that pattern.\n- Minimal guidance for optional targets (`overview.md`, portal page, `log.md`) when absent.\n- Optional lightweight lint/check so the block does not drift.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] every wiki `index.md` links upward to `docs/document-intelligence/README.md`\n- [ ] every wiki `index.md` links to its local `CLAUDE.md`\n- [ ] wiki indexes link to `log.md` / `overview.md` / portal when those files exist\n- [ ] the pattern is consistent across domains and does not depend on one-off formatting\n- [ ] scope stays distinct from portal generation (#2368) and marine index pagination (#2378)\n\n## Related\n- Canonical entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\n- Large-domain portal generation: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22\n- Marine index chunking/pagination: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#28\n- Registry-backed explorer views: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2379\n- Durable/transient boundary context: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/27","display_title":"docs(knowledge): add standard uplink/back-navigation block to wiki index pages"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/24","title":"Phase 2: Promote CSA Z276.1-20 + Z276.18 into marine-engineering wiki/standards/","issue_number":24,"body":"Phase split off from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 to decouple CSA work from OCIMF Tandem.\n\nTargets:\n- knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/standards/csa-z276-1-20.md\n- knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/standards/csa-z276-18.md\n\nFrontmatter contract from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 and .claude/rules/calc-citation-contract.md:\n- code_id, publisher, revision are required unless vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 lands a documented alias.\n\nPrereqs:\n1. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 codification merged to main: schema CLAUDE.md amendment, .gitignore re-include for marine wiki/standards/, and lint path coverage.\n2. CSA OCR remediation: text_preview for both CSA artifacts is currently unusable/corrupted according to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 v5 plan evidence.\n3. Per-code wiki routing decision remains marine-engineering vs naval-architecture per vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 sanction.\n\nThis issue does not block vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 closure. vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2227 closes only when OCIMF Phase 1 Branch A lands on origin/main.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/24","display_title":"Phase 2: Promote CSA Z276.1-20 + Z276.18 into marine-engineering wiki/standards/"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/23","title":"feat(knowledge): update wiki CLAUDE.md files to declare doc_key in L3 frontmatter required-set","issue_number":23,"body":"## Context\n\nParent vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 operating model Section 8.1 (amendment 2026-04-19, [comment](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2205#issuecomment-4277238819)) mandates a baseline floor of `{title, last_updated, doc_key}` as required fields in every wiki `CLAUDE.md` schema declaration. No wiki `CLAUDE.md` currently declares `doc_key` as required.\n\nThis blocks the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 conformance check from being enforced without day-one failures.\n\n## Current state (verified 2026-04-19)\n\n| Wiki | `CLAUDE.md` path | Current required-set | Missing from baseline floor |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| engineering | `knowledge/wikis/engineering/CLAUDE.md` | `{title, tags, added, last_updated}` | `doc_key` |\n| maritime-law | `knowledge/wikis/maritime-law/CLAUDE.md` (if present) | uses `{domain, created, last_updated, page_count}` in index | `title`, `doc_key` |\n| naval-architecture | `knowledge/wikis/naval-architecture/CLAUDE.md` (if present) | uses `{domain, created, last_updated, page_count}` in index | `title`, `doc_key` |\n| _other wikis_ | per-wiki `CLAUDE.md` | varies | all must add `doc_key` |\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Audit every `knowledge/wikis/*/CLAUDE.md` file.\n2. For each, update the required-set declaration to include all three baseline-floor fields: `title`, `last_updated`, `doc_key`.\n3. Preserve domain-specific required fields already in place.\n4. For wikis lacking a `CLAUDE.md`, decide whether to create one (likely yes for any wiki with governed L3 content).\n5. Update existing L3 pages that lack `doc_key` — either backfill from the registry or add a grace-period transition policy.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Changing the baseline floor itself (locked by parent Section 8.1).\n- Implementing the FRONT-1 conformance check in code (separate issue under vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206).\n- Per-child contract fields (#2207, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 own those).\n\n## References\n\n- Parent operating model: `docs/document-intelligence/llm-wiki-resource-doc-intelligence-operating-model.md` §8.1\n- Parent amendment summary: [#2205 comment 4277238819](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2205#issuecomment-4277238819)\n- Surfaced by: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207 residual vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 residual vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 residual R1 (all three 2026-04-19 revision runs)\n\n## Related\n\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 (amendment is authoritative)\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 check enforcement\n- Related: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2207 §6.3 (adds provenance fields on top of baseline), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209 §10.1 (adds durability fields on top of baseline)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every `knowledge/wikis/*/CLAUDE.md` declares `title`, `last_updated`, `doc_key` as required.\n- L3 pages across all wikis have `doc_key` set (via backfill or documented transition policy).\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2206 FRONT-1 passes when run against the live wikis.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/23","display_title":"feat(knowledge): update wiki CLAUDE.md files to declare doc_key in L3 frontmatter required-set"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/21","title":"feat(llm-wiki): regenerate cross-links.md across 8 wikis after Tier C page additions","issue_number":21,"body":"## Summary\n\nTier C added ~75 new wiki pages across 6 wikis (asset-management, naval-architecture, maritime-law, lng-projects, engineering riser, engineering pipeline). The auto-generated `wiki/cross-links.md` files and any faceted-portal pages (#2368 territory) are now stale and need a regeneration pass.\n\n## Why\n\n`scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` (#2011) auto-generates per-wiki `cross-links.md` files showing inbound/outbound links across wikis. These files are not git-committed by Tier C agents — they're meant to be refreshed by the script.\n\nSurfaced specifically by vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2587 close-out: the planned `test_asset_management_appears_in_cross_links_md` was rewritten by the implementing agent because:\n- `cross-links.md` is auto-generated, not hand-edited\n- The agent's scope contract forbade editing files outside its wiki tree\n- The test was replaced with a positive inbound-reference assertion on the new pages themselves\n\nThe result is that asset-management's `cross-links.md` doesn't yet exist, and the other 5 newly-populated wikis' `cross-links.md` files (where they exist) don't reflect the new pages.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Run `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` (or its current entry point — verify before running) across all 8 wikis: marine-engineering, engineering, naval-architecture, engineering-standards, asset-management, maritime-law, lng-projects, acma-projects\n2. Commit the regenerated `cross-links.md` files\n3. Spot-check that the asset-management `cross-links.md` now exists and shows the inbound references from `risk-based-inspection.md`, `fitness-for-service.md`, `integrity-management-cycle.md` to the engineering wiki\n4. (Optional, scope decision) If vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted-portal generation is wired up, run that too — engineering wiki is now at 103 pages and is the largest target\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- 8 `cross-links.md` files refreshed and committed (or note if any wikis don't yet have one as a deliberate gap)\n- Diff reviewable (~bounded by net new pages × link density)\n- No test regressions — `tests/knowledge/test_*` stay green\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Hand-editing `cross-links.md` files (they're auto-gen)\n- Schema changes to the script\n- Cross-link discovery improvements (#2044, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2068 territory)\n- Faceted-portal authoring (separate scope under vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22)\n\n## References\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2587 (closed) — asset-management close-out flagged the gap\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#36 — cross-link discovery infrastructure\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#35 — engineering wiki cross-link discovery with domain wikis\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 — faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 — llm-wiki strengthening epic\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/21","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): regenerate cross-links.md across 8 wikis after Tier C page additions"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/llm-wiki/issues/20","title":"feat(llm-wiki): backfill engineering-wiki reverse cross-links to Tier C riser/pipeline pages","issue_number":20,"body":"## Summary\n\nThe 20 new engineering-wiki concept pages added in Tier C Batch C (#2597 risers + vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 pipelines, commit `6d3483bc5`) have one-way cross-links to existing related pages but the inbound (reverse) links from those existing pages were intentionally deferred to avoid cross-agent races on shared files during the parallel-dispatch phase.\n\n## Why\n\nBoth implementation agents (#2597, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602) flagged this in their close-out reports as a known deferral:\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2597 deferred the \"Related design pages\" pointer block on `concepts/viv-riser-fatigue.md`\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 deferred reverse pointer blocks on `concepts/pipeline-integrity-assessment.md` and `concepts/free-span-viv-fatigue.md`\n\nWithout the reverse links, navigation from existing established pages to the new specialized sub-domain pages requires the user to know the new pages exist. The cross-link discoverability layer (#2011, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#35) and the auto-generated `cross-links.md` (script `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py`) help, but human-curated reverse anchors on the established hub pages are higher-signal.\n\n## Scope (single-session implementation, ~30 min)\n\nAdd a `## Related design pages` block to each of:\n\n1. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/viv-riser-fatigue.md`\n   - Link to all 10 `riser-*.md` pages (or the navigationally relevant subset: configurations, steel-catenary, top-tensioned, flexible, hybrid-tower, drilling-system, global-analysis-load-cases, soil-interaction)\n\n2. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/pipeline-integrity-assessment.md`\n   - Link to relevant `pipeline-*.md` pages (lateral-buckling, upheaval-buckling, walking, soil-interaction, on-bottom-stability, route-selection, installation-methods, end-expansion-spool-design, trawl-impact-protection, coatings)\n\n3. `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/concepts/free-span-viv-fatigue.md`\n   - Link to `pipeline-on-bottom-stability.md`, `pipeline-soil-interaction.md`, `pipeline-route-selection.md`, `riser-soil-interaction.md` (the soil/seabed cluster)\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- 3 existing pages amended with `## Related design pages` block\n- Each new link verified to resolve (the riser-*/pipeline-* targets exist on `main` per Batch C)\n- `tests/knowledge/test_engineering_riser_expansion.py` and `test_engineering_pipeline_expansion.py` still pass (no new tests required — the existing one-way `test_at_least_one_cross_link_to_existing_pipeline_page` already covers the inbound side)\n- Optional: re-run `scripts/knowledge/wiki-cross-links.py` to refresh `engineering/wiki/cross-links.md`\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Editing other established pages (limit to the 3 named above)\n- Adding reverse links into other wikis (Tier C agents stayed in single-wiki scope; cross-wiki backfill is vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#30 territory)\n\n## References\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2597 (closed) — riser dispatch close-out report flags deferral\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2602 (closed) — pipeline dispatch close-out report flags deferral\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 — llm-wiki strengthening epic\n- vamseeach