{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:domain:gtm","sort":"updated","order":"desc","topn":30},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117\", \"title\": \"WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem\", \"issue_number\": 117, \"body\": \"## WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] Write 1-page \\\"value brief\\\" targeting the Oil Man persona (PDF via `data:md-to-pdf`)\\n- [ ] Identify 3 flagship calculation demos: (1) CP cathodic protection per DNV-RP-B401,\\n- [ ] Create `specs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md` with full persona card\\n- [ ] Draft capability map: which repo covers which O&G discipline\\n- [ ] Build shareable Jupyter notebook: CP design + DNV compliance check\\n- [ ] Build shareable Jupyter notebook: production decline forecast (worldenergydata)\\n- [ ] Create short README / landing copy for each repo targeting O&G audience\\n- [ ] Record or document a \\\"5-minute demo\\\" flow: input \\u2192 calculation \\u2192 PDF report\\n- [ ] Identify 10 target contacts: LinkedIn (subsea engineers, PE consultants,\\n- [ ] Draft outreach message templates (email + LinkedIn DM)\\n- [ ] Prepare FAQ: \\\"Is this open source?\\\", \\\"Does it replace OrcaFlex?\\\",\\n- [ ] Set up simple intake: GitHub Discussions or email alias\\n- [ ] Share demo notebooks on LinkedIn (personal + engineering groups)\\n- [ ] Post in relevant communities: SPE LinkedIn group, r/petroleum, O&G Slack channels\\n- [ ] Reach out to 5 warm contacts individually\\n- [ ] Capture feedback: what resonates, what gaps remain\\n- [ ] Write retrospective WRK item for Month 2 based on learnings\\n- [ ] `specs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md` committed with full persona card\\n- [ ] 2 shareable demo notebooks published (CP + decline curve)\\n- [ ] 1-page value brief PDF generated\\n- [ ] Outreach templates drafted and reviewed\\n- [ ] Week 4 retrospective WRK item created\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2640\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): worldenergydata production decline forecast \\u2014 shareable Jupyter notebook for GTM demo\", \"issue_number\": 2640, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nIssue [#117](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117) acceptance criteria includes:\\n> Build shareable Jupyter notebook: production decline forecast (worldenergydata)\\n\\nThe `worldenergydata` library now has a production-ready `ArpsDeclineCurve` module at `worldenergydata.production.forecast.decline`. The GTM candidate review (2026-05-04) confirmed it works end-to-end:\\n- Hyperbolic, exponential, harmonic curve fitting via scipy\\n- EUR (Estimated Ultimate Recovery) calculation\\n- 240-month forecast with confidence intervals\\n- Plotly interactive visualization\\n\\nA 63 KB FDAS GTM HTML report was already generated (`reports/gtm/2026-05-04-fdas-field-development-economics.html`), which includes an Arps decline demo with synthetic data.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nCreate a standalone Jupyter notebook at `worldenergydata/notebooks/gtm_production_decline_forecast.ipynb`:\\n\\n1. **Section 1: Module overview** \\u2014 what Arps decline is, three model types, typical GoM/North Sea use cases\\n2. **Section 2: Synthetic demo** \\u2014 fit a synthetic GoM well (qi=5000 bbl/month, Di=0.08/month, b=0.6), show EUR=146 Mbbls\\n3. **Section 3: Multi-well portfolio** \\u2014 fit 3 hypothetical wells (early, mid, late decline stages), side-by-side comparison\\n4. **Section 4: Sensitivity** \\u2014 how EUR changes with b (hyperbolic exponent) from 0.2 to 1.0\\n5. **Section 5: Connect to FDAS economics** \\u2014 feed EUR directly into `EconomicsQuery.npv()` to compute field-level NPV from decline curve\\n\\nAll sections must run without external data (synthetic data generated in-notebook).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Notebook executes end-to-end with `jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute` in <60 seconds\\n- [ ] All Plotly charts render (interactive HTML output cells)\\n- [ ] A companion `reports/gtm/gtm_production_decline_forecast.html` is exported from the notebook\\n- [ ] Notebook added to `worldenergydata/notebooks/README.md` index\\n- [ ] No BSEE binary data required to run\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- Parent: [#117](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117)\\n- Implemented ArpsDeclineCurve: `worldenergydata/src/worldenergydata/production/forecast/decline.py`\\n- FDAS GTM report with Arps demo: `worldenergydata/reports/gtm/2026-05-04-fdas-field-development-economics.html`\\n- Generation script reference: `worldenergydata/scripts/gtm/generate_fdas_gtm_report.py`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2640\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): worldenergydata production decline forecast \\u2014 shareable Jupyter notebook for GTM demo\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2016\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline -- turn repo capability into paying clients\", \"issue_number\": 2016, \"body\": \"     1|## Mission: Convert engineering capability to paying clients\\n     2|\\n     3|> \\\"All of this is paper work until I get some clients.\\\"\\n     4|\\n     5|ACE Engineer consulting firm with 23yr P.E. experience, $120K/yr retainer target. Everything in this repo (skills, workflows, knowledge bases, agent automation) is infrastructure toward that single goal.\\n     6|\\n     7|### Current GTM Position\\n     8|\\n     9|**What ACE does**: Core engineering -- OrcaFlex/mooring/riser/FEA/cathodic/API 579/Python\\n    10|**Target**: Offshore 10-50 engineer firms\\n    11|**GTM activity**: 1281 ace contacts, 20+ prospects in pipeline, job market scanner cron running\\n    12|**Expert networks**: GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint (#1994)\\n    13|\\n    14|### What Exists vs What Needs to Exist\\n    15|\\n    16|**Has**:\\n    17|- Engineering skills covering marine/offshore, drilling, FEA, CFD, standards\\n    18|- 691 skills across external repos\\n    19|- Knowledge bases and wiki infrastructure\\n    20|- Automated email triage (3 Gmail accounts)\\n    21|- Cron-based job market scanning\\n    22|- Multi-agent workflow (Claude, Codex, Gemini)\\n    23|- Repo as living demo of capability\\n    24|\\n    25|**Needs**:\\n    26|1. Parametric demo reports (HTML/PDF) -- show, don't tell\\n    27|2. Engineering chatbot demo -- see #engineering-chatbot skill\\n    28|3. Expert network responses -- turn insights into revenue\\n    29|4. Follow-up engine from 1281 contacts\\n    30|5. Case studies from digitalmodel/ work\\n    31|\\n    32|### The Ask\\n    33|\\n    34|This issue tracks the conversion funnel from capability to revenue. Sub-issues for each GTM lever below.\\n    35|\\n    36|### Acceptance Criteria\\n    37|- [ ] At least one paying client engaged via any channel\\n    38|- [ ] Demo materials (parametric reports + chatbot) ready for outreach\\n    39|- [ ] 100 expert network queries submitted with responses\\n    40|- [ ] 50 personalized follow-ups sent from contact database\\n    41|- [ ] 3+ public-facing engineering analyses published (aceengineer.com)\\n    42|- [ ] Monthly revenue > $10K from any source\\n    43|\\n    44|### Related\\n    45|- #1994 (expert network registration)\\n    46|- #1993 (Rigzone job pipeline)\\n    47|- GTM: aceengineer-strategy/ notes\\n    48|\\n    49|\\n    50|## GTM EXECUTION PLAN \\u2014 Ordered by Priority\\n    51|Last updated: 2026-04-07\\n    52|\\n    53|### TIER 0 \\u2014 IMMEDIATE REVENUE (this week)\\n    54|Pure hustle, zero engineering work, highest ROI.\\n    55|\\n    56|| # | Sub-issues | Status | Effort |\\n    57||---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n    58|| 1994 | Register expert networks (GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint) | Open | 2 hours |\\n    59|| 1993 | Rigzone job apps \\u2014 check live postings, tailor resume, apply | Open | 4 hours |\\n    60|\\n    61|### TIER 1 \\u2014 DEMO MATERIALS (show don't tell)\\n    62|Demo 2 (wall thickness) is DONE. Build the rest in dependency order.\\n    63|\\n    64|| Step | Sub-issues | Status | Blocked By |\\n    65||------|-----------|--------|-----------|\\n    66|| Inventory models | 1904, 1932 | Open | -- |\\n    67|| Vessel data | 1798 (HLV specs), 1799 (pipelay specs) | Open | -- |\\n    68|| Demo 2 polish | 1831, 1833 (done), 1832 (--from-cache) | Open | -- |\\n    69|| Demo 3 | 1931/1872 (mudmat, 180 cases) | OPEN | vessel data, cache flag |\\n    70|| Demo 5 | 1874, 1905 (jumper model) | Open | Demo 3 code |\\n    71|| Demo 1 | 1930/1871 (freespan, ~680 cases) | Open | cache flag |\\n    72|| Notebook | 1792 (VIV demo notebook) | Open | Demo 1 |\\n    73|| Demo 4 | 1873 (shallow water pipelay) | Open | pipelay specs, cache flag |\\n    74|| Screencasts | 1809 (5x .gif recordings) | Open | all 5 demos |\\n    75|\\n    76|### TIER 2 \\u2014 GTM INFRASTRUCTURE\\n    77|Runs parallel with demo building.\\n    78|\\n    79|| Sub-issues | What | Status |\\n    80||-----------|------|--------|\\n    81|| 1707, 1708, 1709 | Scanner fixes (rate limiting, dedup, retention) | Open |\\n    82|| 1971 | Email triage workflow (aceengineer.com) | Open |\\n    83|\\n    84|### TIER 3 \\u2014 OUTREACH\\n    85|Requires demos + infrastructure ready first.\\n    86|\\n    87|| Sub-issues | What | Blocked By |\\n    88||-----------|------|-----------|\\n    89|| 191 | Chatbot fundamentals \\u2014 persona, tone, pitch template | None |\\n    90|| 117 | Oil-and-gas persona + 1-month GTM plan | #191, 2+ demos |\\n    91|| 1669 | Vessel contractor email outreach (20+ targets) | demos, #191, #117 |\\n    92|| 197 | Narada/WhatsApp AI agent replicate guide | None (best after outreach starts) |\\n    93|\\n    94|### TIER 4 \\u2014 PIPELINE MODULES (expand portfolio)\\n    95|\\n    96|| Sub-issues | What | Effort |\\n    97||-----------|------|--------|\\n    98|| 1834 | Field Development Pipeline Engineering skill | 16 hrs |\\n    99|| 1835 | On-bottom stability (DNV-RP-F109) | 12 hrs |\\n   100|| 1836 | Shore approach (HDD, trenching, pull-in) | 10 hrs |\\n   101|| 1837 | Pipeline CAPEX cost model | 8 hrs |\\n   102|\\n   103|### CRITICAL PATH TO FIRST CLIENT\\n   104|\\n   105|```\\n   106|#1994 (register expert networks) -- 2hrs --> $300-600/hr consultations\\n   107|     |\\n   108|     v\\n   109|#1904 (inventory) --> #1798/#1799 (vessel data) --> #1931 (Demo 3) --> #1874 (Demo 5)\\n   110|     |                                                      |\\n   111|#1831/#1832 (cache infra) --> #1930 (Demo 1) --> #1873 (Demo 4) --> #1809 (GIFs)\\n   112|     |\\n   113|     v\\n   114|#1669 (email outreach with demos) --> paying clients\\n   115|```\\n   116|\\n   117|### RELATED ISSUES\\n   118|- #108 \\u2014 WRK-148: ACE-GTM parent strategy stream (Stage 17)\\n   119|- #1670 \\u2014 Energy company job market scan (CLOSED)\\n   120|- #1671 \\u2014 US-wide job market scan (CLOSED)\\n   121|- #898 \\u2014 Repo portfolio steering skill (CLOSED)\\n   122|\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2016\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline -- turn repo capability into paying clients\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2557\", \"title\": \"chore(productivity): weekly work-pattern review and flow hacks\", \"issue_number\": 2557, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nWeekly Business Brain issue: review the owner's full work pattern and recommend productivity hacks that make work flow faster.\\n\\n## Business Brain target\\nThis week should include a work-pattern review that reduces owner orchestration time and increases GTM/artifact throughput.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Audit recent Hermes/Claude/Codex/Gemini sessions, GitHub issue throughput, plan/review/execution churn, context handoffs, repeated friction points, provider/tool bottlenecks, and GTM artifact flow.\\n- Identify 10-15 practical productivity hacks, separated into immediate, this-week, and structural changes.\\n- Tie each recommendation to observed evidence and expected throughput improvement.\\n- Prefer agent-self-cycling improvements that preserve legal/TDD/review gates while reducing user time.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Repo-tracked productivity review report under `docs/reports/`.\\n- Ranked hack backlog with owner-time impact, implementation effort, and first action.\\n- Follow-up GitHub issues for high-confidence automation/workflow improvements.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Recent work evidence is audited rather than guessed.\\n- [ ] Recommendations distinguish GTM throughput, engineering throughput, agent orchestration, and context/handoff hygiene.\\n- [ ] Each hack has an owner-time reduction hypothesis and a concrete next action.\\n- [ ] At least 3 immediately actionable hacks are packaged for execution without more owner input.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\\n- Provider throughput / credit-burn posture\\n- Autonomous hard-gate evolution metrics\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2557\", \"display_title\": \"chore(productivity): weekly work-pattern review and flow hacks\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1669\", \"title\": \"[WRK] GTM: Vessel Installation Contractor Email Outreach Campaign\", \"issue_number\": 1669, \"body\": \"## Objective\\n\\nPrepare and execute a go-to-market (GTM) email outreach campaign targeting **vessel installation contractors** as the first client segment for ACE Engineer consulting and AI-powered engineering services.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n- ACE Engineer (Vamsee Achanta) offers deep subsea/offshore engineering expertise \\u2014 hydrodynamics, mooring/riser design, structural analysis, OrcaFlex/OrcaWave, fatigue assessment\\n- An engineering chatbot pitch exists at `docs/strategy/engineering-chatbot-oilgas-pitch.md` with a phased capability roadmap (Knowledge Base \\u2192 Document Intelligence \\u2192 Analysis Pre-Processor \\u2192 Review Assistant \\u2192 Digital Advisor)\\n- Target segment: vessel installation contractors (EPIC contractors, pipelay/heavy-lift vessel operators, subsea installation companies)\\n- Goal: generate warm leads for engineering consulting engagements and/or AI-assisted engineering tool pilots\\n\\n## Target Companies (Vessel Installation Contractors)\\n\\nResearch and compile a contact list of key companies including but not limited to:\\n\\n1. **Tier 1 \\u2014 Major EPIC / Installation Contractors**\\n   - Subsea7, TechnipFMC, Saipem, McDermott, Allseas, Heerema\\n   - Boskalis (Boskalis Subsea Services)\\n   - Van Oord (offshore wind installation)\\n   - DEME Offshore\\n\\n2. **Tier 2 \\u2014 Specialist Installation Vessel Operators**\\n   - DOF Subsea, Solstad Offshore, Bourbon Offshore\\n   - Sapura Energy, EMAS (now Ezra Holdings)\\n   - Seaway7 (Subsea7 renewables arm)\\n   - Coastline Maritime (cable/pipe installation)\\n\\n3. **Tier 3 \\u2014 Regional / Niche Players**\\n   - Cal Dive (now Helix Energy Solutions), Superior Energy Services\\n   - Global Industries legacy contacts\\n   - Gulf Offshore, DeepOcean Group\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n### Phase 1 \\u2014 Strategy & Templates (this issue)\\n- [ ] Define value proposition per company tier\\n- [ ] Draft 3 email templates (cold intro, follow-up, meeting request)\\n- [ ] Create a prospect contact list with company, contact name, title, email (research-based)\\n- [ ] Define email sequence timing (Day 0, Day 3, Day 7)\\n- [ ] Prepare a 1-page capability summary / attachment (PDF or link)\\n\\n### Phase 2 \\u2014 Personalization & Execution\\n- [ ] Personalize emails per company (reference their fleet, recent projects, pain points)\\n- [ ] Set up email tracking (open/click if tooling available)\\n- [ ] Execute first batch of outreach\\n- [ ] Log responses and schedule follow-ups\\n\\n### Phase 3 \\u2014 Measure & Iterate\\n- [ ] Track response rates by tier\\n- [ ] Refine messaging based on feedback\\n- [ ] Expand to adjacent segments (drilling contractors, FPSO operators, floating wind developers)\\n\\n## Value Proposition Angles\\n\\n| Angle | Message |\\n|-------|---------|\\n| **Engineering Efficiency** | Reduce analysis turnaround by 40-60% with AI-assisted OrcaFlex/structural workflows |\\n| **Knowledge Continuity** | Stop losing institutional knowledge when engineers leave \\u2014 encode it in AI |\\n| **QC Multiplier** | AI-powered review catches errors that fatigued reviewers miss |\\n| **Junior Engineer Ramp-up** | New hires become productive 3x faster with an AI engineering mentor |\\n| **Cost Arbitrage** | Senior-level engineering insight at a fraction of full-time consultant rates |\\n\\n## Email Template Structure\\n\\n### Email 1 \\u2014 Cold Introduction\\n- Subject line: problem-aware, specific to their operations\\n- Open with a relevant industry pain point (e.g., engineer shortage, project delays, rising analysis costs)\\n- Brief intro of capability (1-2 sentences)\\n- Specific offer (free 30-min consultation or a sample analysis)\\n- Clear CTA\\n\\n### Email 2 \\u2014 Follow-up (Day 3)\\n- Reference Email 1\\n- Share a concrete example / case study\\n- Lower-friction CTA (reply with availability)\\n\\n### Email 3 \\u2014 Meeting Request (Day 7)\\n- Final touch \\u2014 direct calendar link\\n- Mention will reach out via LinkedIn if no response\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/README.md` \\u2014 campaign overview\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/prospect-list.md` \\u2014 target companies and contacts\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/email-templates.md` \\u2014 3 email templates\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/value-proposition.md` \\u2014 per-tier messaging\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/capability-summary.md` \\u2014 1-pager for attachment\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- `docs/strategy/engineering-chatbot-oilgas-pitch.md` \\u2014 existing AI chatbot pitch\\n- `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` \\u2014 ecosystem context\\n- `client_projects/energy_engineering/ecs/ecs_clients.md` \\u2014 existing client contacts\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n- 20+ personalized emails sent to decision-makers at vessel installation contractors\\n- 3+ positive responses or meeting requests within 2 weeks\\n- At least 1 pilot engagement initiated within 30 days\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1669\", \"display_title\": \"[WRK] GTM: Vessel Installation Contractor Email Outreach Campaign\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2347\", \"title\": \"chore(gtm): reconcile stale tracker bodies for #2016, #1669, #117, #191 to shipped reality\", \"issue_number\": 2347, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nFour umbrella / strategy issues have bodies that predate the 2026-04-10 and 2026-04-15 shipping waves. Reviewers can't tell what's open vs. shipped.\\n\\n## Evidence\\nSelf-flagged in `docs/reports/2026-04-15-gtm-cross-review-readiness.md`:\\n- #2016 \\u2014 tracker body stale vs shipped work\\n- #1669 \\u2014 reflects old blockers/file paths\\n- #117  \\u2014 stale paths/status vs actual artifacts\\n- #191  \\u2014 stale scope/status vs current artifacts\\n\\n## Scope\\nFor each issue:\\n- Mark shipped children \\u2713 with date + artifact link\\n- Strip obsolete paths; replace with current artifacts\\n- Restate remaining scope explicitly\\n- Post a summary comment for audit trail\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] #2016 body updated with current GTM inventory\\n- [ ] #1669 narrowed to remaining outreach only\\n- [ ] #117 closed or rescoped\\n- [ ] #191 closed or rescoped\\n\\n## Related\\n- Adversarial review 2026-04-17\\n- Exit summary 2026-04-15\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2347\", \"display_title\": \"chore(gtm): reconcile stale tracker bodies for #2016, #1669, #117, #191 to shipped reality\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2345\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): wire GTM demos into unified smoke runner \\u2014 prevent silent demo rot\", \"issue_number\": 2345, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n#2118 validated all 5 GTM demos once on 2026-04-15 as a manual chore. No regression gate exists. A refactor in digitalmodel or a data-file move will break charts silently; a prospect finds out before we do.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- #2118 acceptance was a one-shot run\\n- Harness smoke runners exist: #2272 (baseline), #2297 (drift), #2298 (phase-2)\\n- `digitalmodel/examples/demos/gtm/` is not covered\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Extend #2298 pattern to the 5 GTM demos in `--from-cache` mode (fast, per-PR) and full-calc mode (weekly cron)\\n- Publish HTML render diff to catch chart breakage\\n- Emit `gtm-demo-health` signal to dashboard\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] CI runs all 5 on every PR touching `digitalmodel/` or `examples/demos/gtm/`\\n- [ ] Full-calc weekly cron verified\\n- [ ] Broken demo fails build with diff artifact\\n\\n## Related\\n- #2272, #2297, #2298, #2118, #2087, #1832\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2345\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): wire GTM demos into unified smoke runner \\u2014 prevent silent demo rot\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2349\", \"title\": \"docs(gtm): refresh 30-day plan \\u2014 #1809 closed, update dependency table + Day-7 checkpoint\", \"issue_number\": 2349, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n`docs/gtm/gtm-plan-30day.md` lists #1809 as a Week-1 dependency. #1809 closed 2026-04-15 and workflow GIFs (#2288) landed. Plan doc still stale.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Plan line 184: \\\"GIF recordings need all 5 demos running clean | #1809\\\"\\n- `gh issue view 1809` \\u2192 CLOSED 2026-04-15\\n- Day-7 checkpoint items not updated\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Strike #1809 from Dependencies; replace with \\\"verify workflow GIFs embedded on aceengineer.com\\\"\\n- Mark Day-7 items \\u2713/pending/blocked\\n- Date-stamp plan revision\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] Dependencies table reflects 2026-04-17 reality\\n- [ ] Day-7 items statused\\n- [ ] Revision date updated\\n\\n## Related\\n- #1809, #2288, companion checkpoint-dashboard issue\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2349\", \"display_title\": \"docs(gtm): refresh 30-day plan \\u2014 #1809 closed, update dependency table + Day-7 checkpoint\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2350\", \"title\": \"verify: #2043 mooring animation render outputs \\u2014 confirm published or reopen\", \"issue_number\": 2350, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n#2043 closed with Manim scene script but acceptance also required rendered GIF + MP4 and README update. Script exists; render and publish status are unverified.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- `scripts/animations/scenes/mooring_layout.py` present\\n- `__pycache__/mooring_layout.cpython-312.pyc` (ran at least once)\\n- Rendered outputs not found under `docs/gtm/media/` or `aceengineer-website/content/`\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Check build output directories for rendered artifacts\\n- If present: confirm publish path and link from gallery / mooring page\\n- If absent: reopen #2043 or open finish-the-render follow-up\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] Render artifacts located or rebuilt\\n- [ ] Published or explicitly deferred\\n- [ ] #2043 closure matches reality\\n\\n## Related\\n- #2035, #2115\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2350\", \"display_title\": \"verify: #2043 mooring animation render outputs \\u2014 confirm published or reopen\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2351\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): Day-7/14/21/30 checkpoint dashboard \\u2014 surface plan metrics for weekly review\", \"issue_number\": 2351, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nThe 30-day GTM plan contains checkpoint tables at Day 7/14/21/30 and a Success Metrics table. Nothing surfaces progress against them; no tripwire for \\\"No paid engagement by Day 30\\\".\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- `docs/gtm/gtm-plan-30day.md` lines 41-44, 89-94, 117-122, 151-156\\n- No tracker issue, no automation, no rollup report\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Choose substrate: (a) long-lived issue with weekly comment updates, or (b) generated `docs/reports/gtm-checkpoint-YYYY-MM-DD.md` on cron\\n- Wire sources: outreach log, expert-network count, LinkedIn count, warm-lead count\\n- Emit red/green vs Success Metrics table\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] Checkpoint tracker exists + populated\\n- [ ] Weekly cadence set\\n- [ ] Day-30 rollup produces go/no-go against plan decision points\\n\\n## Related\\n- #2016, companion 30-day plan refresh issue\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2351\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): Day-7/14/21/30 checkpoint dashboard \\u2014 surface plan metrics for weekly review\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2355\", \"title\": \"chore(website): pin Node engines in aceengineer-website package.json + vercel.json\", \"issue_number\": 2355, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nThe `aceengineer-website/package.json` has no `engines` field and `vercel.json` does not pin a Node runtime version. This leaves the build environment implicit and susceptible to silent drift when Vercel's default Node image changes.\\n\\n## Why accepted as debt (not blocker)\\nFrom the approved plan's Known Minor Debt table (row G): the current Vercel default Node 20 build works today, so this is a forward-looking resiliency fix rather than a regression. The existing demo-detail-pages rollout in #2342/#2343 does not depend on a specific Node version, so pinning was deferred to avoid widening the PR scope.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Add `\\\"engines\\\": { \\\"node\\\": \\\">=20.x <21\\\" }` (or chosen range) to `aceengineer-website/package.json`.\\n- Add a matching Node runtime pin to `aceengineer-website/vercel.json` (e.g. `\\\"build\\\": { \\\"env\\\": { \\\"NODE_VERSION\\\": \\\"20\\\" } }` or the equivalent supported Vercel schema).\\n- Confirm local `npm install` and `vercel build` still succeed with the pin.\\n- Document the chosen Node range in the repo README or build docs.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] `package.json` contains an `engines.node` field with an explicit range.\\n- [ ] `vercel.json` pins the matching Node major version.\\n- [ ] A Vercel preview build completes green with the pin applied.\\n- [ ] A brief note in docs/README explains the pinning rationale and how to bump it.\\n\\n## Parent / context\\n- Approved plan: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-17-issue-2342-2343-demo-detail-pages.md\\n- Documented in plan's \\\"Known Minor Debt\\\" section as row G\\n- Related: #2342, #2343 (parent GTM issues)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2355\", \"display_title\": \"chore(website): pin Node engines in aceengineer-website package.json + vercel.json\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2356\", \"title\": \"feat(ci): add GH Actions workflow to run npm test on aceengineer-website PRs\", \"issue_number\": 2356, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n`aceengineer-website/` has no GitHub Actions workflow under `.github/workflows/`. The Jest link-check suite runs only locally via `npm test`, so PRs can merge without automated verification that internal links resolve.\\n\\n## Why accepted as debt (not blocker)\\nFrom the approved plan's Known Minor Debt table (row CI-1): the link-check tests are already written, passing locally, and were executed by the author during the #2342/#2343 implementation. CI wiring is a harness improvement independent of the demo-detail-pages content itself, and adding a workflow in the same PR would have expanded scope beyond the plan-approved work.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Add `aceengineer-website/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (or equivalent path honored by the repo's actions routing).\\n- Workflow should trigger on `pull_request` affecting `aceengineer-website/**` and on `push` to `main`.\\n- Steps: checkout, setup-node (matching the engines pin from the sibling issue once landed), `npm ci`, `npm test`.\\n- Make the job required for merge on PRs touching the website tree.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] A workflow file exists at `aceengineer-website/.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\\n- [ ] The workflow runs `npm ci && npm test` on PRs changing `aceengineer-website/**`.\\n- [ ] A sample PR shows the job executing green.\\n- [ ] Branch protection / ruleset marks the job required for website PRs.\\n\\n## Parent / context\\n- Approved plan: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-17-issue-2342-2343-demo-detail-pages.md\\n- Documented in plan's \\\"Known Minor Debt\\\" section as row CI-1\\n- Related: #2342, #2343 (parent GTM issues)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2356\", \"display_title\": \"feat(ci): add GH Actions workflow to run npm test on aceengineer-website PRs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1994\", \"title\": \"[WRK] Register for GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint expert networks\", \"issue_number\": 1994, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nExpert networks are the HIGHEST ROI ad-hoc income channel. Zero application hassle vs. full job applications. 1-hour phone consultations with hedge funds, PE firms, law firms about offshore/marine engineering topics. Your 23yr PE + OrcaFlex + Chevron + BP background is exactly what they seek.\\n\\n## Platforms to Register\\n\\n### 1. GLG (Gerson Lehrman Group)\\n- URL: glg.it\\n- Rate: $150-$1,000+/hr (typical $300-600 for offshore PE expertise)\\n- Fee: Zero to expert (client pays GLG, GLG pays you)\\n- Non-exclusive\\n- Action: Create expert profile highlighting 23yr subsea/offshore, Chevron 16yr, PE license\\n\\n### 2. AlphaSights\\n- URL: alphasights.com\\n- Rate: $150-$500/hr\\n- Fee: Zero to expert\\n- Non-exclusive\\n- Action: Create expert profile\\n\\n### 3. Guidepoint\\n- URL: guidepoint.com/experts\\n- Rate: $100-$500/hr\\n- Fee: Zero to expert\\n- Non-exclusive\\n- Action: Create expert profile\\n\\n## Positioning Statement (for all 3)\\n\\n> Subsea Engineering VP/Principal PE with 23 years experience at Chevron, BP, ExxonMobil projects. Expertise: offshore riser/pipeline/mooring design, FEED/pre-FEED, OrcaFlex/AQWA/ANSYS, digital twins/automation. Former BP Macondo emergency response engineering manager. API standards committee member (API-RP-16Q). GoM deepwater specialist.\\n\\n## Topics You Can Consult On\\n- Offshore/subsea oil & gas engineering and economics\\n- Mooring and riser system design for deepwater\\n- OrcaFlex/AQWA hydrodynamic analysis\\n- BP Macondo containment design and emergency response\\n- LNG terminal marine mooring design (current: WoodFibre LNG $1.8B)\\n- GoM deepwater development economics\\n- Offshore installation analysis and vessel operations\\n- Python/automation in subsea engineering\\n- Digital twins for offshore asset management\\n\\n## Tasks\\n- [ ] Register at glg.it as expert\\n- [ ] Register at alphasights.com as expert\\n- [ ] Register at guidepoint.com/experts as expert\\n- [ ] Document registration status and expert profile URLs\\n- [ ] Note: ExpertVoice (expertvoice.com) should be SKIPPED \\u2014 not a consulting platform\\n\\n## Notes\\n- ExpertVoice is NOT a consulting platform \\u2014 it is a product discount/advocacy site\\n- All 3 expert networks are non-exclusive \\u2014 sign up for all\\n- Use ACE Engineer Consulting as entity for professional liability/tax purposes\\n- PE license = major differentiator; display prominently\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1994\", \"display_title\": \"[WRK] Register for GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint expert networks\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/191\", \"title\": \"WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals \\u2014 shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)\", \"issue_number\": 191, \"body\": \"## WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals \\u2014 shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\\n\\n**Repo:** ['frontierdeepwater', 'TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nCreate a shared `ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md` document and embed\\npersona/tone standards into ALL client system prompts (WRK-625, WRK-629).\\n\\nSource: `~/Downloads/Engineering_Chatbot_Pitch_OilGas.md`\\n\\n### 1. Shared Fundamentals File\\n\\n`ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md`\\n\\n#### Persona Design Principles (apply to ALL system prompts)\\n\\nEvery system prompt (rigid jumper, pipeline, structural/diffraction, maritime legal)\\nmust embed these four principles as a closing `## Persona and Tone` section:\\n\\n```markdown\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nTone and persona consistency across all clients is the difference between a demo that\\nfeels like a toy and one that feels like a senior engineer. The four principles\\n(precision, practicality, caution, transparency) + the standard disclaimer protect\\nagainst the two biggest objections: \\\"can we trust this?\\\" and \\\"who's liable?\\\".\\n\\nThe client pitch one-pager turns the demo follow-up into a structured commercial\\nconversation rather than an ad-hoc explanation.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] `ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md` created with all 4 sections\\n- [ ] `ai-initiatives/shared/client_pitch_oilgas.md` created (adapted from source, no names)\\n- [ ] `## Persona and Tone` section present in all 4 system prompt files\\n- [ ] `## Known Limitations` section present in all 4 system prompt files\\n- [ ] Standard disclaimer wording consistent across all prompts\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (source doc is internal \\u2014 no client names in output files)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/191\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals \\u2014 shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2035\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): manim-based engineering explainer pipeline\", \"issue_number\": 2035, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nBuild a Manim-based engineering explainer pipeline that turns key engineering analyses into reusable animated assets for GTM, demos, and public-facing technical content.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe reviewed Hermes+Manim video confirms a capability that fits our ecosystem well: animated explainers are a strong bridge from technical depth to client-facing clarity.\\n\\nWe already have GTM demos and static HTML reporting. The next step is to add a reusable animation workflow for selected flagship engineering examples.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a first-pass engineering animation pipeline that:\\n1. identifies 2-3 flagship scenarios\\n2. defines reusable animation patterns/templates\\n3. generates at least one working Manim explainer from repo data or representative fixtures\\n4. documents how to reproduce/adapt it for future demos and outreach\\n\\n## Candidate flagship scenarios\\n- catenary / lazy-wave riser geometry evolution\\n- mooring layout / force or excursion explainer\\n- installation sequence or vessel-operability envelope\\n- report companion animation for a GTM demo\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- animation workflow docs and file layout\\n- at least one complete Manim explainer checked into repo\\n- template structure for future engineering animations\\n- rendered output suitable for website/outreach/demo reuse\\n- issue comment summarizing what was produced and where to extend next\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] One complete engineering animation pipeline implemented and documented\\n- [ ] At least one rendered animation artifact produced from a real or representative engineering scenario\\n- [ ] Templates/patterns defined so future scenarios are faster to add\\n- [ ] Clear link established to GTM demo/report pipeline\\n- [ ] Follow-on work linked to #1809, #2016, and #2022 as appropriate\\n\\n## Related\\n- #1809 GTM: Create .gif screencasts of all 5 demo reports running\\n- #2016 feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline\\n- #2022 feat: publish repo knowledge bases as aceengineer.com content\\n- docs/notes/2026-04-08-youtube-hermes-opportunities.md\\n\\n## Execution notes for Claude Code\\n- Start by picking the single highest-signal scenario; do not boil the ocean.\\n- Optimize for reusable engineering storytelling, not generic motion graphics.\\n- Prefer artifacts that can feed README/site/outreach collateral.\\n- End by documenting exact commands, asset paths, and next candidate animations.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2035\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): manim-based engineering explainer pipeline\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2117\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): resume + cover letter generator for Rigzone applications (#1993)\", \"issue_number\": 2117, \"body\": \"## Purpose\\nAutomate resume tailoring for offshore engineering job applications. Vamsee applies to Rigzone positions not to get hired but to generate consulting conversations.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\ndocs/gtm/resume-templates/\\n\\nContents:\\n1. **base-resume.md** \\u2014 master resume (23yr P.E., all domains, key projects)\\n2. **cover-letter-template.md** \\u2014 fill-in-the-blank per position\\n3. **tailoring-guide.md** \\u2014 which sections to emphasize per job type:\\n   - Subsea installation \\u2192 OrcaFlex, marine ops, DNV-RP-H103\\n   - Pipeline integrity \\u2192 wall thickness, VIV, on-bottom stability\\n   - Mooring/riser \\u2192 OrcaFlex, fatigue, API RP 2SK\\n   - Structural \\u2192 FEA, API 579, cathodic protection\\n\\n## Related\\n- #1993 \\u2014 Rigzone application pipeline\\n- docs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md (informs positioning)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2117\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): resume + cover letter generator for Rigzone applications (#1993)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2114\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): VIV demo notebook \\u2014 freespan walkthrough for pipeline engineers (#1792)\", \"issue_number\": 2114, \"body\": \"## Purpose\\nCreate a Jupyter notebook walkthrough of Demo 1 (freespan/VIV) for pipeline engineers. Like the S-N notebook but focused on span assessment workflow.\\n\\n## Content\\n1. DNV-RP-F105 methodology overview\\n2. Natural frequency calculation walkthrough\\n3. Reduced velocity and VIV onset screening\\n4. Gap ratio effects on allowable span\\n5. Interactive allowable span map (Plotly)\\n6. Pipe size comparison \\u2014 when to upsize for span tolerance\\n\\n## Prerequisite\\n- Demo 1 results exist (done)\\n- Free span modules exist (done)\\n\\n## Deliverable\\ndocs/notebooks/freespan-viv-demo.ipynb\\n\\n## Related\\n- #1792 \\u2014 original freespan notebook request\\n- Demo 1 script (demo_01_dnv_freespan_viv.py)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2114\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): VIV demo notebook \\u2014 freespan walkthrough for pipeline engineers (#1792)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2038\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): manim installation sequence / operability envelope animation\", \"issue_number\": 2038, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nBuild the third Manim engineering explainer: offshore installation sequence with vessel operability envelope.\\n\\n## Why\\nFollow-on from #2035 (catenary riser explainer). Installation planning and weather window analysis are high-value consulting deliverables. Animating a subsea lift sequence with go/no-go weather limits demonstrates operational engineering capability.\\n\\n## Scope\\nUsing the reusable template from #2035:\\n1. Implement operability envelope calculations (Hs vs Tp limits, crane capacity curves)\\n2. Build Manim scene showing a subsea installation sequence (vessel approach, crane deploy, lower-to-seabed)\\n3. Animate weather window overlay \\u2014 green/red zones on scatter diagram\\n4. Include operability callout (e.g., % weather window availability)\\n\\n## Data sources\\n- Vessel data from #1798 (HLV specs) and #1799 (pipelay specs) when available\\n- Representative crane capacity and weather scatter data\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- [ ] Operability math module with tests\\n- [ ] Complete Manim scene with four-phase structure\\n- [ ] GIF + MP4 renders\\n- [ ] Issue comment with assets and commands\\n\\n## Depends on\\n- #2035 \\u2014 pipeline and template (DONE)\\n- #1798, #1799 \\u2014 vessel data (nice-to-have, can use representative values)\\n\\n## Related\\n- #1809 \\u2014 GIF screencasts\\n- #2016 \\u2014 client conversion pipeline\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2038\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): manim installation sequence / operability envelope animation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2037\", \"title\": \"feat(gtm): manim mooring layout / force explainer animation\", \"issue_number\": 2037, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nBuild the second Manim engineering explainer: mooring layout with force/excursion visualization.\\n\\n## Why\\nFollow-on from #2035 (catenary riser explainer). Mooring systems are a core ACE capability and visually compelling \\u2014 spread mooring patterns, chain catenary shapes, and vessel excursion envelopes tell a complete engineering story.\\n\\n## Scope\\nUsing the reusable template from #2035 (`scripts/animations/scenes/template.py`):\\n1. Implement mooring geometry calculations (spread pattern, chain catenary, pretension)\\n2. Build Manim scene showing vessel excursion under environmental loading\\n3. Animate mooring line tension changes as vessel offsets\\n4. Include code check callout (e.g., maximum line tension vs MBL)\\n\\n## Data sources\\n- `knowledge/seeds/mooring-failures-lng-terminals.yaml` \\u2014 real failure cases for context\\n- Representative 4-point or 8-point spread mooring configuration\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- [ ] Mooring math module with tests\\n- [ ] Complete Manim scene with four-phase structure\\n- [ ] GIF + MP4 renders\\n- [ ] Issue comment with assets and commands\\n\\n## Related\\n- #2035 \\u2014 parent pipeline (DONE)\\n- #1809 \\u2014 GIF screencasts\\n- #2016 \\u2014 client conversion pipeline\\n- #2022 \\u2014 aceengineer.com content\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2037\", \"display_title\": \"feat(gtm): manim mooring layout / force explainer animation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1993\", \"title\": \"[WRK] Rigzone job application pipeline \\u2014 resume tailoring and submission\", \"issue_number\": 1993, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nScraped and scored 13 Rigzone job postings against Vamsee's profile (23yr PE, offshore/subsea, Chevron 16yr, Python/digital transformation). Chevron Project Manager III (R000065929) was the best fit at 9/10 but confirmed EXPIRED on careers.chevron.com.\\n\\n## Top Candidates to Track\\n\\n| Rank | Title | Company | Fit | Status |\\n|------|-------|---------|-----|--------|\\n| 1 | Project Manager III | Chevron | 9/10 | EXPIRED (confirmed) |\\n| 2 | Surface Facilities Assurance Supervisor\\u2013Sr Manager | Occidental | 8/10 | Status unknown |\\n| 3 | Director, Midstream Facilities | Cheniere | 7/10 | Status unknown |\\n| 4 | Regulatory Consultant (CONTRACT) | Wood Group | 6/10 | Status unknown |\\n| 5 | Artificial Lift Systems Engr Sr/Pr | Occidental | 5/10 | Status unknown |\\n\\nAll postings were from Jan 22 \\u2013 Feb 3, 2026. It is now April 6.\\n\\n## Tasks\\n\\n- [ ] Check if Occidental R12978 (Surface Facilities Assurance) is still live at oxy.com/careers\\n- [ ] Check if Chevron R12988 (Surface Analyst) is still live\\n- [ ] Check if Cheniere 2026-2012 (Director Midstream) is still live at careers.cheniere.com\\n- [ ] Resolve merge conflict in teamresumes/cv/va_resume.md\\n- [ ] Create tailored resume versions for each live opening\\n- [ ] Generate brief application statements / cover letters\\n- [ ] Document actual apply URLs for each active posting\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n- `teamresumes/cv/tailored/` \\u2014 directory with company-specific resume variants\\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/job-applications/` \\u2014 cover letters and application tracking\\n- Application status dashboard\\n\\n## Reference\\n\\nSession summary: `~/notes/rigzone-job-pipeline-2026-04-06.md`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1993\", \"display_title\": \"[WRK] Rigzone job application pipeline \\u2014 resume tailoring and submission\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1792\", \"title\": \"feat(freespan): GTM demo notebook \\u2014 free-span VIV assessment walkthrough\", \"issue_number\": 1792, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nThe DNV-RP-F105 free-span VIV module is now complete with 93 passing tests.\\nA Jupyter notebook demonstrating the full workflow would serve as:\\n1. GTM demo material for prospective clients\\n2. Validation documentation for the module\\n3. Quick-start guide for engineers\\n\\n## Notebook Scope\\n\\n### Section 1: Pipeline Input Definition\\n- Define a 10\\\" pipeline span (OD=0.2731m, WT=0.0127m, L=34m)\\n- Show PipeSpanInput dataclass with all parameters\\n\\n### Section 2: Natural Frequency Calculation\\n- Compute fn_IL, fn_CF with boundary condition comparison\\n- Plot fn vs span length (parametric sweep)\\n\\n### Section 3: VIV Onset Screening\\n- Show screening check at design current\\n- Visualize onset boundary (Ur vs Vr_onset)\\n\\n### Section 4: VIV Amplitude & Fatigue\\n- Compute IL/CF amplitudes and stresses\\n- Show bilinear S-N curve (F-class, air vs seawater_cp)\\n- Calculate fatigue life\\n\\n### Section 5: Current Profile & Weibull Extrapolation\\n- 5-bin current profile \\u2192 Weibull fit \\u2192 100-year current\\n- Plot exceedance probability vs current speed\\n\\n### Section 6: Full Assessment\\n- FreespanVIVFatigue facade end-to-end\\n- Results summary table\\n- Allowable span length\\n\\n### Section 7: Parametric Study\\n- Span length sweep \\u2192 fatigue life curve\\n- Wall thickness sensitivity\\n- Current velocity sensitivity\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Self-contained Jupyter notebook\\n- [ ] All cells execute without errors\\n- [ ] Plotly or matplotlib visualizations\\n- [ ] No client-specific or deny-list content\\n- [ ] Placed in `digitalmodel/docs/domains/pipelines/freespan/`\\n\\n## Related\\n- Parent: #1773 (closed), #1783 (closed)\\n- Uses: all free_span modules\\n- GTM: aceengineer-strategy/ demo inventory\\n- Related: #1692 (S-N curve library demo)\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1792\", \"display_title\": \"feat(freespan): GTM demo notebook \\u2014 free-span VIV assessment walkthrough\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/197\", \"title\": \"WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset\", \"issue_number\": 197, \"body\": \"## WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\n### Phase 1 \\u2014 Commit guide to workspace-hub (30 min)\\n\\nCopy the guide into the repository so it is version-controlled and accessible\\nfrom any machine:\\n\\n```\\ndocs/agents/narada-openclaw-setup-guide.md\\n```\\n\\nStrip personal identifiers (user home paths, API key examples) and replace with\\ngeneric placeholders / env-var references before committing. Run legal scan to\\nconfirm no client references.\\n\\n### Phase 2 \\u2014 Create `automation/narada-openclaw` skill (1\\u20132 h)\\n\\nPath: `.claude/skills/automation/narada-openclaw/SKILL.md`\\n\\nCapability sections:\\n- `install` \\u2014 reproduce Phase I end-to-end from guide\\n- `add_workspace` \\u2014 clone an existing agent workspace for a new channel\\n  (e.g., GitHub assistant variant)\\n- `channel_whatsapp` \\u2014 QR pair, reconnect, rotate session\\n- `channel_github` \\u2014 configure GitHub webhook channel (future)\\n- `model_config` \\u2014 swap underlying model (Claude / GPT-4.1 / Gemini)\\n- `debug` \\u2014 common failure modes: QR timeout, build errors, agent not responding\\n- `backup_restore` \\u2014 QMD memory snapshot + restore procedure\\n\\nTrigger: manual, invoked during new agent deployment or channel rotation.\\n\\nRelated skills: `automation/session-memory`, `agents/agent-spawning`\\n\\n### Phase 3 \\u2014 GitHub assistant quick-start (optional, 30 min)\\n\\nExtract the \\\"Part III: Replication\\\" section into a dedicated file:\\n\\n```\\ndocs/agents/narada-github-assistant-quickstart.md\\n```\\n\\nCovers only the delta from the full guide \\u2014 assumes OpenClaw already installed,\\nfocuses on workspace cloning and GitHub channel configuration.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- The guide is currently in a local home directory only \\u2014 one machine wipe loses it\\n- A skill makes the setup reproducible by any Claude agent session on any machine\\n- The GitHub assistant variant is a high-value extension: turns Narada into a\\n  code-aware bot that responds in GitHub issue/PR comments via webhook\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] `docs/agents/narada-openclaw-setup-guide.md` committed (no personal paths,\\n- [ ] `.claude/skills/automation/narada-openclaw/SKILL.md` created with \\u226420 line\\n- [ ] `docs/agents/narada-github-assistant-quickstart.md` created (replication\\n- [ ] Legal scan passes on all three files\\n- [ ] Skill registered in skill index if one exists\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/197\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/108\", \"title\": \"WRK-148: ACE-GTM: A&CE Go-to-Market strategy stream\", \"issue_number\": 108, \"body\": \"## WRK-148: ACE-GTM: A&CE Go-to-Market strategy stream\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\\n\\n**Repo:** ['aceengineer-website', 'aceengineer-strategy', 'workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nParent work item for all A&CE go-to-market activity. This is a **running stream** \\u2014 new findings, recommendations, and action items get added here as the strategy evolves. Child items get spun off for execution.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nRevenue is oxygen. The engineering substance is strong but the packaging, positioning, and pipeline don't exist yet. This stream coordinates all work to fix that.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] All child items (WRK-142, 146, 147) completed\\n- [ ] Website repositioned with firm voice\\n- [ ] Business strategy repo operational with weekly scorecard habit\\n- [ ] At least 1 outbound experiment launched\\n- [ ] Pipeline has 5+ qualified prospects\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. User Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **18. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **19. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/108\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-148: ACE-GTM: A&CE Go-to-Market strategy stream\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117","title":"WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem","issue_number":117,"body":"## WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] Write 1-page \"value brief\" targeting the Oil Man persona (PDF via `data:md-to-pdf`)\n- [ ] Identify 3 flagship calculation demos: (1) CP cathodic protection per DNV-RP-B401,\n- [ ] Create `specs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md` with full persona card\n- [ ] Draft capability map: which repo covers which O&G discipline\n- [ ] Build shareable Jupyter notebook: CP design + DNV compliance check\n- [ ] Build shareable Jupyter notebook: production decline forecast (worldenergydata)\n- [ ] Create short README / landing copy for each repo targeting O&G audience\n- [ ] Record or document a \"5-minute demo\" flow: input → calculation → PDF report\n- [ ] Identify 10 target contacts: LinkedIn (subsea engineers, PE consultants,\n- [ ] Draft outreach message templates (email + LinkedIn DM)\n- [ ] Prepare FAQ: \"Is this open source?\", \"Does it replace OrcaFlex?\",\n- [ ] Set up simple intake: GitHub Discussions or email alias\n- [ ] Share demo notebooks on LinkedIn (personal + engineering groups)\n- [ ] Post in relevant communities: SPE LinkedIn group, r/petroleum, O&G Slack channels\n- [ ] Reach out to 5 warm contacts individually\n- [ ] Capture feedback: what resonates, what gaps remain\n- [ ] Write retrospective WRK item for Month 2 based on learnings\n- [ ] `specs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md` committed with full persona card\n- [ ] 2 shareable demo notebooks published (CP + decline curve)\n- [ ] 1-page value brief PDF generated\n- [ ] Outreach templates drafted and reviewed\n- [ ] Week 4 retrospective WRK item created\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117","display_title":"WRK-470: feat(gtm): oil-and-gas practitioner persona + 1-month GTM plan for workspace-hub ecosystem"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2640","title":"feat(gtm): worldenergydata production decline forecast — shareable Jupyter notebook for GTM demo","issue_number":2640,"body":"## Context\n\nIssue [#117](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117) acceptance criteria includes:\n> Build shareable Jupyter notebook: production decline forecast (worldenergydata)\n\nThe `worldenergydata` library now has a production-ready `ArpsDeclineCurve` module at `worldenergydata.production.forecast.decline`. The GTM candidate review (2026-05-04) confirmed it works end-to-end:\n- Hyperbolic, exponential, harmonic curve fitting via scipy\n- EUR (Estimated Ultimate Recovery) calculation\n- 240-month forecast with confidence intervals\n- Plotly interactive visualization\n\nA 63 KB FDAS GTM HTML report was already generated (`reports/gtm/2026-05-04-fdas-field-development-economics.html`), which includes an Arps decline demo with synthetic data.\n\n## Scope\n\nCreate a standalone Jupyter notebook at `worldenergydata/notebooks/gtm_production_decline_forecast.ipynb`:\n\n1. **Section 1: Module overview** — what Arps decline is, three model types, typical GoM/North Sea use cases\n2. **Section 2: Synthetic demo** — fit a synthetic GoM well (qi=5000 bbl/month, Di=0.08/month, b=0.6), show EUR=146 Mbbls\n3. **Section 3: Multi-well portfolio** — fit 3 hypothetical wells (early, mid, late decline stages), side-by-side comparison\n4. **Section 4: Sensitivity** — how EUR changes with b (hyperbolic exponent) from 0.2 to 1.0\n5. **Section 5: Connect to FDAS economics** — feed EUR directly into `EconomicsQuery.npv()` to compute field-level NPV from decline curve\n\nAll sections must run without external data (synthetic data generated in-notebook).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Notebook executes end-to-end with `jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute` in <60 seconds\n- [ ] All Plotly charts render (interactive HTML output cells)\n- [ ] A companion `reports/gtm/gtm_production_decline_forecast.html` is exported from the notebook\n- [ ] Notebook added to `worldenergydata/notebooks/README.md` index\n- [ ] No BSEE binary data required to run\n\n## References\n\n- Parent: [#117](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/117)\n- Implemented ArpsDeclineCurve: `worldenergydata/src/worldenergydata/production/forecast/decline.py`\n- FDAS GTM report with Arps demo: `worldenergydata/reports/gtm/2026-05-04-fdas-field-development-economics.html`\n- Generation script reference: `worldenergydata/scripts/gtm/generate_fdas_gtm_report.py`","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2640","display_title":"feat(gtm): worldenergydata production decline forecast — shareable Jupyter notebook for GTM demo"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2016","title":"feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline -- turn repo capability into paying clients","issue_number":2016,"body":"     1|## Mission: Convert engineering capability to paying clients\n     2|\n     3|> \"All of this is paper work until I get some clients.\"\n     4|\n     5|ACE Engineer consulting firm with 23yr P.E. experience, $120K/yr retainer target. Everything in this repo (skills, workflows, knowledge bases, agent automation) is infrastructure toward that single goal.\n     6|\n     7|### Current GTM Position\n     8|\n     9|**What ACE does**: Core engineering -- OrcaFlex/mooring/riser/FEA/cathodic/API 579/Python\n    10|**Target**: Offshore 10-50 engineer firms\n    11|**GTM activity**: 1281 ace contacts, 20+ prospects in pipeline, job market scanner cron running\n    12|**Expert networks**: GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint (#1994)\n    13|\n    14|### What Exists vs What Needs to Exist\n    15|\n    16|**Has**:\n    17|- Engineering skills covering marine/offshore, drilling, FEA, CFD, standards\n    18|- 691 skills across external repos\n    19|- Knowledge bases and wiki infrastructure\n    20|- Automated email triage (3 Gmail accounts)\n    21|- Cron-based job market scanning\n    22|- Multi-agent workflow (Claude, Codex, Gemini)\n    23|- Repo as living demo of capability\n    24|\n    25|**Needs**:\n    26|1. Parametric demo reports (HTML/PDF) -- show, don't tell\n    27|2. Engineering chatbot demo -- see #engineering-chatbot skill\n    28|3. Expert network responses -- turn insights into revenue\n    29|4. Follow-up engine from 1281 contacts\n    30|5. Case studies from digitalmodel/ work\n    31|\n    32|### The Ask\n    33|\n    34|This issue tracks the conversion funnel from capability to revenue. Sub-issues for each GTM lever below.\n    35|\n    36|### Acceptance Criteria\n    37|- [ ] At least one paying client engaged via any channel\n    38|- [ ] Demo materials (parametric reports + chatbot) ready for outreach\n    39|- [ ] 100 expert network queries submitted with responses\n    40|- [ ] 50 personalized follow-ups sent from contact database\n    41|- [ ] 3+ public-facing engineering analyses published (aceengineer.com)\n    42|- [ ] Monthly revenue > $10K from any source\n    43|\n    44|### Related\n    45|- #1994 (expert network registration)\n    46|- #1993 (Rigzone job pipeline)\n    47|- GTM: aceengineer-strategy/ notes\n    48|\n    49|\n    50|## GTM EXECUTION PLAN — Ordered by Priority\n    51|Last updated: 2026-04-07\n    52|\n    53|### TIER 0 — IMMEDIATE REVENUE (this week)\n    54|Pure hustle, zero engineering work, highest ROI.\n    55|\n    56|| # | Sub-issues | Status | Effort |\n    57||---|-----------|--------|--------|\n    58|| 1994 | Register expert networks (GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint) | Open | 2 hours |\n    59|| 1993 | Rigzone job apps — check live postings, tailor resume, apply | Open | 4 hours |\n    60|\n    61|### TIER 1 — DEMO MATERIALS (show don't tell)\n    62|Demo 2 (wall thickness) is DONE. Build the rest in dependency order.\n    63|\n    64|| Step | Sub-issues | Status | Blocked By |\n    65||------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n    66|| Inventory models | 1904, 1932 | Open | -- |\n    67|| Vessel data | 1798 (HLV specs), 1799 (pipelay specs) | Open | -- |\n    68|| Demo 2 polish | 1831, 1833 (done), 1832 (--from-cache) | Open | -- |\n    69|| Demo 3 | 1931/1872 (mudmat, 180 cases) | OPEN | vessel data, cache flag |\n    70|| Demo 5 | 1874, 1905 (jumper model) | Open | Demo 3 code |\n    71|| Demo 1 | 1930/1871 (freespan, ~680 cases) | Open | cache flag |\n    72|| Notebook | 1792 (VIV demo notebook) | Open | Demo 1 |\n    73|| Demo 4 | 1873 (shallow water pipelay) | Open | pipelay specs, cache flag |\n    74|| Screencasts | 1809 (5x .gif recordings) | Open | all 5 demos |\n    75|\n    76|### TIER 2 — GTM INFRASTRUCTURE\n    77|Runs parallel with demo building.\n    78|\n    79|| Sub-issues | What | Status |\n    80||-----------|------|--------|\n    81|| 1707, 1708, 1709 | Scanner fixes (rate limiting, dedup, retention) | Open |\n    82|| 1971 | Email triage workflow (aceengineer.com) | Open |\n    83|\n    84|### TIER 3 — OUTREACH\n    85|Requires demos + infrastructure ready first.\n    86|\n    87|| Sub-issues | What | Blocked By |\n    88||-----------|------|-----------|\n    89|| 191 | Chatbot fundamentals — persona, tone, pitch template | None |\n    90|| 117 | Oil-and-gas persona + 1-month GTM plan | #191, 2+ demos |\n    91|| 1669 | Vessel contractor email outreach (20+ targets) | demos, #191, #117 |\n    92|| 197 | Narada/WhatsApp AI agent replicate guide | None (best after outreach starts) |\n    93|\n    94|### TIER 4 — PIPELINE MODULES (expand portfolio)\n    95|\n    96|| Sub-issues | What | Effort |\n    97||-----------|------|--------|\n    98|| 1834 | Field Development Pipeline Engineering skill | 16 hrs |\n    99|| 1835 | On-bottom stability (DNV-RP-F109) | 12 hrs |\n   100|| 1836 | Shore approach (HDD, trenching, pull-in) | 10 hrs |\n   101|| 1837 | Pipeline CAPEX cost model | 8 hrs |\n   102|\n   103|### CRITICAL PATH TO FIRST CLIENT\n   104|\n   105|```\n   106|#1994 (register expert networks) -- 2hrs --> $300-600/hr consultations\n   107|     |\n   108|     v\n   109|#1904 (inventory) --> #1798/#1799 (vessel data) --> #1931 (Demo 3) --> #1874 (Demo 5)\n   110|     |                                                      |\n   111|#1831/#1832 (cache infra) --> #1930 (Demo 1) --> #1873 (Demo 4) --> #1809 (GIFs)\n   112|     |\n   113|     v\n   114|#1669 (email outreach with demos) --> paying clients\n   115|```\n   116|\n   117|### RELATED ISSUES\n   118|- #108 — WRK-148: ACE-GTM parent strategy stream (Stage 17)\n   119|- #1670 — Energy company job market scan (CLOSED)\n   120|- #1671 — US-wide job market scan (CLOSED)\n   121|- #898 — Repo portfolio steering skill (CLOSED)\n   122|","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2016","display_title":"feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline -- turn repo capability into paying clients"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2557","title":"chore(productivity): weekly work-pattern review and flow hacks","issue_number":2557,"body":"## Summary\nWeekly Business Brain issue: review the owner's full work pattern and recommend productivity hacks that make work flow faster.\n\n## Business Brain target\nThis week should include a work-pattern review that reduces owner orchestration time and increases GTM/artifact throughput.\n\n## Scope\n- Audit recent Hermes/Claude/Codex/Gemini sessions, GitHub issue throughput, plan/review/execution churn, context handoffs, repeated friction points, provider/tool bottlenecks, and GTM artifact flow.\n- Identify 10-15 practical productivity hacks, separated into immediate, this-week, and structural changes.\n- Tie each recommendation to observed evidence and expected throughput improvement.\n- Prefer agent-self-cycling improvements that preserve legal/TDD/review gates while reducing user time.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Repo-tracked productivity review report under `docs/reports/`.\n- Ranked hack backlog with owner-time impact, implementation effort, and first action.\n- Follow-up GitHub issues for high-confidence automation/workflow improvements.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recent work evidence is audited rather than guessed.\n- [ ] Recommendations distinguish GTM throughput, engineering throughput, agent orchestration, and context/handoff hygiene.\n- [ ] Each hack has an owner-time reduction hypothesis and a concrete next action.\n- [ ] At least 3 immediately actionable hacks are packaged for execution without more owner input.\n\n## Related\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\n- Provider throughput / credit-burn posture\n- Autonomous hard-gate evolution metrics\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2557","display_title":"chore(productivity): weekly work-pattern review and flow hacks"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1669","title":"[WRK] GTM: Vessel Installation Contractor Email Outreach Campaign","issue_number":1669,"body":"## Objective\n\nPrepare and execute a go-to-market (GTM) email outreach campaign targeting **vessel installation contractors** as the first client segment for ACE Engineer consulting and AI-powered engineering services.\n\n## Context\n\n- ACE Engineer (Vamsee Achanta) offers deep subsea/offshore engineering expertise — hydrodynamics, mooring/riser design, structural analysis, OrcaFlex/OrcaWave, fatigue assessment\n- An engineering chatbot pitch exists at `docs/strategy/engineering-chatbot-oilgas-pitch.md` with a phased capability roadmap (Knowledge Base → Document Intelligence → Analysis Pre-Processor → Review Assistant → Digital Advisor)\n- Target segment: vessel installation contractors (EPIC contractors, pipelay/heavy-lift vessel operators, subsea installation companies)\n- Goal: generate warm leads for engineering consulting engagements and/or AI-assisted engineering tool pilots\n\n## Target Companies (Vessel Installation Contractors)\n\nResearch and compile a contact list of key companies including but not limited to:\n\n1. **Tier 1 — Major EPIC / Installation Contractors**\n   - Subsea7, TechnipFMC, Saipem, McDermott, Allseas, Heerema\n   - Boskalis (Boskalis Subsea Services)\n   - Van Oord (offshore wind installation)\n   - DEME Offshore\n\n2. **Tier 2 — Specialist Installation Vessel Operators**\n   - DOF Subsea, Solstad Offshore, Bourbon Offshore\n   - Sapura Energy, EMAS (now Ezra Holdings)\n   - Seaway7 (Subsea7 renewables arm)\n   - Coastline Maritime (cable/pipe installation)\n\n3. **Tier 3 — Regional / Niche Players**\n   - Cal Dive (now Helix Energy Solutions), Superior Energy Services\n   - Global Industries legacy contacts\n   - Gulf Offshore, DeepOcean Group\n\n## Deliverables\n\n### Phase 1 — Strategy & Templates (this issue)\n- [ ] Define value proposition per company tier\n- [ ] Draft 3 email templates (cold intro, follow-up, meeting request)\n- [ ] Create a prospect contact list with company, contact name, title, email (research-based)\n- [ ] Define email sequence timing (Day 0, Day 3, Day 7)\n- [ ] Prepare a 1-page capability summary / attachment (PDF or link)\n\n### Phase 2 — Personalization & Execution\n- [ ] Personalize emails per company (reference their fleet, recent projects, pain points)\n- [ ] Set up email tracking (open/click if tooling available)\n- [ ] Execute first batch of outreach\n- [ ] Log responses and schedule follow-ups\n\n### Phase 3 — Measure & Iterate\n- [ ] Track response rates by tier\n- [ ] Refine messaging based on feedback\n- [ ] Expand to adjacent segments (drilling contractors, FPSO operators, floating wind developers)\n\n## Value Proposition Angles\n\n| Angle | Message |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Engineering Efficiency** | Reduce analysis turnaround by 40-60% with AI-assisted OrcaFlex/structural workflows |\n| **Knowledge Continuity** | Stop losing institutional knowledge when engineers leave — encode it in AI |\n| **QC Multiplier** | AI-powered review catches errors that fatigued reviewers miss |\n| **Junior Engineer Ramp-up** | New hires become productive 3x faster with an AI engineering mentor |\n| **Cost Arbitrage** | Senior-level engineering insight at a fraction of full-time consultant rates |\n\n## Email Template Structure\n\n### Email 1 — Cold Introduction\n- Subject line: problem-aware, specific to their operations\n- Open with a relevant industry pain point (e.g., engineer shortage, project delays, rising analysis costs)\n- Brief intro of capability (1-2 sentences)\n- Specific offer (free 30-min consultation or a sample analysis)\n- Clear CTA\n\n### Email 2 — Follow-up (Day 3)\n- Reference Email 1\n- Share a concrete example / case study\n- Lower-friction CTA (reply with availability)\n\n### Email 3 — Meeting Request (Day 7)\n- Final touch — direct calendar link\n- Mention will reach out via LinkedIn if no response\n\n## Files to Create\n\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/README.md` — campaign overview\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/prospect-list.md` — target companies and contacts\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/email-templates.md` — 3 email templates\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/value-proposition.md` — per-tier messaging\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/vessel-installation-contractors/capability-summary.md` — 1-pager for attachment\n\n## References\n\n- `docs/strategy/engineering-chatbot-oilgas-pitch.md` — existing AI chatbot pitch\n- `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` — ecosystem context\n- `client_projects/energy_engineering/ecs/ecs_clients.md` — existing client contacts\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- 20+ personalized emails sent to decision-makers at vessel installation contractors\n- 3+ positive responses or meeting requests within 2 weeks\n- At least 1 pilot engagement initiated within 30 days\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1669","display_title":"[WRK] GTM: Vessel Installation Contractor Email Outreach Campaign"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2347","title":"chore(gtm): reconcile stale tracker bodies for #2016, #1669, #117, #191 to shipped reality","issue_number":2347,"body":"## Summary\nFour umbrella / strategy issues have bodies that predate the 2026-04-10 and 2026-04-15 shipping waves. Reviewers can't tell what's open vs. shipped.\n\n## Evidence\nSelf-flagged in `docs/reports/2026-04-15-gtm-cross-review-readiness.md`:\n- #2016 — tracker body stale vs shipped work\n- #1669 — reflects old blockers/file paths\n- #117  — stale paths/status vs actual artifacts\n- #191  — stale scope/status vs current artifacts\n\n## Scope\nFor each issue:\n- Mark shipped children ✓ with date + artifact link\n- Strip obsolete paths; replace with current artifacts\n- Restate remaining scope explicitly\n- Post a summary comment for audit trail\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] #2016 body updated with current GTM inventory\n- [ ] #1669 narrowed to remaining outreach only\n- [ ] #117 closed or rescoped\n- [ ] #191 closed or rescoped\n\n## Related\n- Adversarial review 2026-04-17\n- Exit summary 2026-04-15","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2347","display_title":"chore(gtm): reconcile stale tracker bodies for #2016, #1669, #117, #191 to shipped reality"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2345","title":"feat(gtm): wire GTM demos into unified smoke runner — prevent silent demo rot","issue_number":2345,"body":"## Summary\n#2118 validated all 5 GTM demos once on 2026-04-15 as a manual chore. No regression gate exists. A refactor in digitalmodel or a data-file move will break charts silently; a prospect finds out before we do.\n\n## Evidence\n- #2118 acceptance was a one-shot run\n- Harness smoke runners exist: #2272 (baseline), #2297 (drift), #2298 (phase-2)\n- `digitalmodel/examples/demos/gtm/` is not covered\n\n## Scope\n- Extend #2298 pattern to the 5 GTM demos in `--from-cache` mode (fast, per-PR) and full-calc mode (weekly cron)\n- Publish HTML render diff to catch chart breakage\n- Emit `gtm-demo-health` signal to dashboard\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] CI runs all 5 on every PR touching `digitalmodel/` or `examples/demos/gtm/`\n- [ ] Full-calc weekly cron verified\n- [ ] Broken demo fails build with diff artifact\n\n## Related\n- #2272, #2297, #2298, #2118, #2087, #1832","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2345","display_title":"feat(gtm): wire GTM demos into unified smoke runner — prevent silent demo rot"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2349","title":"docs(gtm): refresh 30-day plan — #1809 closed, update dependency table + Day-7 checkpoint","issue_number":2349,"body":"## Summary\n`docs/gtm/gtm-plan-30day.md` lists #1809 as a Week-1 dependency. #1809 closed 2026-04-15 and workflow GIFs (#2288) landed. Plan doc still stale.\n\n## Evidence\n- Plan line 184: \"GIF recordings need all 5 demos running clean | #1809\"\n- `gh issue view 1809` → CLOSED 2026-04-15\n- Day-7 checkpoint items not updated\n\n## Scope\n- Strike #1809 from Dependencies; replace with \"verify workflow GIFs embedded on aceengineer.com\"\n- Mark Day-7 items ✓/pending/blocked\n- Date-stamp plan revision\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Dependencies table reflects 2026-04-17 reality\n- [ ] Day-7 items statused\n- [ ] Revision date updated\n\n## Related\n- #1809, #2288, companion checkpoint-dashboard issue","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2349","display_title":"docs(gtm): refresh 30-day plan — #1809 closed, update dependency table + Day-7 checkpoint"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2350","title":"verify: #2043 mooring animation render outputs — confirm published or reopen","issue_number":2350,"body":"## Summary\n#2043 closed with Manim scene script but acceptance also required rendered GIF + MP4 and README update. Script exists; render and publish status are unverified.\n\n## Evidence\n- `scripts/animations/scenes/mooring_layout.py` present\n- `__pycache__/mooring_layout.cpython-312.pyc` (ran at least once)\n- Rendered outputs not found under `docs/gtm/media/` or `aceengineer-website/content/`\n\n## Scope\n- Check build output directories for rendered artifacts\n- If present: confirm publish path and link from gallery / mooring page\n- If absent: reopen #2043 or open finish-the-render follow-up\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Render artifacts located or rebuilt\n- [ ] Published or explicitly deferred\n- [ ] #2043 closure matches reality\n\n## Related\n- #2035, #2115","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2350","display_title":"verify: #2043 mooring animation render outputs — confirm published or reopen"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2351","title":"feat(gtm): Day-7/14/21/30 checkpoint dashboard — surface plan metrics for weekly review","issue_number":2351,"body":"## Summary\nThe 30-day GTM plan contains checkpoint tables at Day 7/14/21/30 and a Success Metrics table. Nothing surfaces progress against them; no tripwire for \"No paid engagement by Day 30\".\n\n## Evidence\n- `docs/gtm/gtm-plan-30day.md` lines 41-44, 89-94, 117-122, 151-156\n- No tracker issue, no automation, no rollup report\n\n## Scope\n- Choose substrate: (a) long-lived issue with weekly comment updates, or (b) generated `docs/reports/gtm-checkpoint-YYYY-MM-DD.md` on cron\n- Wire sources: outreach log, expert-network count, LinkedIn count, warm-lead count\n- Emit red/green vs Success Metrics table\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Checkpoint tracker exists + populated\n- [ ] Weekly cadence set\n- [ ] Day-30 rollup produces go/no-go against plan decision points\n\n## Related\n- #2016, companion 30-day plan refresh issue","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2351","display_title":"feat(gtm): Day-7/14/21/30 checkpoint dashboard — surface plan metrics for weekly review"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2355","title":"chore(website): pin Node engines in aceengineer-website package.json + vercel.json","issue_number":2355,"body":"## Summary\nThe `aceengineer-website/package.json` has no `engines` field and `vercel.json` does not pin a Node runtime version. This leaves the build environment implicit and susceptible to silent drift when Vercel's default Node image changes.\n\n## Why accepted as debt (not blocker)\nFrom the approved plan's Known Minor Debt table (row G): the current Vercel default Node 20 build works today, so this is a forward-looking resiliency fix rather than a regression. The existing demo-detail-pages rollout in #2342/#2343 does not depend on a specific Node version, so pinning was deferred to avoid widening the PR scope.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=20.x <21\" }` (or chosen range) to `aceengineer-website/package.json`.\n- Add a matching Node runtime pin to `aceengineer-website/vercel.json` (e.g. `\"build\": { \"env\": { \"NODE_VERSION\": \"20\" } }` or the equivalent supported Vercel schema).\n- Confirm local `npm install` and `vercel build` still succeed with the pin.\n- Document the chosen Node range in the repo README or build docs.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `package.json` contains an `engines.node` field with an explicit range.\n- [ ] `vercel.json` pins the matching Node major version.\n- [ ] A Vercel preview build completes green with the pin applied.\n- [ ] A brief note in docs/README explains the pinning rationale and how to bump it.\n\n## Parent / context\n- Approved plan: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-17-issue-2342-2343-demo-detail-pages.md\n- Documented in plan's \"Known Minor Debt\" section as row G\n- Related: #2342, #2343 (parent GTM issues)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2355","display_title":"chore(website): pin Node engines in aceengineer-website package.json + vercel.json"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2356","title":"feat(ci): add GH Actions workflow to run npm test on aceengineer-website PRs","issue_number":2356,"body":"## Summary\n`aceengineer-website/` has no GitHub Actions workflow under `.github/workflows/`. The Jest link-check suite runs only locally via `npm test`, so PRs can merge without automated verification that internal links resolve.\n\n## Why accepted as debt (not blocker)\nFrom the approved plan's Known Minor Debt table (row CI-1): the link-check tests are already written, passing locally, and were executed by the author during the #2342/#2343 implementation. CI wiring is a harness improvement independent of the demo-detail-pages content itself, and adding a workflow in the same PR would have expanded scope beyond the plan-approved work.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `aceengineer-website/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (or equivalent path honored by the repo's actions routing).\n- Workflow should trigger on `pull_request` affecting `aceengineer-website/**` and on `push` to `main`.\n- Steps: checkout, setup-node (matching the engines pin from the sibling issue once landed), `npm ci`, `npm test`.\n- Make the job required for merge on PRs touching the website tree.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] A workflow file exists at `aceengineer-website/.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n- [ ] The workflow runs `npm ci && npm test` on PRs changing `aceengineer-website/**`.\n- [ ] A sample PR shows the job executing green.\n- [ ] Branch protection / ruleset marks the job required for website PRs.\n\n## Parent / context\n- Approved plan: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-17-issue-2342-2343-demo-detail-pages.md\n- Documented in plan's \"Known Minor Debt\" section as row CI-1\n- Related: #2342, #2343 (parent GTM issues)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2356","display_title":"feat(ci): add GH Actions workflow to run npm test on aceengineer-website PRs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1994","title":"[WRK] Register for GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint expert networks","issue_number":1994,"body":"## Context\n\nExpert networks are the HIGHEST ROI ad-hoc income channel. Zero application hassle vs. full job applications. 1-hour phone consultations with hedge funds, PE firms, law firms about offshore/marine engineering topics. Your 23yr PE + OrcaFlex + Chevron + BP background is exactly what they seek.\n\n## Platforms to Register\n\n### 1. GLG (Gerson Lehrman Group)\n- URL: glg.it\n- Rate: $150-$1,000+/hr (typical $300-600 for offshore PE expertise)\n- Fee: Zero to expert (client pays GLG, GLG pays you)\n- Non-exclusive\n- Action: Create expert profile highlighting 23yr subsea/offshore, Chevron 16yr, PE license\n\n### 2. AlphaSights\n- URL: alphasights.com\n- Rate: $150-$500/hr\n- Fee: Zero to expert\n- Non-exclusive\n- Action: Create expert profile\n\n### 3. Guidepoint\n- URL: guidepoint.com/experts\n- Rate: $100-$500/hr\n- Fee: Zero to expert\n- Non-exclusive\n- Action: Create expert profile\n\n## Positioning Statement (for all 3)\n\n> Subsea Engineering VP/Principal PE with 23 years experience at Chevron, BP, ExxonMobil projects. Expertise: offshore riser/pipeline/mooring design, FEED/pre-FEED, OrcaFlex/AQWA/ANSYS, digital twins/automation. Former BP Macondo emergency response engineering manager. API standards committee member (API-RP-16Q). GoM deepwater specialist.\n\n## Topics You Can Consult On\n- Offshore/subsea oil & gas engineering and economics\n- Mooring and riser system design for deepwater\n- OrcaFlex/AQWA hydrodynamic analysis\n- BP Macondo containment design and emergency response\n- LNG terminal marine mooring design (current: WoodFibre LNG $1.8B)\n- GoM deepwater development economics\n- Offshore installation analysis and vessel operations\n- Python/automation in subsea engineering\n- Digital twins for offshore asset management\n\n## Tasks\n- [ ] Register at glg.it as expert\n- [ ] Register at alphasights.com as expert\n- [ ] Register at guidepoint.com/experts as expert\n- [ ] Document registration status and expert profile URLs\n- [ ] Note: ExpertVoice (expertvoice.com) should be SKIPPED — not a consulting platform\n\n## Notes\n- ExpertVoice is NOT a consulting platform — it is a product discount/advocacy site\n- All 3 expert networks are non-exclusive — sign up for all\n- Use ACE Engineer Consulting as entity for professional liability/tax purposes\n- PE license = major differentiator; display prominently\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1994","display_title":"[WRK] Register for GLG, AlphaSights, Guidepoint expert networks"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/191","title":"WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals — shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)","issue_number":191,"body":"## WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals — shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\n\n**Repo:** ['frontierdeepwater', 'TBD-client2-repo'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nCreate a shared `ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md` document and embed\npersona/tone standards into ALL client system prompts (WRK-625, WRK-629).\n\nSource: `~/Downloads/Engineering_Chatbot_Pitch_OilGas.md`\n\n### 1. Shared Fundamentals File\n\n`ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md`\n\n#### Persona Design Principles (apply to ALL system prompts)\n\nEvery system prompt (rigid jumper, pipeline, structural/diffraction, maritime legal)\nmust embed these four principles as a closing `## Persona and Tone` section:\n\n```markdown\n\n### Why\n\nTone and persona consistency across all clients is the difference between a demo that\nfeels like a toy and one that feels like a senior engineer. The four principles\n(precision, practicality, caution, transparency) + the standard disclaimer protect\nagainst the two biggest objections: \"can we trust this?\" and \"who's liable?\".\n\nThe client pitch one-pager turns the demo follow-up into a structured commercial\nconversation rather than an ad-hoc explanation.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] `ai-initiatives/shared/chatbot_fundamentals.md` created with all 4 sections\n- [ ] `ai-initiatives/shared/client_pitch_oilgas.md` created (adapted from source, no names)\n- [ ] `## Persona and Tone` section present in all 4 system prompt files\n- [ ] `## Known Limitations` section present in all 4 system prompt files\n- [ ] Standard disclaimer wording consistent across all prompts\n- [ ] Legal scan passes (source doc is internal — no client names in output files)\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/191","display_title":"WRK-632: feat(frontierdeepwater): chatbot fundamentals — shared persona, tone, tiers, pitch template (all clients)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2035","title":"feat(gtm): manim-based engineering explainer pipeline","issue_number":2035,"body":"## Summary\nBuild a Manim-based engineering explainer pipeline that turns key engineering analyses into reusable animated assets for GTM, demos, and public-facing technical content.\n\n## Why\nThe reviewed Hermes+Manim video confirms a capability that fits our ecosystem well: animated explainers are a strong bridge from technical depth to client-facing clarity.\n\nWe already have GTM demos and static HTML reporting. The next step is to add a reusable animation workflow for selected flagship engineering examples.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a first-pass engineering animation pipeline that:\n1. identifies 2-3 flagship scenarios\n2. defines reusable animation patterns/templates\n3. generates at least one working Manim explainer from repo data or representative fixtures\n4. documents how to reproduce/adapt it for future demos and outreach\n\n## Candidate flagship scenarios\n- catenary / lazy-wave riser geometry evolution\n- mooring layout / force or excursion explainer\n- installation sequence or vessel-operability envelope\n- report companion animation for a GTM demo\n\n## Deliverables\n- animation workflow docs and file layout\n- at least one complete Manim explainer checked into repo\n- template structure for future engineering animations\n- rendered output suitable for website/outreach/demo reuse\n- issue comment summarizing what was produced and where to extend next\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One complete engineering animation pipeline implemented and documented\n- [ ] At least one rendered animation artifact produced from a real or representative engineering scenario\n- [ ] Templates/patterns defined so future scenarios are faster to add\n- [ ] Clear link established to GTM demo/report pipeline\n- [ ] Follow-on work linked to #1809, #2016, and #2022 as appropriate\n\n## Related\n- #1809 GTM: Create .gif screencasts of all 5 demo reports running\n- #2016 feat(gtm): client conversion pipeline\n- #2022 feat: publish repo knowledge bases as aceengineer.com content\n- docs/notes/2026-04-08-youtube-hermes-opportunities.md\n\n## Execution notes for Claude Code\n- Start by picking the single highest-signal scenario; do not boil the ocean.\n- Optimize for reusable engineering storytelling, not generic motion graphics.\n- Prefer artifacts that can feed README/site/outreach collateral.\n- End by documenting exact commands, asset paths, and next candidate animations.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2035","display_title":"feat(gtm): manim-based engineering explainer pipeline"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2117","title":"feat(gtm): resume + cover letter generator for Rigzone applications (#1993)","issue_number":2117,"body":"## Purpose\nAutomate resume tailoring for offshore engineering job applications. Vamsee applies to Rigzone positions not to get hired but to generate consulting conversations.\n\n## Deliverable\ndocs/gtm/resume-templates/\n\nContents:\n1. **base-resume.md** — master resume (23yr P.E., all domains, key projects)\n2. **cover-letter-template.md** — fill-in-the-blank per position\n3. **tailoring-guide.md** — which sections to emphasize per job type:\n   - Subsea installation → OrcaFlex, marine ops, DNV-RP-H103\n   - Pipeline integrity → wall thickness, VIV, on-bottom stability\n   - Mooring/riser → OrcaFlex, fatigue, API RP 2SK\n   - Structural → FEA, API 579, cathodic protection\n\n## Related\n- #1993 — Rigzone application pipeline\n- docs/gtm/oil-man-persona.md (informs positioning)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2117","display_title":"feat(gtm): resume + cover letter generator for Rigzone applications (#1993)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2114","title":"feat(gtm): VIV demo notebook — freespan walkthrough for pipeline engineers (#1792)","issue_number":2114,"body":"## Purpose\nCreate a Jupyter notebook walkthrough of Demo 1 (freespan/VIV) for pipeline engineers. Like the S-N notebook but focused on span assessment workflow.\n\n## Content\n1. DNV-RP-F105 methodology overview\n2. Natural frequency calculation walkthrough\n3. Reduced velocity and VIV onset screening\n4. Gap ratio effects on allowable span\n5. Interactive allowable span map (Plotly)\n6. Pipe size comparison — when to upsize for span tolerance\n\n## Prerequisite\n- Demo 1 results exist (done)\n- Free span modules exist (done)\n\n## Deliverable\ndocs/notebooks/freespan-viv-demo.ipynb\n\n## Related\n- #1792 — original freespan notebook request\n- Demo 1 script (demo_01_dnv_freespan_viv.py)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2114","display_title":"feat(gtm): VIV demo notebook — freespan walkthrough for pipeline engineers (#1792)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2038","title":"feat(gtm): manim installation sequence / operability envelope animation","issue_number":2038,"body":"## Summary\nBuild the third Manim engineering explainer: offshore installation sequence with vessel operability envelope.\n\n## Why\nFollow-on from #2035 (catenary riser explainer). Installation planning and weather window analysis are high-value consulting deliverables. Animating a subsea lift sequence with go/no-go weather limits demonstrates operational engineering capability.\n\n## Scope\nUsing the reusable template from #2035:\n1. Implement operability envelope calculations (Hs vs Tp limits, crane capacity curves)\n2. Build Manim scene showing a subsea installation sequence (vessel approach, crane deploy, lower-to-seabed)\n3. Animate weather window overlay — green/red zones on scatter diagram\n4. Include operability callout (e.g., % weather window availability)\n\n## Data sources\n- Vessel data from #1798 (HLV specs) and #1799 (pipelay specs) when available\n- Representative crane capacity and weather scatter data\n\n## Deliverables\n- [ ] Operability math module with tests\n- [ ] Complete Manim scene with four-phase structure\n- [ ] GIF + MP4 renders\n- [ ] Issue comment with assets and commands\n\n## Depends on\n- #2035 — pipeline and template (DONE)\n- #1798, #1799 — vessel data (nice-to-have, can use representative values)\n\n## Related\n- #1809 — GIF screencasts\n- #2016 — client conversion pipeline","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2038","display_title":"feat(gtm): manim installation sequence / operability envelope animation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2037","title":"feat(gtm): manim mooring layout / force explainer animation","issue_number":2037,"body":"## Summary\nBuild the second Manim engineering explainer: mooring layout with force/excursion visualization.\n\n## Why\nFollow-on from #2035 (catenary riser explainer). Mooring systems are a core ACE capability and visually compelling — spread mooring patterns, chain catenary shapes, and vessel excursion envelopes tell a complete engineering story.\n\n## Scope\nUsing the reusable template from #2035 (`scripts/animations/scenes/template.py`):\n1. Implement mooring geometry calculations (spread pattern, chain catenary, pretension)\n2. Build Manim scene showing vessel excursion under environmental loading\n3. Animate mooring line tension changes as vessel offsets\n4. Include code check callout (e.g., maximum line tension vs MBL)\n\n## Data sources\n- `knowledge/seeds/mooring-failures-lng-terminals.yaml` — real failure cases for context\n- Representative 4-point or 8-point spread mooring configuration\n\n## Deliverables\n- [ ] Mooring math module with tests\n- [ ] Complete Manim scene with four-phase structure\n- [ ] GIF + MP4 renders\n- [ ] Issue comment with assets and commands\n\n## Related\n- #2035 — parent pipeline (DONE)\n- #1809 — GIF screencasts\n- #2016 — client conversion pipeline\n- #2022 — aceengineer.com content","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2037","display_title":"feat(gtm): manim mooring layout / force explainer animation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1993","title":"[WRK] Rigzone job application pipeline — resume tailoring and submission","issue_number":1993,"body":"## Context\n\nScraped and scored 13 Rigzone job postings against Vamsee's profile (23yr PE, offshore/subsea, Chevron 16yr, Python/digital transformation). Chevron Project Manager III (R000065929) was the best fit at 9/10 but confirmed EXPIRED on careers.chevron.com.\n\n## Top Candidates to Track\n\n| Rank | Title | Company | Fit | Status |\n|------|-------|---------|-----|--------|\n| 1 | Project Manager III | Chevron | 9/10 | EXPIRED (confirmed) |\n| 2 | Surface Facilities Assurance Supervisor–Sr Manager | Occidental | 8/10 | Status unknown |\n| 3 | Director, Midstream Facilities | Cheniere | 7/10 | Status unknown |\n| 4 | Regulatory Consultant (CONTRACT) | Wood Group | 6/10 | Status unknown |\n| 5 | Artificial Lift Systems Engr Sr/Pr | Occidental | 5/10 | Status unknown |\n\nAll postings were from Jan 22 – Feb 3, 2026. It is now April 6.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Check if Occidental R12978 (Surface Facilities Assurance) is still live at oxy.com/careers\n- [ ] Check if Chevron R12988 (Surface Analyst) is still live\n- [ ] Check if Cheniere 2026-2012 (Director Midstream) is still live at careers.cheniere.com\n- [ ] Resolve merge conflict in teamresumes/cv/va_resume.md\n- [ ] Create tailored resume versions for each live opening\n- [ ] Generate brief application statements / cover letters\n- [ ] Document actual apply URLs for each active posting\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- `teamresumes/cv/tailored/` — directory with company-specific resume variants\n- `docs/strategy/gtm/job-applications/` — cover letters and application tracking\n- Application status dashboard\n\n## Reference\n\nSession summary: `~/notes/rigzone-job-pipeline-2026-04-06.md`\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1993","display_title":"[WRK] Rigzone job application pipeline — resume tailoring and submission"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1792","title":"feat(freespan): GTM demo notebook — free-span VIV assessment walkthrough","issue_number":1792,"body":"## Context\n\nThe DNV-RP-F105 free-span VIV module is now complete with 93 passing tests.\nA Jupyter notebook demonstrating the full workflow would serve as:\n1. GTM demo material for prospective clients\n2. Validation documentation for the module\n3. Quick-start guide for engineers\n\n## Notebook Scope\n\n### Section 1: Pipeline Input Definition\n- Define a 10\" pipeline span (OD=0.2731m, WT=0.0127m, L=34m)\n- Show PipeSpanInput dataclass with all parameters\n\n### Section 2: Natural Frequency Calculation\n- Compute fn_IL, fn_CF with boundary condition comparison\n- Plot fn vs span length (parametric sweep)\n\n### Section 3: VIV Onset Screening\n- Show screening check at design current\n- Visualize onset boundary (Ur vs Vr_onset)\n\n### Section 4: VIV Amplitude & Fatigue\n- Compute IL/CF amplitudes and stresses\n- Show bilinear S-N curve (F-class, air vs seawater_cp)\n- Calculate fatigue life\n\n### Section 5: Current Profile & Weibull Extrapolation\n- 5-bin current profile → Weibull fit → 100-year current\n- Plot exceedance probability vs current speed\n\n### Section 6: Full Assessment\n- FreespanVIVFatigue facade end-to-end\n- Results summary table\n- Allowable span length\n\n### Section 7: Parametric Study\n- Span length sweep → fatigue life curve\n- Wall thickness sensitivity\n- Current velocity sensitivity\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Self-contained Jupyter notebook\n- [ ] All cells execute without errors\n- [ ] Plotly or matplotlib visualizations\n- [ ] No client-specific or deny-list content\n- [ ] Placed in `digitalmodel/docs/domains/pipelines/freespan/`\n\n## Related\n- Parent: #1773 (closed), #1783 (closed)\n- Uses: all free_span modules\n- GTM: aceengineer-strategy/ demo inventory\n- Related: #1692 (S-N curve library demo)","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1792","display_title":"feat(freespan): GTM demo notebook — free-span VIV assessment walkthrough"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/197","title":"WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset","issue_number":197,"body":"## WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\n### Phase 1 — Commit guide to workspace-hub (30 min)\n\nCopy the guide into the repository so it is version-controlled and accessible\nfrom any machine:\n\n```\ndocs/agents/narada-openclaw-setup-guide.md\n```\n\nStrip personal identifiers (user home paths, API key examples) and replace with\ngeneric placeholders / env-var references before committing. Run legal scan to\nconfirm no client references.\n\n### Phase 2 — Create `automation/narada-openclaw` skill (1–2 h)\n\nPath: `.claude/skills/automation/narada-openclaw/SKILL.md`\n\nCapability sections:\n- `install` — reproduce Phase I end-to-end from guide\n- `add_workspace` — clone an existing agent workspace for a new channel\n  (e.g., GitHub assistant variant)\n- `channel_whatsapp` — QR pair, reconnect, rotate session\n- `channel_github` — configure GitHub webhook channel (future)\n- `model_config` — swap underlying model (Claude / GPT-4.1 / Gemini)\n- `debug` — common failure modes: QR timeout, build errors, agent not responding\n- `backup_restore` — QMD memory snapshot + restore procedure\n\nTrigger: manual, invoked during new agent deployment or channel rotation.\n\nRelated skills: `automation/session-memory`, `agents/agent-spawning`\n\n### Phase 3 — GitHub assistant quick-start (optional, 30 min)\n\nExtract the \"Part III: Replication\" section into a dedicated file:\n\n```\ndocs/agents/narada-github-assistant-quickstart.md\n```\n\nCovers only the delta from the full guide — assumes OpenClaw already installed,\nfocuses on workspace cloning and GitHub channel configuration.\n\n### Why\n\n- The guide is currently in a local home directory only — one machine wipe loses it\n- A skill makes the setup reproducible by any Claude agent session on any machine\n- The GitHub assistant variant is a high-value extension: turns Narada into a\n  code-aware bot that responds in GitHub issue/PR comments via webhook\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] `docs/agents/narada-openclaw-setup-guide.md` committed (no personal paths,\n- [ ] `.claude/skills/automation/narada-openclaw/SKILL.md` created with ≤20 line\n- [ ] `docs/agents/narada-github-assistant-quickstart.md` created (replication\n- [ ] Legal scan passes on all three files\n- [ ] Skill registered in skill index if one exists\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **14. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **15. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **16. User Review** — done\n- [ ] **17. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **18. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **19. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/197","display_title":"WRK-665: docs(narada): capture OpenClaw/WhatsApp AI agent setup guide as replicable workspace asset"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/108","title":"WRK-148: ACE-GTM: A&CE Go-to-Market strategy stream","issue_number":108,"body":"## WRK-148: ACE-GTM: A&CE Go-to-Market strategy stream\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 17: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** high | **Category:** business | **Subcategory:** gtm\n\n**Repo:** ['aceengineer-website', 'aceengineer-strategy', 'workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** complex | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nParent work item for all A&CE go-to-market activity. This is a **running stream** — new findings, recommendations, and action items get added here as the strategy evolves. Child items get spun off for execution.\n\n### Why\n\nRevenue is oxygen. The engineering substance is strong but the packaging, positioning, and pipeline don't exist yet. This stream coordinates all work to fix that.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] All child items (WRK-142, 146, 147) completed\n- [ ] Website repositioned with firm voice\n- [ ] Business strategy repo operational with weekly scorecard habit\n- [ ] At least 1 outbound experiment launched\n- [ ] Pipeline has 5+ qualified prospects\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- 