{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:cat:documentation","sort":"updated","order":"desc","topn":30},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\", \"issue_number\": 2269, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\\n\\nPart of #1782.\\nPrimary reference: #25.\\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\\n\\nExpected deliverables:\\n- baseline docs\\n- run/validation entrypoints\\n- minimal smoke example\\n- troubleshooting guidance\\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\\n\\n## Notes\\nImplementation should prefer:\\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"display_title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\", \"issue_number\": 2657, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\\n\\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\\n\\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\\n\\nReads:\\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\\n- `github.github-issues`\\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\\n\\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\\n\\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\\n\\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\\n\\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"display_title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312\", \"title\": \"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority\", \"issue_number\": 2312, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nClaude continues to read removed local work-queue lifecycle scripts even though GitHub issues and `.planning/` are now the authoritative work-tracking surfaces:\\n\\n- `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh` \\u2014 94 reads\\n- `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh` \\u2014 62 reads\\n- `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh` \\u2014 60 reads\\n- 216 total remediation-mapped stale reads in the latest provider-session ecosystem audit\\n\\nThis indicates parts of the repo ecosystem still imply that local queue lifecycle scripts are canonical, which wastes session budget and weakens the GitHub-first workflow.\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nRemove remaining live references that teach agents to use the deleted local lifecycle scripts, and replace them with current queue-authority surfaces.\\n\\n## Canonical redirect targets\\n\\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.py`\\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.sh`\\n- `notes/agent-work-queue.md`\\n- `.planning/`\\n- GitHub issues\\n- `docs/work-queue-workflow.md`\\n- `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Find live docs, prompts, templates, and routing instructions that still reference:\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh`\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh`\\n   - `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh`\\n2. Update those surfaces so they describe GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh scripts as the authoritative workflow.\\n3. Expand stale-reference regression coverage where needed so deleted lifecycle-script references stay confined to explicit legacy/reference docs.\\n4. Refresh the provider-session ecosystem audit after cleanup.\\n\\n## Existing related issues\\n\\n- #1717 \\u2014 policy/docs contradiction between GitHub issues and legacy work-queue guidance\\n- #2213 \\u2014 expand strict stale-reference enforcement across more live docs\\n- #2214 \\u2014 split current architecture guidance from legacy wrapper redirects\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Live instructional surfaces no longer reference the deleted lifecycle scripts\\n- [ ] Current queue authority is documented as GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh helpers\\n- [ ] Regression tests cover the deleted lifecycle-script references in protected live docs/templates\\n- [ ] Provider-session ecosystem audit is refreshed after cleanup and linked from the issue\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n- `analysis/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.json`\\n- `docs/reports/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.md`\\n- Audit timestamp: `2026-04-16T23:34:23Z`\\n- Reference doc: `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312\", \"display_title\": \"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\", \"issue_number\": 2643, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\\n\\n## Context\\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\\n\\nLive prerequisite checks found:\\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\\n\\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\\n\\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\\n\\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\\n\\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\", \"issue_number\": 2626, \"body\": \"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\\n\\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\\n\\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\\n\\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\\n\\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\\nScenario 3 suggests \\\"temporary lift of interaction limit\\\" \\u2014 globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\\n\\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\\n\\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\\n\\n## Severity\\n\\nMedium \\u2014 the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"display_title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2552\", \"title\": \"docs(security): external contributor and unsolicited paid-help response runbook\", \"issue_number\": 2552, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nCreate a concise policy/runbook for handling non-collaborator comments, unsolicited paid-help offers, and external contributor requests on public repos.\\n\\n## Why\\nIssue #2546 was triggered by an outside commenter offering paid implementation help on #2401. The technical lockdown is now in place for public repos, but operators still need a repeatable response path for existing comments, future exceptions, legitimate contributors, and paid external execution requests.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Document when to ignore, hide, report, or reply to external comments.\\n- Define how to route legitimate contributor requests without granting broad access.\\n- Define paid-pilot intake requirements: scope, NDA/confidentiality, repo access level, payment approval, and PR review gate.\\n- Add a short issue-comment template for declining or redirecting unsolicited offers.\\n- Link the policy from the security/governance docs or ops runbook.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Runbook covers unsolicited paid-help comments, spam, legitimate contributor requests, and collaborator onboarding.\\n- [ ] Runbook preserves public-repo security posture: no collaborator access without explicit owner approval.\\n- [ ] Templates avoid engaging suspicious accounts while keeping legitimate contributors routed through a safe process.\\n- [ ] Documentation references #2546 and #2401 as the triggering example.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Trigger comment context: #2401\\n- Repository interaction lockdown: #2546\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2552\", \"display_title\": \"docs(security): external contributor and unsolicited paid-help response runbook\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2533\", \"title\": \"feat(repo-portfolio): review and revise mission/objective statements across active repos\", \"issue_number\": 2533, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nReview and revise the mission/objective statements across all active workspace repos so future GitHub issue work can quickly answer:\\n\\n1. what is this repo for?\\n2. what work belongs here?\\n3. what work should route elsewhere?\\n4. is the repo active, support-only, client/archive, or deprecated/no-new-issues?\\n\\nThis is the portfolio-wide complement to the Tier-1 routing/indexing work already tracked under vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460-#2465.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe Tier-1 contract now improves code placement and routing, but the portfolio still needs a canonical mission/objective layer across all active repos. Without that layer, agents can still mis-route issues between overlapping repos such as:\\n\\n- `workspace-hub` vs per-repo execution docs\\n- `assetutilities` vs repo-specific utilities\\n- `digitalmodel` vs client/project verticals\\n- `investments` vs `assethold`\\n- `client_projects` vs client-specific repos\\n- active engineering repos vs archives/reference repos\\n\\n## Initial repo scope\\n\\nUse `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and live immediate-child git repos as the starting inventory.\\n\\n### Tier-1\\n\\n- `workspace-hub`\\n- `digitalmodel`\\n- `assetutilities`\\n- `aceengineer-website`\\n\\n### Tier-2\\n\\n- `OGManufacturing`\\n- `acma-projects`\\n- `frontierdeepwater`\\n- `seanation`\\n- `worldenergydata`\\n- `investments`\\n- `rock-oil-field`\\n\\n### Tier-3 / support / archive candidates\\n\\n- `aceengineer-admin`\\n- `aceengineer-strategy`\\n- `achantas-data`\\n- `achantas-media`\\n- `assethold`\\n- `client_projects`\\n- `doris`\\n- `hobbies`\\n- `pdf-large-reader` if present/active\\n- `sabithaandkrishnaestates`\\n- `saipem`\\n- `sd-work`\\n- `teamresumes`\\n- `CAD-DEVELOPMENTS` if confirmed active in this workspace\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Canonical portfolio mission/objective artifact, preferably `docs/REPO_MISSION_PORTFOLIO.md` or an equivalent linked from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\\n2. Per-repo classification:\\n   - active product/library\\n   - client vertical\\n   - business/admin support\\n   - archive/reference\\n   - deprecated / no-new-issues\\n3. Per-repo mission/objective statement grounded in the strongest available source:\\n   - `.agent-os/product/mission.md`\\n   - `README.md`\\n   - `AGENTS.md`\\n   - `docs/README.md`\\n   - existing workspace-hub portfolio docs\\n4. Per-repo routing rule:\\n   - \\\"work belongs here when...\\\"\\n   - \\\"work should route elsewhere when...\\\"\\n5. Conflict/dedupe notes for overlapping repo missions.\\n6. Update links from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and/or `docs/ROUTING_INDEX.md` so the mission artifact is discoverable.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Every active repo in `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` has a current mission/objective row.\\n- [ ] Every immediate-child local git repo not listed in `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` is either added, explicitly excluded, or marked as inventory drift.\\n- [ ] Each row has a source path proving where the mission came from.\\n- [ ] Each row has an activity/status classification.\\n- [ ] Each row has an issue-routing rule for work that belongs vs work that should route elsewhere.\\n- [ ] Overlapping missions are explicitly called out and resolved or marked for follow-up.\\n- [ ] Tier-1 mission/objective rows are consistent with vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 and its child routing issues (#2461-#2465).\\n- [ ] The artifact is linked from a canonical workspace discovery surface.\\n- [ ] The plan receives adversarial review before implementation.\\n\\n## Suggested execution waves\\n\\n1. Wave 1: Tier-1 mission alignment and consistency with vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460-#2465.\\n2. Wave 2: Tier-2 repo mission/objective review.\\n3. Wave 3: Tier-3/support/archive classification and no-new-issues guidance.\\n4. Wave 4: final portfolio table integration, dedupe/conflict notes, and discoverability links.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent/umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1962\\n- Tier-1 structure epic: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2397\\n- LLM-wiki roadmap context: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13\\n- Tier-1 routing contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460\\n- Tier-1 child issues: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465\\n\\n## Planning requirements\\n\\nFollow the normal issue gate:\\n\\nIssue \\u2192 resource intelligence \\u2192 canonical plan in `docs/plans/` \\u2192 adversarial plan review \\u2192 `status:plan-review` \\u2192 user approval \\u2192 `status:plan-approved` \\u2192 implementation.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2533\", \"display_title\": \"feat(repo-portfolio): review and revise mission/objective statements across active repos\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2553\", \"title\": \"docs(repo-portfolio): reconcile repository overview docs after mission review\", \"issue_number\": 2553, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nReconcile the remaining portfolio/context documentation after the mission-document review wave and Business Brain update.\\n\\nThe mission review updated multiple per-repo mission documents and `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`. The remaining portfolio docs should be reviewed next so they do not preserve stale repo counts, stale tiering, or legacy `.agent-os/product/*` authority language.\\n\\n## Scope\\nReview and update, at minimum:\\n- `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_REPOSITORY_OVERVIEW.md`\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-21-repo-mission-revision-sequence.md`\\n- Any linked docs index entries that still imply stale repo mission authority or outdated repository classifications.\\n\\n## Source context\\n- Parent/current review issue: #2533\\n- Business Brain refresh issue: #2549\\n- Machine/provider dispatch inventory issue: #2548\\n- Current authoritative review state: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` after the 2026-04-28 mission/business-brain review wave.\\n\\n## Requirements\\n- Do not duplicate #2533's canonical portfolio artifact work.\\n- Treat this as a documentation reconciliation follow-up: align overview/report docs with the already-reviewed mission and Business Brain corrections.\\n- Preserve private/client confidentiality; do not expose sensitive project details in public issue comments or docs.\\n- Explicitly mark archive/extraction candidates consistently with the Business Brain: `investments`, `rock-oil-field`, `seanation`, and `saipem`.\\n- Keep `ace-linux-1` / Hermes control-plane and `licensed-win-1` OrcaFlex/AQWA dispatch assumptions consistent with #2548 and `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_REPOSITORY_OVERVIEW.md` no longer conflicts with the updated Business Brain repo classifications.\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-21-repo-mission-revision-sequence.md` either reflects the completed review wave or is clearly marked historical/superseded.\\n- Any remaining stale mission-authority references are either corrected, linked to #2533, or explicitly marked as legacy/historical.\\n- Changes are reviewed under the normal plan-gated documentation workflow before implementation if scope grows beyond direct doc reconciliation.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2553\", \"display_title\": \"docs(repo-portfolio): reconcile repository overview docs after mission review\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2549\", \"title\": \"chore(business-brain): periodically assess repo work and refresh ecosystem context\", \"issue_number\": 2549, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nBusiness Brain is the ecosystem's single-file onboarding source, but substantial work is happening across repositories. We need a recurring/readable assessment workflow that reviews completed repo work and updates Business Brain so repo classifications, provider accounts, machine inventory, and archive/retirement candidates do not go stale.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Assess recent GitHub issues/PRs and repo mission changes across active repos.\\n- Reconcile repo mission/objective updates into `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and future `docs/REPO_MISSION_PORTFOLIO.md` if applicable.\\n- Update archive/extraction candidates and retirement targets after repo-specific migration issues progress.\\n- Refresh AI provider account assumptions, including current Codex-only $200 paid account state.\\n- Refresh machine/software/auth inventory summary after machine readiness work lands.\\n- Keep the document concise (<200 lines) and link out to detailed registries/reports.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Business Brain reflects current repo work and no longer relies on stale provider/machine assumptions.\\n- A checklist or scriptable workflow exists for periodic Business Brain refresh from issues/PRs/repo missions.\\n- Updates link to evidence where details exceed the Business Brain line budget.\\n- Parent/related issues are linked so future agents know when to update the Brain.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2549\", \"display_title\": \"chore(business-brain): periodically assess repo work and refresh ecosystem context\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2548\", \"title\": \"feat(control-plane): inventory machine software/auth and dispatch OrcaFlex/AQWA runs to licensed-win-1\", \"issue_number\": 2548, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nBusiness Brain now records that `ace-linux-1` is the Hermes control plane and that work should be dispatchable to other machines. We need a durable machine/software inventory and dispatch readiness surface, starting with OrcaFlex and AQWA runs on `licensed-win-1`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Build/maintain inventory for all machines: installed programs, licensed software, AI-provider auth state, repo checkout roots, run/smoke-test commands, and dispatch readiness.\\n- Keep `ace-linux-1` as the primary Hermes control plane for GitHub mutation, provider routing, dispatch ledgers, and reconciliation.\\n- Verify all AI providers are authenticated on machines where practical; record gaps rather than assuming readiness.\\n- Establish `licensed-win-1` as initial licensed engineering worker for OrcaFlex and AQWA runs.\\n- Define dispatch/smoke-test commands for OrcaFlex and AQWA from `ace-linux-1` to `licensed-win-1`.\\n- Record evidence in a durable report or registry linked from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Machine inventory exists and covers all known machines from Business Brain.\\n- `licensed-win-1` has verified OrcaFlex and AQWA availability or explicit blockers.\\n- AI-provider auth state is recorded per machine.\\n- At least one dry-run/smoke workflow is documented for dispatching OrcaFlex/AQWA runs from Hermes on `ace-linux-1`.\\n- Business Brain points to or summarizes the inventory state.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\\n- Control-plane policy: `docs/standards/CONTROL_PLANE_CONTRACT.md`\\n- Portfolio mission review: #2533\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2548\", \"display_title\": \"feat(control-plane): inventory machine software/auth and dispatch OrcaFlex/AQWA runs to licensed-win-1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2547\", \"title\": \"chore(seanation): extract useful client information and archive repo\", \"issue_number\": 2547, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`seanation` belongs to another client and should be treated as a client-specific extraction/archive repository. The objective is to review the repo, extract any useful data or information, preserve context/provenance, migrate reusable artifacts to the appropriate durable destination if needed, and then archive the repo.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Inventory and sanity-check `seanation` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\\n- Classify artifacts as useful data, technical information, analysis context, documents, reusable code, duplicate, archive-only, or discard candidate.\\n- Extract useful client project data/information and preserve provenance/assumptions needed for future interpretation.\\n- Migrate reusable code/data/analysis to the appropriate durable repository after sensitivity review.\\n- Create a no-loss extraction/archive manifest showing what moved where, what remains archived, and why.\\n- Archive `seanation` after useful data/information has been extracted and verified.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Every useful file has a disposition: extracted/migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\\n- Durable reusable artifacts no longer live only in `seanation`.\\n- Final repo state is archived after extraction verification, or blocked with explicit reason.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\\n- Similar archive/migration patterns: #2539 (`rock-oil-field`), #2545 (`saipem`)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2547\", \"display_title\": \"chore(seanation): extract useful client information and archive repo\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2545\", \"title\": \"chore(saipem): extract useful installation-project information and archive or retire repo\", \"issue_number\": 2545, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`saipem` should be treated as a temporary engineering-installation contractor project repository, similar to Rock Oil Field, ACMA, and Doris client/project repositories. The objective is to extract useful Saipem installation-project information, migrate durable code/data/analysis to the appropriate Tier-1 repositories, and archive or retire the repo over time.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Inventory and sanity-check `saipem` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\\n- Classify artifacts as code, data, analysis, technical documentation, reference/context, duplicate, or discard candidate.\\n- Preserve useful offshore installation engineering knowledge, including project context, assumptions, provenance, and progression history.\\n- Migrate reusable engineering methods/calculations/workflows to `digitalmodel` where appropriate.\\n- Migrate reusable utility code/tooling to `assetutilities` where appropriate.\\n- Migrate reusable data workflows or normalized data products to the correct Tier-1 data repo where applicable.\\n- Create a no-loss migration manifest showing what moved where and what was intentionally archived or retained as a pointer.\\n- Archive or retire `saipem` over time once useful information has been migrated and verified.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Every useful file has a disposition: migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\\n- Durable code, data, and analysis no longer live only in `saipem`.\\n- Final repo state is archived/retired if possible, or contains only a minimal pointer/manifest for traceability.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\\n- Similar migration pattern: #2539 (`rock-oil-field`)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2545\", \"display_title\": \"chore(saipem): extract useful installation-project information and archive or retire repo\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2539\", \"title\": \"chore(rock-oil-field): sanity-check and migrate useful code/data/analysis to Tier-1 repos\", \"issue_number\": 2539, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`rock-oil-field` should be treated as a temporary triage/archive repository, not a durable execution home. Sanity-check all code, data, engineering methods, and analysis, then migrate useful artifacts to the appropriate Tier-1 repositories.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Inventory and sanity-check `rock-oil-field` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\\n- Classify artifacts as code, data, analysis, reference/context, duplicate, or discard candidate.\\n- Migrate reusable engineering methods/calculations/workflows to `digitalmodel` where appropriate.\\n- Migrate reusable utility code/tooling to `assetutilities` where appropriate.\\n- Migrate reusable energy data workflows or normalized data products to `worldenergydata` where appropriate.\\n- Preserve useful context, provenance, assumptions, and deal/project progression with a migration manifest.\\n- Retire or reduce `rock-oil-field` to a minimal pointer/manifest after verified no-loss migration.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- Every file has a disposition: migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\\n- Durable code, data, and analysis no longer live only in `rock-oil-field`.\\n- Final repo state is either retired/archived or contains only a minimal migration manifest and routing pointer.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\\n- Large repo/data relocation context may overlap with #1341, but this issue is specifically about Rock Oil Field mission-driven migration to Tier-1 repos.\\n\\n\\n## Archive/retire preference\\n\\n- Preferred end state is to archive or retire `rock-oil-field` if possible after verified no-loss migration.\\n- Keep only a minimal pointer/manifest if a traceability stub is required.\\n- Do not leave this repo as an active long-term home for code, data, or analysis.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2539\", \"display_title\": \"chore(rock-oil-field): sanity-check and migrate useful code/data/analysis to Tier-1 repos\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2537\", \"title\": \"chore(investments): sanity-check and migrate files to assethold or achantasdata\", \"issue_number\": 2537, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nReview the private `investments` repository, sanity check all files, and migrate durable artifacts to the correct long-term home:\\n\\n- analysis/code/model/reporting artifacts -> `assethold`\\n- private/source/reference/deal records -> `achantasdata`\\n- temporary undecided material may remain in `investments` only with an explicit triage marker\\n\\n## Why\\nThe mission review clarified that `investments` should not become a permanent parallel analytics codebase. Reusable investment analytics belong in `assethold`; private source records belong in `achantasdata`; deal progression must remain traceable after migration.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Inventory `investments` files without exposing private data in GitHub comments.\\n- Classify files by destination: `assethold`, `achantasdata`, keep-temporary, or delete/archive candidate.\\n- Preserve deal/progression understanding with a private manifest or summary artifact.\\n- Migrate analysis/code files to `assethold` with tests or runnable examples where applicable.\\n- Stage private/source records for `achantasdata` with confidentiality-safe metadata.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] File inventory exists with classification and rationale.\\n- [ ] Analysis/code files are migrated or have explicit blockers.\\n- [ ] Private/source/reference files are migrated or have explicit blockers.\\n- [ ] Deal progression remains understandable via manifest/links/summaries.\\n- [ ] `investments` no longer contains unclassified durable analysis code.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Origin: mission review of `investments/.agent-os/product/mission.md`\\n- Portfolio mission umbrella: #2533\\n\\n\\n## Additional retirement requirement\\n\\n- Retire `investments` within 3 months after completing file classification and migration.\\n- Do not leave `investments` as an active long-term repository; at most keep a minimal pointer/manifest if needed for traceability.\\n\\n\\n## Migration completeness requirement\\n\\n- All data must be migrated, archived, or intentionally dispositioned before retirement.\\n- No useful information should be lost; preserve deal context, provenance, and progression history through destination files, manifests, summaries, or links.\\n- Create a migration manifest showing what moved where and what, if anything, was intentionally archived or left as a pointer.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2537\", \"display_title\": \"chore(investments): sanity-check and migrate files to assethold or achantasdata\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2512\", \"title\": \"feat(career): build semiconductor CAD/FEM portfolio and job-application packet\", \"issue_number\": 2512, \"body\": \"## Context\\nParent: #2507\\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\\n\\nPackage the lane outputs into job-application material for semiconductor-adjacent roles.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Portfolio index linking research, EDA demo, CAD/layout demo, FEM benchmark, and reports.\\n2. Resume bullets grounded in completed artifacts.\\n3. Role-specific application snippets for packaging simulation, CAD/layout automation, and ASIC/EDA technical program roles.\\n4. Interview prep notes explaining PDK, DRC/LVS, RTL-to-GDS, GDS/OASIS, thermal-mechanical FEM, reliability terminology, and how ACE Engineer experience transfers.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Each resume/application claim links to a concrete repo artifact.\\n- The packet differentiates \\\"hands-on artifact built\\\" from \\\"concept researched\\\".\\n- Packet is easy to tailor for a specific job posting.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2512\", \"display_title\": \"feat(career): build semiconductor CAD/FEM portfolio and job-application packet\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2501\", \"title\": \"chore(planning): #2105 governance-lock \\u2014 handoff vs live-state discrepancy\", \"issue_number\": 2501, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nThe 2026-04-26 morning handoff stated [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) (governance-lock) needs a v5 plan revision before [#2483](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483) and [#2484](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2484) can unblock. However, live-state inspection shows:\\n\\n- [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) state: OPEN\\n- Labels: `enhancement,priority:medium,cat:documentation,cat:harness,status:plan-approved`\\n- Most-recent comment (2026-04-24T16:56:37Z): linked children #2483 (matrix population) + #2484 (scanner extension)\\n\\nThe `status:plan-approved` label is already present.\\n\\n## Question\\n\\nIs [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) actually ready to execute (handoff is stale), or is v5 needed to address something the v4 approval missed (handoff is right, label is premature)?\\n\\n## Action\\n\\nUser clarification needed:\\n- If ready: schedule exec routine for [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105), then unblock #2483/#2484.\\n- If v5 needed: open a v5 planning session.\\n\\n## Surfaced\\n\\n2026-04-26 from autonomous-wave session \\u2014 flagged in `/tmp/handoff-2026-04-26-session-close.md`.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2501\", \"display_title\": \"chore(planning): #2105 governance-lock \\u2014 handoff vs live-state discrepancy\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2497\", \"title\": \"chore(memory): handoff-doc cross-row SHA transcription hazard\", \"issue_number\": 2497, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nThe 2026-04-26 morning handoff (`/tmp/handoff-prompt.md`) recorded:\\n\\n```\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 v3 | cb1c4a972 |\\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 v3 | cb1c4a972 |\\n```\\n\\nBoth rows referenced the same SHA. Investigation showed:\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124's actual tip IS `cb1c4a972` \\u2705\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471's actual tip is `f4218a7f6` \\u274c (`cb1c4a972` does not exist in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471's branch history)\\n\\nThe morning handoff propagated the wrong SHA into the execute-#2471 routine's expected-SHA field. Had this not been caught, routine 1 would have triggered a false drift detection at 13:00 UTC and lost ~3 hours.\\n\\n## Failure mode\\n\\nWhen two plans get approved in the same session, hand-written SHA tables collide if the writer copy-pastes a row and forgets to update the SHA value. This is a recurring hazard in approval-binding workflows.\\n\\n## Mitigation options\\n\\n1. **Auto-generate the handoff SHA table from `gh issue list --label status:plan-approved --json number` + `git ls-remote origin plan/issue-N-*`** \\u2014 eliminates hand-transcription. Could be a script under `scripts/handoff/`.\\n2. **Add a self-consistency check at handoff write time**: each row's SHA must come from a fresh `git rev-parse origin/plan/issue-N-...` call, with the result echoed inline.\\n3. **Promote to Level-2 enforcement**: pre-handoff hook that verifies all SHAs in the handoff resolve to commits on their stated branches.\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\nOption 1 (script) is the simplest to land. Option 3 is the durable answer per `.claude/rules/patterns.md` enforcement gradient.\\n\\n## Related memory\\n\\n- `feedback_git_switch_discard_changes_pattern.md` (added 2026-04-26) \\u2014 covers the related cross-branch contamination pattern that caused the actual drift on vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25.\\n- `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md` \\u2014 the binding rule the transcription error violated.\\n\\nSurfaced 2026-04-26 from autonomous-wave session.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2497\", \"display_title\": \"chore(memory): handoff-doc cross-row SHA transcription hazard\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483\", \"title\": \"chore(knowledge): populate freshness-cadence matrix with per-asset cadences and thresholds\", \"issue_number\": 2483, \"body\": \"## Parent\\nSplit from #2105 (Lane I scope-split, user-approved 2026-04-24 Option A).\\n\\n## Dependency\\n**Blocked on #2105** (governance lock) landing first. This issue cannot begin until the cadence vocabulary, threshold constants, and source-of-truth precedence are locked in #2105.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nIN:\\n1. Create `docs/document-intelligence/freshness-cadence-matrix.md` (or, if #2105 locks `data/document-index/freshness-cadences.yaml` as the canonical artifact, skip the markdown and document the decision here).\\n2. Populate every intelligence-asset class with: cadence, threshold, evidence source, owner.\\n3. Align entries with `intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml`, the maturity ledger, and the weekly-review checklist.\\n4. Link matrix rows to `staleness-scanner.py` output where applicable.\\n\\nOUT:\\n- Changing vocabulary, precedence, or ownership rules \\u2014 those are locked by #2105.\\n- Extending the scanner to new asset classes \\u2014 tracked as a separate child.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- (a) Every asset in `intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml` has a matching matrix row.\\n- (b) Every `freshness_cadence` value in the registry appears in the matrix's allowed-values set.\\n- (c) Matrix cadence vocabulary matches #2105's lock exactly.\\n- (d) Maturity-ledger assets are present in the matrix.\\n- (e) TDD test: registry-cadence values are a subset of matrix-allowed cadences (behavioral, not existence-only).\\n\\n## Complexity\\n**T2** \\u2014 bounded data-entry + cross-link task once vocabulary is fixed upstream.\\n\\n## Context\\nThe parent #2105 returned MAJOR across 4 consecutive review rounds due to scope-creep. Splitting matrix population out as its own issue keeps this work cleanly scoped and allows #2105 to land its governance blocker first.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483\", \"display_title\": \"chore(knowledge): populate freshness-cadence matrix with per-asset cadences and thresholds\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2392\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): wiki coverage-gap detector \\u2014 inventory \\u00d7 wiki diff per discipline\", \"issue_number\": 2392, \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nThe LLM-wiki portfolio has no coverage-gap detector. We cannot currently answer the question *\\\"which authoritative sources on `/mnt/ace/**`, in `docs/reports/**`, or in `data/document-index/**.yaml` have no corresponding L3 wiki page in `knowledge/wikis/**`?\\\"* without a manual sweep.\\n\\nExisting related work:\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067 (eng wiki ingest) produces seeds, not gap lists.\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 (WRK completions \\u2192 seeds) normalizes completed work, not external inventory.\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 (design-code registry \\u2192 standards overviews) is scoped to one registry.\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 (scorecard + action queue) prioritizes known work, but does not detect *unknown* gaps.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\nA script that joins three inventories:\\n1. `/mnt/ace/**` indexed via `data/document-index/registry.yaml` (+ `mounted-source-registry.yaml`)\\n2. Durable analysis outputs in `docs/reports/*.md` (filtered to those with L3-eligible findings per vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209)\\n3. Structured registries: `code-registry.yaml`, `online-resource-registry.yaml`, `dde-standards-inventory.yaml`\\n\\n\\u2026against wiki coverage in `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/**/*.md` (joined by `doc_key` per vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389), and emits per-domain gap reports:\\n\\n```\\ndocs/reports/wiki-coverage-gaps/<domain>.yaml\\n```\\n\\nEach entry records candidate `doc_key`, source path, discipline, and a suggested wiki page skeleton.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Script lives at `scripts/knowledge/detect_wiki_gaps.py` with unit tests\\n- [ ] Emits gap YAML per wiki domain under `docs/reports/wiki-coverage-gaps/`\\n- [ ] Each gap entry includes `doc_key`, source path, availability tier (per operating-model \\u00a77), and discipline tag\\n- [ ] Dry-run mode prints summary counts without writing files\\n- [ ] Scheduled weekly via `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\\n- [ ] Runs in <5 min against current corpus\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Blocks: prioritization waves under vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 (gap list becomes input)\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (wiki `doc_key`), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 (`source_doc_key` threading) \\u2014 soft; script tolerates missing `doc_key` by marking gap as `identity-unresolved`\\n- Relates to: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 operating model \\u00a72 (most-durable-owner rule informs gap classification)\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- This issue is **analysis-only**; it surfaces gaps. Promotion decisions remain in existing Batch-Pack issues (#2364/#2369/#2373/#2380) and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374.\\n- Out of scope: automatic wiki-page generation (handled by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 for WRK-completions; a separate issue if needed).\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2392\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): wiki coverage-gap detector \\u2014 inventory \\u00d7 wiki diff per discipline\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2470\", \"title\": \"feat(acma-codes): produce readable source-grounded summaries for OCIMF/CSA wiki promotion\", \"issue_number\": 2470, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nCreate a source-grounded, readable-summary unblocker for the ACMA wiki-promotion targets currently blocking #2227.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe #2227 plan-review wave found that the candidate summary artifacts exist but are not content-ready:\\n- `docs/reports/acma-wiki-unblock-2245-handoff.yaml` has `ready_for_2227: false`\\n- the target summary JSON files exist, but their `summary` fields are empty\\n- #2227 currently encodes a known-blocked/no-op branch, which reviewers correctly rejected as MAJOR\\n\\nWithout readable source-grounded summaries or an explicitly authorized manual-curation substitute, wiki promotion would risk unsupported claims outranking provenance.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Identify the bounded OCIMF/CSA target documents needed by #2227.\\n- Determine the available authorized-readable source surface for each target.\\n- Produce or specify source-grounded summaries sufficient for non-conditional wiki-promotion planning.\\n- Record provenance links/doc_keys for each summary.\\n- Keep this issue as an unblocker; do not directly promote wiki pages unless a later approved plan says so.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] each #2227 target has a readable, source-grounded summary or an explicit documented reason it cannot be summarized from this machine/toolchain\\n- [ ] summaries include provenance/doc_key references\\n- [ ] empty-summary artifacts are no longer treated as promotion-ready\\n- [ ] #2227 can be rewritten without a known-blocked Branch B/no-op path\\n\\n## Related\\n- Blocks: #2227\\n- Related umbrella: #2216\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2470\", \"display_title\": \"feat(acma-codes): produce readable source-grounded summaries for OCIMF/CSA wiki promotion\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2381\", \"title\": \"chore(governance): add computable expiration metadata to session handoffs\", \"issue_number\": 2381, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd computable expiration metadata to session handoffs so retention, cleanup advisories, and handoff lifecycle signals can be derived from repo content instead of guessed from filenames or issue comments.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found this is the strongest remaining small governance gap after the newer transient-promotion issues:\\n- the durable/transient boundary policy explicitly calls for an `## Expiration` section with issue reference and expected lifetime\\n- current handoffs still do not consistently carry that metadata\\n- cleanup/archive automation and handoff governance depend on these signals being present\\n- #2374 builds a promotion-candidate queue from handoffs/review artifacts, but it does not standardize handoff lifecycle metadata\\n\\nThis is a prerequisite-quality governance issue: the repo needs the metadata before it can cleanly compute retention behavior for future handoffs.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Define the required expiration/retention fields for new session handoffs.\\n- Update session-exit / handoff template or workflow guidance across supported agent paths.\\n- Include issue-linked and no-issue fallback cases.\\n- Keep scope at metadata/template/workflow level only; do not absorb cleanup automation.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Standard `## Expiration` section/schema for session handoffs.\\n- Updated template/workflow guidance for handoff-producing flows.\\n- Examples for open-issue, closed-issue, and no-issue handoffs.\\n- Minimal documentation of how the metadata supports later retention automation.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] new handoffs have a standard place to record associated issue and expected lifetime\\n- [ ] no-issue handoffs have a documented fallback expiration rule\\n- [ ] guidance is consistent across the main agent/session handoff paths\\n- [ ] scope stays distinct from cleanup/archive automation itself\\n\\n## Related\\n- Durable/transient boundary policy: #2209\\n- Cleanup/archive automation: #2237\\n- Post-closure promotion workflow: #2236\\n- Transient-promotion queue: #2374\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2381\", \"display_title\": \"chore(governance): add computable expiration metadata to session handoffs\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2379\", \"title\": \"feat(knowledge): generate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry\", \"issue_number\": 2379, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nGenerate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry so humans and agents can navigate the intelligence ecosystem by question, task, and access path instead of reading raw YAML or scattered docs.\\n\\n## Why\\nParallel repo review found that the repo already has the right metadata, but not the right explorer surface:\\n- `data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml` already contains `human_entry_point`, `agent_entry_point`, `query_command`, `machine_scope`, and discoverability metadata.\\n- `docs/document-intelligence/README.md` is still a short static landing page rather than a generated registry-backed explorer.\\n- Several intelligence assets remain hard to discover from navigation surfaces even though the registry already knows how they should be reached.\\n\\nThis is a high-leverage discoverability improvement because it converts existing structured metadata into a durable navigation product.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Generate docs-facing explorer page(s) from `data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml`.\\n- Support browsing by asset type, question/task type, machine availability, and discoverability status.\\n- Surface practical paths like \\\"if you need to answer X, start here\\\" using registry metadata plus query examples.\\n- Link the explorer from `docs/document-intelligence/README.md` and, where appropriate, `docs/README.md`.\\n- Keep the explorer generated from the registry so it stays aligned with the canonical data surface.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Registry-backed task explorer and/or asset explorer page.\\n- Generation path from accessibility-registry to docs-facing explorer.\\n- Navigation links from current intelligence landing pages.\\n- Guidance for how future registry fields should flow into the explorer.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] users can browse intelligence assets by task/question, not just by raw path\\n- [ ] generated explorer exposes human/agent entry points and query commands\\n- [ ] discoverability/machine-scope metadata is visible without reading raw YAML\\n- [ ] explorer is generated from the registry rather than hand-maintained\\n\\n## Related\\n- Accessibility registry: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2136\\n- Canonical intelligence entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\\n- Weekly review query packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2121\\n- Strengthening scorecard: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2379\", \"display_title\": \"feat(knowledge): generate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2299\", \"title\": \"chore(plans): make retention metadata a required planning artifact\", \"issue_number\": 2299, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nCreate a follow-on governance issue to make retention metadata a required, consistently enforced part of the issue-planning workflow after #2235 lands.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe overnight planning review for #2235 adds a retention metadata section to the plan template, but explicitly leaves open whether that section should become a required part of `docs/plans/README.md`, reviewer expectations, and workflow enforcement.\\n\\n## Proposed scope\\n- update `docs/plans/README.md` required-sections guidance to include retention metadata\\n- define when retention metadata is mandatory vs not-applicable\\n- align template, README, and review expectations\\n- decide whether any lint/check should validate presence of the section\\n- keep #2235 scoped to template addition only\\n\\n## Deliverable\\nA planning-ready governance issue covering retention metadata normalization and enforcement across issue-planning artifacts.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Foundation: #2235\\n- Policy context: #2209\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2299\", \"display_title\": \"chore(plans): make retention metadata a required planning artifact\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2236\", \"title\": \"chore(workflow): add post-closure promotion step to issue-planning-mode\", \"issue_number\": 2236, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nExtend the issue planning/execution workflow with an explicit post-closure promotion step that asks whether the issue produced reusable knowledge worth promoting into durable artifacts.\\n\\n## Why\\n#2209 requires explicit promotion from transient execution artifacts into durable knowledge. Without a closeout step, valuable findings remain trapped in issues, review files, and handoffs.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- update the issue-planning-mode workflow/skill to include a post-closure promotion check\\n- define what kinds of findings qualify for promotion routing\\n- clarify expected targets (wiki page, registry update, follow-on issue) without implementing those targets here\\n- ensure this integrates cleanly with the retrieval contract work in #2208\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- updated workflow guidance with post-closure promotion step\\n- concrete prompt/checklist for promotion consideration\\n- clear distinction between execution closeout and durable knowledge promotion\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] issue workflow includes a post-closure promotion step\\n- [ ] the step points to durable targets rather than leaving findings in the issue\\n- [ ] relationship to #2208 and #2209 is explicit\\n- [ ] no conformance tooling or automation is implemented here\\n\\n## Parent / related\\n- Parent policy: #2209\\n- Related retrieval/workflow contract: #2208\\n- Related wiki schema follow-on: issue to add `promoted_from`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2236\", \"display_title\": \"chore(workflow): add post-closure promotion step to issue-planning-mode\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2235\", \"title\": \"chore(plans): add retention metadata section to issue plan template\", \"issue_number\": 2235, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd a `Retention` section to the issue plan template so plan artifacts carry explicit expiration/archival expectations aligned with the durable-vs-transient boundary policy.\\n\\n## Why\\n#2209 defines plans as transient execution artifacts with finite retention. The current template does not carry explicit retention metadata, which makes cleanup automation and policy compliance harder.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- update `docs/plans/_template-issue-plan.md`\\n- define the minimum retention metadata needed for plans\\n- document how plan retention relates to issue lifecycle and archival behavior\\n- update any nearby plan guidance/index documentation if needed\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- template section for retention metadata\\n- guidance for how authors should fill it in\\n- alignment with the retention schedule defined in #2209\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] plan template contains a retention section\\n- [ ] retention semantics are aligned with #2209\\n- [ ] nearby planning guidance references the new section where appropriate\\n- [ ] change remains template/governance scoped\\n\\n## Parent / related\\n- Parent policy: #2209\\n- Related planning workflow: docs/plans/README.md\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2235\", \"display_title\": \"chore(plans): add retention metadata section to issue plan template\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2294\", \"title\": \"chore(skills): salvage #2290 follow-on learnings for regression coverage and github-code-review scope\", \"issue_number\": 2294, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe preserved local duplicate branch from #2290 (`issue-2290-implementation`) contains two potentially useful follow-on learnings that did not land upstream and should be evaluated deliberately rather than cherry-picked wholesale:\\n\\n1. stronger regression coverage for skill-dedup fallout, especially dangling references across agent/config surfaces\\n2. a much richer alternate version of `development/github/code-review`, which may contain useful workflow guidance but currently appears too broad to merge blindly\\n\\nThis issue captures a focused salvage/review pass for those two deltas as a concrete step toward higher skill-system productivity.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nAfter comparing the preserved local duplicate implementation against landed upstream commit `3f6ac3f5d`, the branch appears to contain:\\n\\n- one clearly useful idea: broader regression checks for deleted-path references after skill dedup\\n- one possibly useful but risky idea: expanding `github-code-review` into a much larger operational guide\\n\\nThe branch also contains unrelated drift, so direct cherry-pick is not appropriate.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n### Delta 1: regression test expansion\\nCurrent upstream `tests/skills/test_issue_2290_dedup_regression.py` verifies:\\n- audit findings for targeted duplicate names / leaf collisions\\n- deleted directories removed\\n- canonical directories still exist\\n\\nPreserved local branch additionally verifies:\\n- auxiliary reference files survive in canonical locations\\n- no residual collisions for the resolved leaves\\n- no dangling deleted-path references across:\\n  - `.claude/agent-skills-map.yaml`\\n  - `.claude/skill-registry.yaml`\\n  - `AGENTS.md`\\n  - `.mcp.json`\\n  - `.claude/rules/`\\n  - `.codex/`\\n  - `.gemini/`\\n  - `.hermes/`\\n  - `config/`\\n  - `scripts/`\\n\\n### Delta 2: github-code-review alternate draft\\nCurrent canonical skill is concise and review-focused.\\nThe preserved local branch contains a much larger alternate `development/github/code-review/SKILL.md` that adds:\\n- explicit pre-push local review workflow\\n- more end-to-end PR review workflow details\\n- many `curl` fallback examples\\n- expanded summary/report structure\\n\\nHowever, that alternate draft likely duplicates neighboring skills (`github-issues`, `github-pr-workflow`, `github-auth`) and may be too large / noisy for the canonical role of this skill.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n1. Review the preserved branch delta for `tests/skills/test_issue_2290_dedup_regression.py`\\n2. Selectively port only the high-signal regression checks that improve durability without overfitting\\n3. Review the preserved branch delta for `.claude/skills/development/github/code-review/SKILL.md`\\n4. Decide one of:\\n   - keep current canonical skill as-is\\n   - selectively import the best missing guidance\\n   - split any useful content into a better-targeted neighboring skill instead of bloating `github-code-review`\\n5. Update any linked docs/tests if the selected changes require it\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] A deliberate decision is documented for the stronger #2290 regression-surface checks\\n- [ ] Any accepted regression improvements are landed as a minimal, targeted change\\n- [ ] A deliberate decision is documented for the alternate `github-code-review` draft\\n- [ ] If content is imported, it is selective and avoids duplicating `github-issues` / `github-pr-workflow` / `github-auth`\\n- [ ] No wholesale cherry-pick from `issue-2290-implementation`\\n- [ ] Final outcome improves skill discoverability or reliability without adding scope sprawl\\n\\n## Non-Goals\\n\\n- Reopening or redoing #2290\\n- Blindly merging all preserved-branch changes\\n- Full skill taxonomy redesign in this issue\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- #2290 \\u2014 deduplicate audited skill collisions\\n- #2083 \\u2014 reconcile duplicate session-corpus-audit canonical path\\n- #2019 \\u2014 consolidate email skill sprawl\\n\\n## Suggested Labels\\n\\n- enhancement\\n- priority:medium\\n- cat:ai-orchestration\\n- cat:documentation\\n- cat:maintenance\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2294\", \"display_title\": \"chore(skills): salvage #2290 follow-on learnings for regression coverage and github-code-review scope\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2286\", \"title\": \"feat(wiki): promote SIGTTO LNG and mooring publications as batch\", \"issue_number\": 2286, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nFollow-on issue split from #2244 triage artifact to handle a bounded slice of ACMA breadth discovered outside the approved #2227 scope.\\n\\n## Why this is split\\n8 relevant publications across LNG + mooring domains; batch to avoid issue proliferation\\n\\n## Parent / source chain\\n- Parent umbrella: #2216\\n- Discovery source: #2226\\n- Triage decision source: #2244\\n- Bounded wiki-promotion issue kept separate: #2227\\n\\n## Target domain\\nLNG + mooring\\n\\n## Candidate items\\nSIGTTO-DAM-QRH-01, SIGTTO-ROLLOVER-PREVENTION, SIGTTO-HMPE-MOORING, SIGTTO-LNG-HARD-ARMS, SIGTTO-RISK-MITIGATION-LNG, SIGTTO-FIRE-LNG-CONTAINMENT, SIGTTO-LNG-SHIPPING-50, SIGTTO-HCB-NOV06\\n\\n## Expected scope\\n- convert the #2244 triage recommendation into a bounded implementation or routing decision\\n- stay within the candidate items listed above\\n- do not expand #2227 scope retroactively\\n\\n## Blocking / prerequisites\\nnone identified in #2244\\n\\n## Source artifact\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.md`\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.yaml`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2286\", \"display_title\": \"feat(wiki): promote SIGTTO LNG and mooring publications as batch\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2285\", \"title\": \"feat(wiki): promote API RP 2SK 3rd ed. to mooring wiki domain\", \"issue_number\": 2285, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nFollow-on issue split from #2244 triage artifact to handle a bounded slice of ACMA breadth discovered outside the approved #2227 scope.\\n\\n## Why this is split\\nDifferent org and standard from #2227 targets; requires own promotion issue\\n\\n## Parent / source chain\\n- Parent umbrella: #2216\\n- Discovery source: #2226\\n- Triage decision source: #2244\\n- Bounded wiki-promotion issue kept separate: #2227\\n\\n## Target domain\\nmooring\\n\\n## Candidate items\\nAPI-RP-2SK-3E\\n\\n## Expected scope\\n- convert the #2244 triage recommendation into a bounded implementation or routing decision\\n- stay within the candidate items listed above\\n- do not expand #2227 scope retroactively\\n\\n## Blocking / prerequisites\\nnone identified in #2244\\n\\n## Source artifact\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.md`\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.yaml`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2285\", \"display_title\": \"feat(wiki): promote API RP 2SK 3rd ed. to mooring wiki domain\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2284\", \"title\": \"feat(wiki): promote OCIMF MEG3 and MEG4 to mooring wiki domain\", \"issue_number\": 2284, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nFollow-on issue split from #2244 triage artifact to handle a bounded slice of ACMA breadth discovered outside the approved #2227 scope.\\n\\n## Why this is split\\nMajor standards (297pp + 293pp) deserving dedicated wiki pages with edition lineage\\n\\n## Parent / source chain\\n- Parent umbrella: #2216\\n- Discovery source: #2226\\n- Triage decision source: #2244\\n- Bounded wiki-promotion issue kept separate: #2227\\n\\n## Target domain\\nmooring\\n\\n## Candidate items\\nOCIMF-MEG4-4E, OCIMF-MEG-3E\\n\\n## Expected scope\\n- convert the #2244 triage recommendation into a bounded implementation or routing decision\\n- stay within the candidate items listed above\\n- do not expand #2227 scope retroactively\\n\\n## Blocking / prerequisites\\nnone identified in #2244\\n\\n## Source artifact\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.md`\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.yaml`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2284\", \"display_title\": \"feat(wiki): promote OCIMF MEG3 and MEG4 to mooring wiki domain\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2283\", \"title\": \"feat(wiki): promote CSA Z276.2-19 to LNG wiki domain\", \"issue_number\": 2283, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nFollow-on issue split from #2244 triage artifact to handle a bounded slice of ACMA breadth discovered outside the approved #2227 scope.\\n\\n## Why this is split\\nSame Z276 family as #2227 targets but must not expand #2227 scope\\n\\n## Parent / source chain\\n- Parent umbrella: #2216\\n- Discovery source: #2226\\n- Triage decision source: #2244\\n- Bounded wiki-promotion issue kept separate: #2227\\n\\n## Target domain\\nLNG\\n\\n## Candidate items\\nCSA-Z276.2-19\\n\\n## Expected scope\\n- convert the #2244 triage recommendation into a bounded implementation or routing decision\\n- stay within the candidate items listed above\\n- do not expand #2227 scope retroactively\\n\\n## Blocking / prerequisites\\n#2227\\n\\n## Source artifact\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.md`\\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.yaml`\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2283\", \"display_title\": \"feat(wiki): promote CSA Z276.2-19 to LNG wiki domain\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation","issue_number":2269,"body":"## Summary\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\n\nPart of #1782.\nPrimary reference: #25.\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\n\n## Motivation\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\n\n## Scope\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\n\nExpected deliverables:\n- baseline docs\n- run/validation entrypoints\n- minimal smoke example\n- troubleshooting guidance\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\n\n## Notes\nImplementation should prefer:\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","display_title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657","title":"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift","issue_number":2657,"body":"## Summary\n\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\n\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\n\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\n\nReads:\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\n- `github.github-issues`\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\n\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\n\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\n\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\n\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657","display_title":"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312","title":"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority","issue_number":2312,"body":"## Summary\n\nClaude continues to read removed local work-queue lifecycle scripts even though GitHub issues and `.planning/` are now the authoritative work-tracking surfaces:\n\n- `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh` — 94 reads\n- `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh` — 62 reads\n- `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh` — 60 reads\n- 216 total remediation-mapped stale reads in the latest provider-session ecosystem audit\n\nThis indicates parts of the repo ecosystem still imply that local queue lifecycle scripts are canonical, which wastes session budget and weakens the GitHub-first workflow.\n\n## Goal\n\nRemove remaining live references that teach agents to use the deleted local lifecycle scripts, and replace them with current queue-authority surfaces.\n\n## Canonical redirect targets\n\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.py`\n- `scripts/refresh-agent-work-queue.sh`\n- `notes/agent-work-queue.md`\n- `.planning/`\n- GitHub issues\n- `docs/work-queue-workflow.md`\n- `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Find live docs, prompts, templates, and routing instructions that still reference:\n   - `scripts/work-queue/close-item.sh`\n   - `scripts/work-queue/archive-item.sh`\n   - `scripts/work-queue/claim-item.sh`\n2. Update those surfaces so they describe GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh scripts as the authoritative workflow.\n3. Expand stale-reference regression coverage where needed so deleted lifecycle-script references stay confined to explicit legacy/reference docs.\n4. Refresh the provider-session ecosystem audit after cleanup.\n\n## Existing related issues\n\n- #1717 — policy/docs contradiction between GitHub issues and legacy work-queue guidance\n- #2213 — expand strict stale-reference enforcement across more live docs\n- #2214 — split current architecture guidance from legacy wrapper redirects\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Live instructional surfaces no longer reference the deleted lifecycle scripts\n- [ ] Current queue authority is documented as GitHub issues + `.planning/` + refresh helpers\n- [ ] Regression tests cover the deleted lifecycle-script references in protected live docs/templates\n- [ ] Provider-session ecosystem audit is refreshed after cleanup and linked from the issue\n\n## Source\n\n- `analysis/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.json`\n- `docs/reports/provider-session-ecosystem-audit.md`\n- Audit timestamp: `2026-04-16T23:34:23Z`\n- Reference doc: `docs/ops/legacy-claude-reference-map.md`\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2312","display_title":"chore(harness): replace legacy local lifecycle-script guidance with GitHub/.planning authority"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage","issue_number":2643,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\n\n## Context\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\n\nLive prerequisite checks found:\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\n\n## Problem\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\n\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\n\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\n\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\n\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction","issue_number":2626,"body":"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\n\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\n\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\n\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\n\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\nScenario 3 suggests \"temporary lift of interaction limit\" — globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\n\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\n\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\n\n## Severity\n\nMedium — the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","display_title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2552","title":"docs(security): external contributor and unsolicited paid-help response runbook","issue_number":2552,"body":"## Summary\nCreate a concise policy/runbook for handling non-collaborator comments, unsolicited paid-help offers, and external contributor requests on public repos.\n\n## Why\nIssue #2546 was triggered by an outside commenter offering paid implementation help on #2401. The technical lockdown is now in place for public repos, but operators still need a repeatable response path for existing comments, future exceptions, legitimate contributors, and paid external execution requests.\n\n## Scope\n- Document when to ignore, hide, report, or reply to external comments.\n- Define how to route legitimate contributor requests without granting broad access.\n- Define paid-pilot intake requirements: scope, NDA/confidentiality, repo access level, payment approval, and PR review gate.\n- Add a short issue-comment template for declining or redirecting unsolicited offers.\n- Link the policy from the security/governance docs or ops runbook.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Runbook covers unsolicited paid-help comments, spam, legitimate contributor requests, and collaborator onboarding.\n- [ ] Runbook preserves public-repo security posture: no collaborator access without explicit owner approval.\n- [ ] Templates avoid engaging suspicious accounts while keeping legitimate contributors routed through a safe process.\n- [ ] Documentation references #2546 and #2401 as the triggering example.\n\n## Related\n- Trigger comment context: #2401\n- Repository interaction lockdown: #2546\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2552","display_title":"docs(security): external contributor and unsolicited paid-help response runbook"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2533","title":"feat(repo-portfolio): review and revise mission/objective statements across active repos","issue_number":2533,"body":"## Summary\n\nReview and revise the mission/objective statements across all active workspace repos so future GitHub issue work can quickly answer:\n\n1. what is this repo for?\n2. what work belongs here?\n3. what work should route elsewhere?\n4. is the repo active, support-only, client/archive, or deprecated/no-new-issues?\n\nThis is the portfolio-wide complement to the Tier-1 routing/indexing work already tracked under vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460-#2465.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Tier-1 contract now improves code placement and routing, but the portfolio still needs a canonical mission/objective layer across all active repos. Without that layer, agents can still mis-route issues between overlapping repos such as:\n\n- `workspace-hub` vs per-repo execution docs\n- `assetutilities` vs repo-specific utilities\n- `digitalmodel` vs client/project verticals\n- `investments` vs `assethold`\n- `client_projects` vs client-specific repos\n- active engineering repos vs archives/reference repos\n\n## Initial repo scope\n\nUse `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and live immediate-child git repos as the starting inventory.\n\n### Tier-1\n\n- `workspace-hub`\n- `digitalmodel`\n- `assetutilities`\n- `aceengineer-website`\n\n### Tier-2\n\n- `OGManufacturing`\n- `acma-projects`\n- `frontierdeepwater`\n- `seanation`\n- `worldenergydata`\n- `investments`\n- `rock-oil-field`\n\n### Tier-3 / support / archive candidates\n\n- `aceengineer-admin`\n- `aceengineer-strategy`\n- `achantas-data`\n- `achantas-media`\n- `assethold`\n- `client_projects`\n- `doris`\n- `hobbies`\n- `pdf-large-reader` if present/active\n- `sabithaandkrishnaestates`\n- `saipem`\n- `sd-work`\n- `teamresumes`\n- `CAD-DEVELOPMENTS` if confirmed active in this workspace\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. Canonical portfolio mission/objective artifact, preferably `docs/REPO_MISSION_PORTFOLIO.md` or an equivalent linked from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\n2. Per-repo classification:\n   - active product/library\n   - client vertical\n   - business/admin support\n   - archive/reference\n   - deprecated / no-new-issues\n3. Per-repo mission/objective statement grounded in the strongest available source:\n   - `.agent-os/product/mission.md`\n   - `README.md`\n   - `AGENTS.md`\n   - `docs/README.md`\n   - existing workspace-hub portfolio docs\n4. Per-repo routing rule:\n   - \"work belongs here when...\"\n   - \"work should route elsewhere when...\"\n5. Conflict/dedupe notes for overlapping repo missions.\n6. Update links from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and/or `docs/ROUTING_INDEX.md` so the mission artifact is discoverable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every active repo in `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` has a current mission/objective row.\n- [ ] Every immediate-child local git repo not listed in `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` is either added, explicitly excluded, or marked as inventory drift.\n- [ ] Each row has a source path proving where the mission came from.\n- [ ] Each row has an activity/status classification.\n- [ ] Each row has an issue-routing rule for work that belongs vs work that should route elsewhere.\n- [ ] Overlapping missions are explicitly called out and resolved or marked for follow-up.\n- [ ] Tier-1 mission/objective rows are consistent with vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 and its child routing issues (#2461-#2465).\n- [ ] The artifact is linked from a canonical workspace discovery surface.\n- [ ] The plan receives adversarial review before implementation.\n\n## Suggested execution waves\n\n1. Wave 1: Tier-1 mission alignment and consistency with vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460-#2465.\n2. Wave 2: Tier-2 repo mission/objective review.\n3. Wave 3: Tier-3/support/archive classification and no-new-issues guidance.\n4. Wave 4: final portfolio table integration, dedupe/conflict notes, and discoverability links.\n\n## Related\n\n- Parent/umbrella: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#1962\n- Tier-1 structure epic: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2397\n- LLM-wiki roadmap context: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13\n- Tier-1 routing contract: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460\n- Tier-1 child issues: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2461, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2462, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2463, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2464, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2465\n\n## Planning requirements\n\nFollow the normal issue gate:\n\nIssue → resource intelligence → canonical plan in `docs/plans/` → adversarial plan review → `status:plan-review` → user approval → `status:plan-approved` → implementation.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2533","display_title":"feat(repo-portfolio): review and revise mission/objective statements across active repos"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2553","title":"docs(repo-portfolio): reconcile repository overview docs after mission review","issue_number":2553,"body":"## Summary\nReconcile the remaining portfolio/context documentation after the mission-document review wave and Business Brain update.\n\nThe mission review updated multiple per-repo mission documents and `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`. The remaining portfolio docs should be reviewed next so they do not preserve stale repo counts, stale tiering, or legacy `.agent-os/product/*` authority language.\n\n## Scope\nReview and update, at minimum:\n- `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_REPOSITORY_OVERVIEW.md`\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-21-repo-mission-revision-sequence.md`\n- Any linked docs index entries that still imply stale repo mission authority or outdated repository classifications.\n\n## Source context\n- Parent/current review issue: #2533\n- Business Brain refresh issue: #2549\n- Machine/provider dispatch inventory issue: #2548\n- Current authoritative review state: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` after the 2026-04-28 mission/business-brain review wave.\n\n## Requirements\n- Do not duplicate #2533's canonical portfolio artifact work.\n- Treat this as a documentation reconciliation follow-up: align overview/report docs with the already-reviewed mission and Business Brain corrections.\n- Preserve private/client confidentiality; do not expose sensitive project details in public issue comments or docs.\n- Explicitly mark archive/extraction candidates consistently with the Business Brain: `investments`, `rock-oil-field`, `seanation`, and `saipem`.\n- Keep `ace-linux-1` / Hermes control-plane and `licensed-win-1` OrcaFlex/AQWA dispatch assumptions consistent with #2548 and `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `docs/WORKSPACE_HUB_REPOSITORY_OVERVIEW.md` no longer conflicts with the updated Business Brain repo classifications.\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-21-repo-mission-revision-sequence.md` either reflects the completed review wave or is clearly marked historical/superseded.\n- Any remaining stale mission-authority references are either corrected, linked to #2533, or explicitly marked as legacy/historical.\n- Changes are reviewed under the normal plan-gated documentation workflow before implementation if scope grows beyond direct doc reconciliation.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2553","display_title":"docs(repo-portfolio): reconcile repository overview docs after mission review"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2549","title":"chore(business-brain): periodically assess repo work and refresh ecosystem context","issue_number":2549,"body":"## Summary\n\nBusiness Brain is the ecosystem's single-file onboarding source, but substantial work is happening across repositories. We need a recurring/readable assessment workflow that reviews completed repo work and updates Business Brain so repo classifications, provider accounts, machine inventory, and archive/retirement candidates do not go stale.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Assess recent GitHub issues/PRs and repo mission changes across active repos.\n- Reconcile repo mission/objective updates into `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` and future `docs/REPO_MISSION_PORTFOLIO.md` if applicable.\n- Update archive/extraction candidates and retirement targets after repo-specific migration issues progress.\n- Refresh AI provider account assumptions, including current Codex-only $200 paid account state.\n- Refresh machine/software/auth inventory summary after machine readiness work lands.\n- Keep the document concise (<200 lines) and link out to detailed registries/reports.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Business Brain reflects current repo work and no longer relies on stale provider/machine assumptions.\n- A checklist or scriptable workflow exists for periodic Business Brain refresh from issues/PRs/repo missions.\n- Updates link to evidence where details exceed the Business Brain line budget.\n- Parent/related issues are linked so future agents know when to update the Brain.\n\n## Related\n\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2549","display_title":"chore(business-brain): periodically assess repo work and refresh ecosystem context"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2548","title":"feat(control-plane): inventory machine software/auth and dispatch OrcaFlex/AQWA runs to licensed-win-1","issue_number":2548,"body":"## Summary\n\nBusiness Brain now records that `ace-linux-1` is the Hermes control plane and that work should be dispatchable to other machines. We need a durable machine/software inventory and dispatch readiness surface, starting with OrcaFlex and AQWA runs on `licensed-win-1`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build/maintain inventory for all machines: installed programs, licensed software, AI-provider auth state, repo checkout roots, run/smoke-test commands, and dispatch readiness.\n- Keep `ace-linux-1` as the primary Hermes control plane for GitHub mutation, provider routing, dispatch ledgers, and reconciliation.\n- Verify all AI providers are authenticated on machines where practical; record gaps rather than assuming readiness.\n- Establish `licensed-win-1` as initial licensed engineering worker for OrcaFlex and AQWA runs.\n- Define dispatch/smoke-test commands for OrcaFlex and AQWA from `ace-linux-1` to `licensed-win-1`.\n- Record evidence in a durable report or registry linked from `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Machine inventory exists and covers all known machines from Business Brain.\n- `licensed-win-1` has verified OrcaFlex and AQWA availability or explicit blockers.\n- AI-provider auth state is recorded per machine.\n- At least one dry-run/smoke workflow is documented for dispatching OrcaFlex/AQWA runs from Hermes on `ace-linux-1`.\n- Business Brain points to or summarizes the inventory state.\n\n## Related\n\n- Business Brain: `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md`\n- Control-plane policy: `docs/standards/CONTROL_PLANE_CONTRACT.md`\n- Portfolio mission review: #2533\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2548","display_title":"feat(control-plane): inventory machine software/auth and dispatch OrcaFlex/AQWA runs to licensed-win-1"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2547","title":"chore(seanation): extract useful client information and archive repo","issue_number":2547,"body":"## Summary\n\n`seanation` belongs to another client and should be treated as a client-specific extraction/archive repository. The objective is to review the repo, extract any useful data or information, preserve context/provenance, migrate reusable artifacts to the appropriate durable destination if needed, and then archive the repo.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inventory and sanity-check `seanation` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\n- Classify artifacts as useful data, technical information, analysis context, documents, reusable code, duplicate, archive-only, or discard candidate.\n- Extract useful client project data/information and preserve provenance/assumptions needed for future interpretation.\n- Migrate reusable code/data/analysis to the appropriate durable repository after sensitivity review.\n- Create a no-loss extraction/archive manifest showing what moved where, what remains archived, and why.\n- Archive `seanation` after useful data/information has been extracted and verified.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every useful file has a disposition: extracted/migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\n- Durable reusable artifacts no longer live only in `seanation`.\n- Final repo state is archived after extraction verification, or blocked with explicit reason.\n\n## Related\n\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\n- Similar archive/migration patterns: #2539 (`rock-oil-field`), #2545 (`saipem`)\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2547","display_title":"chore(seanation): extract useful client information and archive repo"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2545","title":"chore(saipem): extract useful installation-project information and archive or retire repo","issue_number":2545,"body":"## Summary\n\n`saipem` should be treated as a temporary engineering-installation contractor project repository, similar to Rock Oil Field, ACMA, and Doris client/project repositories. The objective is to extract useful Saipem installation-project information, migrate durable code/data/analysis to the appropriate Tier-1 repositories, and archive or retire the repo over time.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inventory and sanity-check `saipem` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\n- Classify artifacts as code, data, analysis, technical documentation, reference/context, duplicate, or discard candidate.\n- Preserve useful offshore installation engineering knowledge, including project context, assumptions, provenance, and progression history.\n- Migrate reusable engineering methods/calculations/workflows to `digitalmodel` where appropriate.\n- Migrate reusable utility code/tooling to `assetutilities` where appropriate.\n- Migrate reusable data workflows or normalized data products to the correct Tier-1 data repo where applicable.\n- Create a no-loss migration manifest showing what moved where and what was intentionally archived or retained as a pointer.\n- Archive or retire `saipem` over time once useful information has been migrated and verified.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every useful file has a disposition: migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\n- Durable code, data, and analysis no longer live only in `saipem`.\n- Final repo state is archived/retired if possible, or contains only a minimal pointer/manifest for traceability.\n\n## Related\n\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\n- Similar migration pattern: #2539 (`rock-oil-field`)\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2545","display_title":"chore(saipem): extract useful installation-project information and archive or retire repo"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2539","title":"chore(rock-oil-field): sanity-check and migrate useful code/data/analysis to Tier-1 repos","issue_number":2539,"body":"## Summary\n\n`rock-oil-field` should be treated as a temporary triage/archive repository, not a durable execution home. Sanity-check all code, data, engineering methods, and analysis, then migrate useful artifacts to the appropriate Tier-1 repositories.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inventory and sanity-check `rock-oil-field` files without exposing private/client-sensitive content in GitHub comments.\n- Classify artifacts as code, data, analysis, reference/context, duplicate, or discard candidate.\n- Migrate reusable engineering methods/calculations/workflows to `digitalmodel` where appropriate.\n- Migrate reusable utility code/tooling to `assetutilities` where appropriate.\n- Migrate reusable energy data workflows or normalized data products to `worldenergydata` where appropriate.\n- Preserve useful context, provenance, assumptions, and deal/project progression with a migration manifest.\n- Retire or reduce `rock-oil-field` to a minimal pointer/manifest after verified no-loss migration.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every file has a disposition: migrated, archived, retained as pointer, duplicate, or intentionally discarded with rationale.\n- No useful information is lost; context/provenance is preserved in destination repos or manifest.\n- Durable code, data, and analysis no longer live only in `rock-oil-field`.\n- Final repo state is either retired/archived or contains only a minimal migration manifest and routing pointer.\n\n## Related\n\n- Parent portfolio mission review: #2533\n- Large repo/data relocation context may overlap with #1341, but this issue is specifically about Rock Oil Field mission-driven migration to Tier-1 repos.\n\n\n## Archive/retire preference\n\n- Preferred end state is to archive or retire `rock-oil-field` if possible after verified no-loss migration.\n- Keep only a minimal pointer/manifest if a traceability stub is required.\n- Do not leave this repo as an active long-term home for code, data, or analysis.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2539","display_title":"chore(rock-oil-field): sanity-check and migrate useful code/data/analysis to Tier-1 repos"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2537","title":"chore(investments): sanity-check and migrate files to assethold or achantasdata","issue_number":2537,"body":"## Summary\nReview the private `investments` repository, sanity check all files, and migrate durable artifacts to the correct long-term home:\n\n- analysis/code/model/reporting artifacts -> `assethold`\n- private/source/reference/deal records -> `achantasdata`\n- temporary undecided material may remain in `investments` only with an explicit triage marker\n\n## Why\nThe mission review clarified that `investments` should not become a permanent parallel analytics codebase. Reusable investment analytics belong in `assethold`; private source records belong in `achantasdata`; deal progression must remain traceable after migration.\n\n## Scope\n- Inventory `investments` files without exposing private data in GitHub comments.\n- Classify files by destination: `assethold`, `achantasdata`, keep-temporary, or delete/archive candidate.\n- Preserve deal/progression understanding with a private manifest or summary artifact.\n- Migrate analysis/code files to `assethold` with tests or runnable examples where applicable.\n- Stage private/source records for `achantasdata` with confidentiality-safe metadata.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] File inventory exists with classification and rationale.\n- [ ] Analysis/code files are migrated or have explicit blockers.\n- [ ] Private/source/reference files are migrated or have explicit blockers.\n- [ ] Deal progression remains understandable via manifest/links/summaries.\n- [ ] `investments` no longer contains unclassified durable analysis code.\n\n## Related\n- Origin: mission review of `investments/.agent-os/product/mission.md`\n- Portfolio mission umbrella: #2533\n\n\n## Additional retirement requirement\n\n- Retire `investments` within 3 months after completing file classification and migration.\n- Do not leave `investments` as an active long-term repository; at most keep a minimal pointer/manifest if needed for traceability.\n\n\n## Migration completeness requirement\n\n- All data must be migrated, archived, or intentionally dispositioned before retirement.\n- No useful information should be lost; preserve deal context, provenance, and progression history through destination files, manifests, summaries, or links.\n- Create a migration manifest showing what moved where and what, if anything, was intentionally archived or left as a pointer.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2537","display_title":"chore(investments): sanity-check and migrate files to assethold or achantasdata"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2512","title":"feat(career): build semiconductor CAD/FEM portfolio and job-application packet","issue_number":2512,"body":"## Context\nParent: #2507\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\n\nPackage the lane outputs into job-application material for semiconductor-adjacent roles.\n\n## Deliverables\n1. Portfolio index linking research, EDA demo, CAD/layout demo, FEM benchmark, and reports.\n2. Resume bullets grounded in completed artifacts.\n3. Role-specific application snippets for packaging simulation, CAD/layout automation, and ASIC/EDA technical program roles.\n4. Interview prep notes explaining PDK, DRC/LVS, RTL-to-GDS, GDS/OASIS, thermal-mechanical FEM, reliability terminology, and how ACE Engineer experience transfers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Each resume/application claim links to a concrete repo artifact.\n- The packet differentiates \"hands-on artifact built\" from \"concept researched\".\n- Packet is easy to tailor for a specific job posting.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2512","display_title":"feat(career): build semiconductor CAD/FEM portfolio and job-application packet"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2501","title":"chore(planning): #2105 governance-lock — handoff vs live-state discrepancy","issue_number":2501,"body":"## Context\n\nThe 2026-04-26 morning handoff stated [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) (governance-lock) needs a v5 plan revision before [#2483](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483) and [#2484](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2484) can unblock. However, live-state inspection shows:\n\n- [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) state: OPEN\n- Labels: `enhancement,priority:medium,cat:documentation,cat:harness,status:plan-approved`\n- Most-recent comment (2026-04-24T16:56:37Z): linked children #2483 (matrix population) + #2484 (scanner extension)\n\nThe `status:plan-approved` label is already present.\n\n## Question\n\nIs [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105) actually ready to execute (handoff is stale), or is v5 needed to address something the v4 approval missed (handoff is right, label is premature)?\n\n## Action\n\nUser clarification needed:\n- If ready: schedule exec routine for [#2105](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2105), then unblock #2483/#2484.\n- If v5 needed: open a v5 planning session.\n\n## Surfaced\n\n2026-04-26 from autonomous-wave session — flagged in `/tmp/handoff-2026-04-26-session-close.md`.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2501","display_title":"chore(planning): #2105 governance-lock — handoff vs live-state discrepancy"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2497","title":"chore(memory): handoff-doc cross-row SHA transcription hazard","issue_number":2497,"body":"## Context\n\nThe 2026-04-26 morning handoff (`/tmp/handoff-prompt.md`) recorded:\n\n```\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 v3 | cb1c4a972 |\n| vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 v3 | cb1c4a972 |\n```\n\nBoth rows referenced the same SHA. Investigation showed:\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124's actual tip IS `cb1c4a972` ✅\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471's actual tip is `f4218a7f6` ❌ (`cb1c4a972` does not exist in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471's branch history)\n\nThe morning handoff propagated the wrong SHA into the execute-#2471 routine's expected-SHA field. Had this not been caught, routine 1 would have triggered a false drift detection at 13:00 UTC and lost ~3 hours.\n\n## Failure mode\n\nWhen two plans get approved in the same session, hand-written SHA tables collide if the writer copy-pastes a row and forgets to update the SHA value. This is a recurring hazard in approval-binding workflows.\n\n## Mitigation options\n\n1. **Auto-generate the handoff SHA table from `gh issue list --label status:plan-approved --json number` + `git ls-remote origin plan/issue-N-*`** — eliminates hand-transcription. Could be a script under `scripts/handoff/`.\n2. **Add a self-consistency check at handoff write time**: each row's SHA must come from a fresh `git rev-parse origin/plan/issue-N-...` call, with the result echoed inline.\n3. **Promote to Level-2 enforcement**: pre-handoff hook that verifies all SHAs in the handoff resolve to commits on their stated branches.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nOption 1 (script) is the simplest to land. Option 3 is the durable answer per `.claude/rules/patterns.md` enforcement gradient.\n\n## Related memory\n\n- `feedback_git_switch_discard_changes_pattern.md` (added 2026-04-26) — covers the related cross-branch contamination pattern that caused the actual drift on vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25.\n- `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md` — the binding rule the transcription error violated.\n\nSurfaced 2026-04-26 from autonomous-wave session.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2497","display_title":"chore(memory): handoff-doc cross-row SHA transcription hazard"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483","title":"chore(knowledge): populate freshness-cadence matrix with per-asset cadences and thresholds","issue_number":2483,"body":"## Parent\nSplit from #2105 (Lane I scope-split, user-approved 2026-04-24 Option A).\n\n## Dependency\n**Blocked on #2105** (governance lock) landing first. This issue cannot begin until the cadence vocabulary, threshold constants, and source-of-truth precedence are locked in #2105.\n\n## Scope\n\nIN:\n1. Create `docs/document-intelligence/freshness-cadence-matrix.md` (or, if #2105 locks `data/document-index/freshness-cadences.yaml` as the canonical artifact, skip the markdown and document the decision here).\n2. Populate every intelligence-asset class with: cadence, threshold, evidence source, owner.\n3. Align entries with `intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml`, the maturity ledger, and the weekly-review checklist.\n4. Link matrix rows to `staleness-scanner.py` output where applicable.\n\nOUT:\n- Changing vocabulary, precedence, or ownership rules — those are locked by #2105.\n- Extending the scanner to new asset classes — tracked as a separate child.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- (a) Every asset in `intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml` has a matching matrix row.\n- (b) Every `freshness_cadence` value in the registry appears in the matrix's allowed-values set.\n- (c) Matrix cadence vocabulary matches #2105's lock exactly.\n- (d) Maturity-ledger assets are present in the matrix.\n- (e) TDD test: registry-cadence values are a subset of matrix-allowed cadences (behavioral, not existence-only).\n\n## Complexity\n**T2** — bounded data-entry + cross-link task once vocabulary is fixed upstream.\n\n## Context\nThe parent #2105 returned MAJOR across 4 consecutive review rounds due to scope-creep. Splitting matrix population out as its own issue keeps this work cleanly scoped and allows #2105 to land its governance blocker first.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2483","display_title":"chore(knowledge): populate freshness-cadence matrix with per-asset cadences and thresholds"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2392","title":"feat(knowledge): wiki coverage-gap detector — inventory × wiki diff per discipline","issue_number":2392,"body":"## Problem\n\nThe LLM-wiki portfolio has no coverage-gap detector. We cannot currently answer the question *\"which authoritative sources on `/mnt/ace/**`, in `docs/reports/**`, or in `data/document-index/**.yaml` have no corresponding L3 wiki page in `knowledge/wikis/**`?\"* without a manual sweep.\n\nExisting related work:\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2034 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2067 (eng wiki ingest) produces seeds, not gap lists.\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 (WRK completions → seeds) normalizes completed work, not external inventory.\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#31 (design-code registry → standards overviews) is scoped to one registry.\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 (scorecard + action queue) prioritizes known work, but does not detect *unknown* gaps.\n\n## Deliverable\n\nA script that joins three inventories:\n1. `/mnt/ace/**` indexed via `data/document-index/registry.yaml` (+ `mounted-source-registry.yaml`)\n2. Durable analysis outputs in `docs/reports/*.md` (filtered to those with L3-eligible findings per vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2209)\n3. Structured registries: `code-registry.yaml`, `online-resource-registry.yaml`, `dde-standards-inventory.yaml`\n\n…against wiki coverage in `knowledge/wikis/*/wiki/**/*.md` (joined by `doc_key` per vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 / vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389), and emits per-domain gap reports:\n\n```\ndocs/reports/wiki-coverage-gaps/<domain>.yaml\n```\n\nEach entry records candidate `doc_key`, source path, discipline, and a suggested wiki page skeleton.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Script lives at `scripts/knowledge/detect_wiki_gaps.py` with unit tests\n- [ ] Emits gap YAML per wiki domain under `docs/reports/wiki-coverage-gaps/`\n- [ ] Each gap entry includes `doc_key`, source path, availability tier (per operating-model §7), and discipline tag\n- [ ] Dry-run mode prints summary counts without writing files\n- [ ] Scheduled weekly via `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\n- [ ] Runs in <5 min against current corpus\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Blocks: prioritization waves under vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37 (gap list becomes input)\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (wiki `doc_key`), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2389 (`source_doc_key` threading) — soft; script tolerates missing `doc_key` by marking gap as `identity-unresolved`\n- Relates to: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2205 operating model §2 (most-durable-owner rule informs gap classification)\n\n## Notes\n\n- This issue is **analysis-only**; it surfaces gaps. Promotion decisions remain in existing Batch-Pack issues (#2364/#2369/#2373/#2380) and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2374.\n- Out of scope: automatic wiki-page generation (handled by vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#38 for WRK-completions; a separate issue if needed).\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2392","display_title":"feat(knowledge): wiki coverage-gap detector — inventory × wiki diff per discipline"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2470","title":"feat(acma-codes): produce readable source-grounded summaries for OCIMF/CSA wiki promotion","issue_number":2470,"body":"## Summary\nCreate a source-grounded, readable-summary unblocker for the ACMA wiki-promotion targets currently blocking #2227.\n\n## Why\nThe #2227 plan-review wave found that the candidate summary artifacts exist but are not content-ready:\n- `docs/reports/acma-wiki-unblock-2245-handoff.yaml` has `ready_for_2227: false`\n- the target summary JSON files exist, but their `summary` fields are empty\n- #2227 currently encodes a known-blocked/no-op branch, which reviewers correctly rejected as MAJOR\n\nWithout readable source-grounded summaries or an explicitly authorized manual-curation substitute, wiki promotion would risk unsupported claims outranking provenance.\n\n## Scope\n- Identify the bounded OCIMF/CSA target documents needed by #2227.\n- Determine the available authorized-readable source surface for each target.\n- Produce or specify source-grounded summaries sufficient for non-conditional wiki-promotion planning.\n- Record provenance links/doc_keys for each summary.\n- Keep this issue as an unblocker; do not directly promote wiki pages unless a later approved plan says so.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] each #2227 target has a readable, source-grounded summary or an explicit documented reason it cannot be summarized from this machine/toolchain\n- [ ] summaries include provenance/doc_key references\n- [ ] empty-summary artifacts are no longer treated as promotion-ready\n- [ ] #2227 can be rewritten without a known-blocked Branch B/no-op path\n\n## Related\n- Blocks: #2227\n- Related umbrella: #2216\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2470","display_title":"feat(acma-codes): produce readable source-grounded summaries for OCIMF/CSA wiki promotion"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2381","title":"chore(governance): add computable expiration metadata to session handoffs","issue_number":2381,"body":"## Summary\nAdd computable expiration metadata to session handoffs so retention, cleanup advisories, and handoff lifecycle signals can be derived from repo content instead of guessed from filenames or issue comments.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found this is the strongest remaining small governance gap after the newer transient-promotion issues:\n- the durable/transient boundary policy explicitly calls for an `## Expiration` section with issue reference and expected lifetime\n- current handoffs still do not consistently carry that metadata\n- cleanup/archive automation and handoff governance depend on these signals being present\n- #2374 builds a promotion-candidate queue from handoffs/review artifacts, but it does not standardize handoff lifecycle metadata\n\nThis is a prerequisite-quality governance issue: the repo needs the metadata before it can cleanly compute retention behavior for future handoffs.\n\n## Scope\n- Define the required expiration/retention fields for new session handoffs.\n- Update session-exit / handoff template or workflow guidance across supported agent paths.\n- Include issue-linked and no-issue fallback cases.\n- Keep scope at metadata/template/workflow level only; do not absorb cleanup automation.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Standard `## Expiration` section/schema for session handoffs.\n- Updated template/workflow guidance for handoff-producing flows.\n- Examples for open-issue, closed-issue, and no-issue handoffs.\n- Minimal documentation of how the metadata supports later retention automation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] new handoffs have a standard place to record associated issue and expected lifetime\n- [ ] no-issue handoffs have a documented fallback expiration rule\n- [ ] guidance is consistent across the main agent/session handoff paths\n- [ ] scope stays distinct from cleanup/archive automation itself\n\n## Related\n- Durable/transient boundary policy: #2209\n- Cleanup/archive automation: #2237\n- Post-closure promotion workflow: #2236\n- Transient-promotion queue: #2374\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2381","display_title":"chore(governance): add computable expiration metadata to session handoffs"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2379","title":"feat(knowledge): generate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry","issue_number":2379,"body":"## Summary\nGenerate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry so humans and agents can navigate the intelligence ecosystem by question, task, and access path instead of reading raw YAML or scattered docs.\n\n## Why\nParallel repo review found that the repo already has the right metadata, but not the right explorer surface:\n- `data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml` already contains `human_entry_point`, `agent_entry_point`, `query_command`, `machine_scope`, and discoverability metadata.\n- `docs/document-intelligence/README.md` is still a short static landing page rather than a generated registry-backed explorer.\n- Several intelligence assets remain hard to discover from navigation surfaces even though the registry already knows how they should be reached.\n\nThis is a high-leverage discoverability improvement because it converts existing structured metadata into a durable navigation product.\n\n## Scope\n- Generate docs-facing explorer page(s) from `data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml`.\n- Support browsing by asset type, question/task type, machine availability, and discoverability status.\n- Surface practical paths like \"if you need to answer X, start here\" using registry metadata plus query examples.\n- Link the explorer from `docs/document-intelligence/README.md` and, where appropriate, `docs/README.md`.\n- Keep the explorer generated from the registry so it stays aligned with the canonical data surface.\n\n## Deliverables\n- Registry-backed task explorer and/or asset explorer page.\n- Generation path from accessibility-registry to docs-facing explorer.\n- Navigation links from current intelligence landing pages.\n- Guidance for how future registry fields should flow into the explorer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] users can browse intelligence assets by task/question, not just by raw path\n- [ ] generated explorer exposes human/agent entry points and query commands\n- [ ] discoverability/machine-scope metadata is visible without reading raw YAML\n- [ ] explorer is generated from the registry rather than hand-maintained\n\n## Related\n- Accessibility registry: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2136\n- Canonical intelligence entry points: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2137\n- Weekly review query packs: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2121\n- Strengthening scorecard: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#37\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2379","display_title":"feat(knowledge): generate task and asset explorer views from the intelligence accessibility registry"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2299","title":"chore(plans): make retention metadata a required planning artifact","issue_number":2299,"body":"## Summary\nCreate a follow-on governance issue to make retention metadata a required, consistently enforced part of the issue-planning workflow after #2235 lands.\n\n## Why\nThe overnight planning review for #2235 adds a retention metadata section to the plan template, but explicitly leaves open whether that section should become a required part of `docs/plans/README.md`, reviewer expectations, and workflow enforcement.\n\n## Proposed scope\n- update `docs/plans/README.md` required-sections guidance to include retention metadata\n- define when retention metadata is mandatory vs not-applicable\n- align template, README, and review expectations\n- decide whether any lint/check should validate presence of the section\n- keep #2235 scoped to template addition only\n\n## Deliverable\nA planning-ready governance issue covering retention metadata normalization and enforcement across issue-planning artifacts.\n\n## Related\n- Foundation: #2235\n- Policy context: #2209\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2299","display_title":"chore(plans): make retention metadata a required planning artifact"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2236","title":"chore(workflow): add post-closure promotion step to issue-planning-mode","issue_number":2236,"body":"## Summary\nExtend the issue planning/execution workflow with an explicit post-closure promotion step that asks whether the issue produced reusable knowledge worth promoting into durable artifacts.\n\n## Why\n#2209 requires explicit promotion from transient execution artifacts into durable knowledge. Without a closeout step, valuable findings remain trapped in issues, review files, and handoffs.\n\n## Scope\n- update the issue-planning-mode workflow/skill to include a post-closure promotion check\n- define what kinds of findings qualify for promotion routing\n- clarify expected targets (wiki page, registry update, follow-on issue) without implementing those targets here\n- ensure this integrates cleanly with the retrieval contract work in #2208\n\n## Deliverables\n- updated workflow guidance with post-closure promotion step\n- concrete prompt/checklist for promotion consideration\n- clear distinction between execution closeout and durable knowledge promotion\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] issue workflow includes a post-closure promotion step\n- [ ] the step points to durable targets rather than leaving findings in the issue\n- [ ] relationship to #2208 and #2209 is explicit\n- [ ] no conformance tooling or automation is implemented here\n\n## Parent / related\n- Parent policy: #2209\n- Related retrieval/workflow contract: #2208\n- Related wiki schema follow-on: issue to add `promoted_from`\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2236","display_title":"chore(workflow): add post-closure promotion step to issue-planning-mode"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2235","title":"chore(plans): add retention metadata section to issue plan template","issue_number":2235,"body":"## Summary\nAdd a `Retention` section to the issue plan template so plan artifacts carry explicit expiration/archival expectations aligned with the durable-vs-transient boundary policy.\n\n## Why\n#2209 defines plans as transient execution artifacts with finite retention. The current template does not carry explicit retention metadata, which makes cleanup automation and policy compliance harder.\n\n## Scope\n- update `docs/plans/_template-issue-plan.md`\n- define the minimum retention metadata needed for plans\n- document how plan retention relates to issue lifecycle and archival behavior\n- update any nearby plan guidance/index documentation if needed\n\n## Deliverables\n- template section for retention metadata\n- guidance for how authors should fill it in\n- alignment with the retention schedule defined in #2209\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] plan template contains a retention section\n- [ ] retention semantics are aligned with #2209\n- [ ] nearby planning guidance references the new section where appropriate\n- [ ] change remains template/governance scoped\n\n## Parent / related\n- Parent policy: #2209\n- Related planning workflow: docs/plans/README.md\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2235","display_title":"chore(plans): add retention metadata section to issue plan template"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2294","title":"chore(skills): salvage #2290 follow-on learnings for regression coverage and github-code-review scope","issue_number":2294,"body":"## Summary\n\nThe preserved local duplicate branch from #2290 (`issue-2290-implementation`) contains two potentially useful follow-on learnings that did not land upstream and should be evaluated deliberately rather than cherry-picked wholesale:\n\n1. stronger regression coverage for skill-dedup fallout, especially dangling references across agent/config surfaces\n2. a much richer alternate version of `development/github/code-review`, which may contain useful workflow guidance but currently appears too broad to merge blindly\n\nThis issue captures a focused salvage/review pass for those two deltas as a concrete step toward higher skill-system productivity.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter comparing the preserved local duplicate implementation against landed upstream commit `3f6ac3f5d`, the branch appears to contain:\n\n- one clearly useful idea: broader regression checks for deleted-path references after skill dedup\n- one possibly useful but risky idea: expanding `github-code-review` into a much larger operational guide\n\nThe branch also contains unrelated drift, so direct cherry-pick is not appropriate.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Delta 1: regression test expansion\nCurrent upstream `tests/skills/test_issue_2290_dedup_regression.py` verifies:\n- audit findings for targeted duplicate names / leaf collisions\n- deleted directories removed\n- canonical directories still exist\n\nPreserved local branch additionally verifies:\n- auxiliary reference files survive in canonical locations\n- no residual collisions for the resolved leaves\n- no dangling deleted-path references across:\n  - `.claude/agent-skills-map.yaml`\n  - `.claude/skill-registry.yaml`\n  - `AGENTS.md`\n  - `.mcp.json`\n  - `.claude/rules/`\n  - `.codex/`\n  - `.gemini/`\n  - `.hermes/`\n  - `config/`\n  - `scripts/`\n\n### Delta 2: github-code-review alternate draft\nCurrent canonical skill is concise and review-focused.\nThe preserved local branch contains a much larger alternate `development/github/code-review/SKILL.md` that adds:\n- explicit pre-push local review workflow\n- more end-to-end PR review workflow details\n- many `curl` fallback examples\n- expanded summary/report structure\n\nHowever, that alternate draft likely duplicates neighboring skills (`github-issues`, `github-pr-workflow`, `github-auth`) and may be too large / noisy for the canonical role of this skill.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Review the preserved branch delta for `tests/skills/test_issue_2290_dedup_regression.py`\n2. Selectively port only the high-signal regression checks that improve durability without overfitting\n3. Review the preserved branch delta for `.claude/skills/development/github/code-review/SKILL.md`\n4. Decide one of:\n   - keep current canonical skill as-is\n   - selectively import the best missing guidance\n   - split any useful content into a better-targeted neighboring skill instead of bloating `github-code-review`\n5. Update any linked docs/tests if the selected changes require it\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A deliberate decision is documented for the stronger #2290 regression-surface checks\n- [ ] Any accepted regression improvements are landed as a minimal, targeted change\n- [ ] A deliberate decision is documented for the alternate `github-code-review` draft\n- [ ] If content is imported, it is selective and avoids duplicating `github-issues` / `github-pr-workflow` / `github-auth`\n- [ ] No wholesale cherry-pick from `issue-2290-implementation`\n- [ ] Final outcome improves skill discoverability or reliability without adding scope sprawl\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Reopening or redoing #2290\n- Blindly merging all preserved-branch changes\n- Full skill taxonomy redesign in this issue\n\n## Related\n\n- #2290 — deduplicate audited skill collisions\n- #2083 — reconcile duplicate session-corpus-audit canonical path\n- #2019 — consolidate email skill sprawl\n\n## Suggested Labels\n\n- enhancement\n- priority:medium\n- cat:ai-orchestration\n- cat:documentation\n- cat:maintenance\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2294","display_title":"chore(skills): salvage #2290 follow-on learnings for regression coverage and github-code-review scope"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2286","title":"feat(wiki): promote SIGTTO LNG and mooring publications as batch","issue_number":2286,"body":"## Summary\nFollow-on issue split from #2244 triage artifact to handle a bounded slice of ACMA breadth discovered outside the approved #2227 scope.\n\n## Why this is split\n8 relevant publications across LNG + mooring domains; batch to avoid issue proliferation\n\n## Parent / source chain\n- Parent umbrella: #2216\n- Discovery source: #2226\n- Triage decision source: #2244\n- Bounded wiki-promotion issue kept separate: #2227\n\n## Target domain\nLNG + mooring\n\n## Candidate items\nSIGTTO-DAM-QRH-01, SIGTTO-ROLLOVER-PREVENTION, SIGTTO-HMPE-MOORING, SIGTTO-LNG-HARD-ARMS, SIGTTO-RISK-MITIGATION-LNG, SIGTTO-FIRE-LNG-CONTAINMENT, SIGTTO-LNG-SHIPPING-50, SIGTTO-HCB-NOV06\n\n## Expected scope\n- convert the #2244 triage recommendation into a bounded implementation or routing decision\n- stay within the candidate items listed above\n- do not expand #2227 scope retroactively\n\n## Blocking / prerequisites\nnone identified in #2244\n\n## Source artifact\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.md`\n- `docs/reports/2026-04-15-issue-2244-acma-breadth-triage.yaml`\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_